{"parentUuid":"a2424b6e-6dc3-417c-94c0-58a68bb50090","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"028832f6-ac65-4611-9b62-8068d7d219e0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UQMn2ipHeQZmtPrRjiDLHu","type":"tool_result","content":"  on `globalThis` out of the module's top level.\n- A copy starts the first time it shows, then stays alive while its block is in\n  the layout, shown or not (a hidden column, the other child of a stack, a pane\n  in another tab or behind a zoom): switching back finds it as it was. Its\n  timers keep running while hidden, so poll gently. Another layout starts its\n  mods fresh (pane mods belong to their tab and stay); a block removed or given\n  another mod or props starts over. `<mod>.<command>` reaches shown copies only.\n- Images and SVGs are referenced from `~/.config/herdr-app`:\n  `image(\"mods/<name>/logo.svg\")` (full color), `svg(\"mods/<name>/icon.svg\")`\n  (tinted with the text color). Saving an asset under `mods/` updates every\n  mod showing it, including images that were missing or invalid on first load.\n- The defaults are mods too, read them as examples: `spaces`, `agents`,\n  `tabs` (the tab bar), `menu`, `prompt`, `confirm`, `help`, `toast`,\n  Terminals' `picker`, `peek`, and `pane` (an\n  example pane header, not used by the default layouts), and `worktree`\n  (git worktrees as spaces: the space menu's and the + menu's New worktree,\n  Open worktree (the repo's checkouts, filtered; one already shown is gone\n  to) and Remove worktree open it as a dialog with props `{space, folder?,\n655-     */\n656-    content<Self extends Element>(this: Self, element: Element): Self;\n657-    /**\n658:     * Fills an `Avatar`'s `image` slot, which takes an `AvatarImage`.\n659-     *\n660-     * Consumed exactly as `content` is — a slot element is not also drawn as a\n661-     * child. Base renders this one when it is there and the `fallback` when it\n662-     * is not, so filling both is how a picture gets something to fall back to.\n663-     */\n664-    image<Self extends Element>(this: Self, element: Element): Self;\n665:    /** Fills an `Avatar`'s `fallback` slot, which takes an `AvatarFallback`. */\n666-    fallback<Self extends Element>(this: Self, element: Element): Self;\n667-    /** Fills an `AccordionItem`'s `header` slot, which takes an `AccordionHeader`. */\n668-    header<Self extends Element>(this: Self, element: Element): Self;\n669-    /** Fills a component's named `footer` slot. */\n670-    footer<Self extends Element>(this: Self, element: Element): Self;\n671-    /** Fills an `AccordionItem`'s `panel` slot, which takes an `AccordionPanel`. */\n672-    panel<Self extends Element>(this: Self, element: Element): Self;\n673-    /**\n674-     * Fills the `trigger` slot of a `Popover` or a `HoverCard`: the element\n675-     * that is on screen while the surface is closed, and that opens it.\n676-     *\n677-     * Consumed exactly as `content` is. A surface with no trigger draws\n--\n20783-   * background go on the root, and the fallback is styled where it is written.\n20784-   *\n20785-   * ```js\n20786:   * Avatar.new().w(40).h(40).rounded_full().overflow_hidden()\n20787:   *   .image(AvatarImage.new(\"avatars/ada.png\").size_full())\n20788:   *   .fallback(AvatarFallback.new().size_full().items_center().justify_center().child(\"AL\"));\n20789-   * ```\n20790-   *\n20791-   * Ordinary children are drawn beside whichever slot won, which is where a\n20792-   * status dot or a badge goes.\n20793-   */\n20794:  export const Avatar: PartType;\n20795-  /**\n20796-   * The image slot: a picture from the application's own directory, at the\n20797-   * same kind of path `image(...)` takes.\n20798-   *\n20799-   * It is a slot type, not an element — used as an ordinary child it draws\n20800-   * nothing and says so in the log. Give it `size_full()` unless you want it at\n20801-   * its natural size.\n20802-   */\n20803:  export const AvatarImage: { new(path: string): Element };\n20804-  /**\n20805-   * The fallback slot: an ordinary box holding whatever stands in for the\n20806-   * image — initials, a shape, an `svg(...)`.\n20807-   *\n20808:   * A slot type like `AvatarImage`, and worth filling: an `Avatar` with an\n20809-   * image path that does not resolve has nothing else to show.\n20810-   */\n20811:  export const AvatarFallback: PartType;\n20812-  /**\n20813-   * A pagination root: a navigation landmark carrying the announced label, and\n20814-   * nothing on screen.\n20815-   *\n20816-   * The page buttons are yours. What base contributes that you cannot write\n20817-   * for yourself is which page numbers to show — that is `pagination_items`\n20818-   * below, a calculation rather than a component.\ngpui-kit.d.ts:20318:  export function image(path: string): NativeElement;\nShell cwd was reset to /Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"dbfb26a9-83f5-42d7-bb01-93a68604c0b2","timestamp":"2026-11-18T04:53:17.566Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"  on `globalThis` out of the module's top level.\n- A copy starts the first time it shows, then stays alive while its block is in\n  the layout, shown or not (a hidden column, the other child of a stack, a pane\n  in another tab or behind a zoom): switching back finds it as it was. Its\n  timers keep running while hidden, so poll gently. Another layout starts its\n  mods fresh (pane mods belong to their tab and stay); a block removed or given\n  another mod or props starts over. `<mod>.<command>` reaches shown copies only.\n- Images and SVGs are referenced from `~/.config/herdr-app`:\n  `image(\"mods/<name>/logo.svg\")` (full color), `svg(\"mods/<name>/icon.svg\")`\n  (tinted with the text color). Saving an asset under `mods/` updates every\n  mod showing it, including images that were missing or invalid on first load.\n- The defaults are mods too, read them as examples: `spaces`, `agents`,\n  `tabs` (the tab bar), `menu`, `prompt`, `confirm`, `help`, `toast`,\