/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/.claude/rules/moai/workflow/context-window-management.md","type":"Project"},{"content":"","path":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/.claude/rules/moai/workflow/session-handoff.md","type":"Project"},{"content":"","path":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/.claude/rules/moai/workflow/skill-routing.md","type":"Project"},{"content":"","path":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/.claude/rules/moai/workflow/goal-directive.md","type":"Project"},{"content":"","path":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/.claude/rules/moai/workflow/cross-session-messaging.md","type":"Project"},{"content":"","path":"/Users/allan/.claude/projects/-Volumes-WorkSpace-vogle-herdr-gitdeck/memory/MEMORY.md","type":"AutoMem"}],"type":"instructions"},"cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","isSidechain":false,"parentUuid":"48b4212f-0847-457e-bc93-d0aaebe9414e","rendered":[{"content":""}],"renderedRole":"user","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","session_id":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch","timestamp":"2026-11-18T05:03:19.753Z","type":"attachment","userType":"external","uuid":"d0a6fffa-9c9b-43ea-bdfa-ce5674d12572","version":"2.1.325"}
{"attachment":{"context":{"gitStatus":"","userEmail":""},"type":"session_context"},"cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","isSidechain":false,"parentUuid":"d0a6fffa-9c9b-43ea-bdfa-ce5674d12572","rendered":[{"content":""}],"renderedRole":"user","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","session_id":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch","timestamp":"2026-11-18T05:03:19.753Z","type":"attachment","userType":"external","uuid":"64626799-f4e4-49f3-bae2-64885e3d2c22","version":"2.1.325"}
{"parentUuid":"64626799-f4e4-49f3-bae2-64885e3d2c22","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a839a4fb-7dd5-4c35-a523-15c45a35bd9a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Artifact, AskUserQuestion, Bash, Edit, Glob, Grep, ListAgents, Read, Skill, TaskCreate, TaskStop, TaskUpdate, ToolSearch, Write, mcp__firecrawl__firecrawl_search</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Request 1 (done, uncommitted): \"히스토리에서 그래프로나오는데 아이콘이랑 좀 색상이랑.. 지금 git패널에서 보여주는거 참조해서 업데이트해줄래\". Make GitDeck's History graph look like Herdr's Git panel (the `my-git-graph` mod).\n   - Request 2 (in progress): \"음.. 좋은에 fork 스타일로 해줄수 있을까? [Fork screenshot] 깃허브인지,깃렙인지 보여주고, 아니면 공용git 아이콘으로 해주는식으로. 커밋한유저 아이콘도 가져올수 있을까? 이렇게까지는 힘든가?\"\n     - Wants Fork-app style.\n     - Remote labels show a GitHub or GitLab logo, else a generic git icon.\n     - Committer avatar.\n   - User decision on avatars: \"사진 없이\". No external requests. Show the author's initial in a colored circle. All other Fork styling proceeds:\n     - forge logos\n     - tinted labels\n     - bold conventional-commit prefix\n     - Fork-style merge dot\n   - Fork screenshot details:\n     - Labels have a forge icon box first, then the branch name.\n     - Labels are filled with a tint of the lane color and outlined in the lane color.\n     - Tag labels use a tag icon in a purple/blue box.\n     - Merge commits have a ring dot with a chevron inside.\n     - The `feat:` / `chore(main):` prefix is bold.\n     - Each row has an author avatar and name, and a ↩ after subjects that have a body. The ↩ is not planned.\n   - The user rejected my multi-select question about hash column, header bar, label clicks and line style, then interrupted.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Herdr mod runtime rules:\n     - no Node APIs and no setTimeout\n     - never keep a `cx`\n     - exec has no stdin and a 30 s limit\n     - state is immutable\n   - Images and SVGs:\n     - Loaded only from paths under `~/.config/herdr-app`: `svg(\"mods/gitdeck/icons/x.svg\")` (tinted) and `image(path)`.\n     - `writeTextFile` writes text only.\n     - Avatars would have needed curl downloads. Moot now: no photos.\n   - Herdr commands to drive the UI:\n     - `herdr-app do layout.select --stack panel-body --child graph|gitdeck` switches the right panel. Panel ids: files, changes, graph (my-git-graph), gitdeck.\n     - `herdr-app do gitdeck.tab:history` switches the GitDeck tab.\n     - `herdr-app shot <file>` takes a screenshot.\n     - Crop the right panel with `sips -c 2100 1000 --cropOffset 0 2840 in.png --out out.png`.\n   - The Git panel mod lives at `~/.config/herdr-app/mods/my-git-graph`:\n     - `graph.js` label() at ~line 598 draws the labels.\n     - `git.js` labelsOf() and LABEL={CHAR:6.6,PAD:5,ICON:13,GAP:6,MAX:22,FONT:11}.\n     - Lane colors: ansi4,2,5,3,6,1,12,10,13,11,14,9.\n   - Tests use `node --test` with TypeScript. Coverage covers `src/core/**` only (80% gate).\n   - forge/remote.ts:\n     - `parseRemote(url)` → `{host, path}`.\n     - `forgeOf(remote, override)`. The override is `git config gitdeck.forge`, which applies to origin.\n     - Only github.com and gitlab.com are guessed. Self-hosted `bsp-git.uzen.io` is GitLab via override/probe.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - NEW `src/core/graph/refLabels.ts`: groups a commit's refs into labels.\n     - A local branch carries same-named remotes as \"rider\" parts.\n     - Lone remotes and tags get their own labels.\n     - The current branch comes first.\n     - Names are cut with `fit` (MAX 22, remote rider 12, ellipsis \"…\").\n     - Exports `LabelPart {kind:\"branch\"|\"remote\"|\"tag\"; name; text}`, `RefLabel {kind; current; parts}` and `refLabels(refs: readonly Ref[]): RefLabel[]`.\n     - Rider match: `r.name.slice(r.name.indexOf(\"/\")+1) === b.name`. The rider text is the remote name before \"/\". A `paired` Set stops a remote pairing twice.\n   - NEW `tests/refLabels.test.ts`: 5 tests, all pass.\n     - pairing → `[{kind:\"branch\",current:false,parts:[{kind:\"branch\",name:\"main\",text:\"main\"},{kind:\"remote\",name:\"origin/main\",text:\"origin\"}]}]`\n     - lone remote + tag order\n     - current first\n     - truncation: \"feat/a-very-long-bran…\", \"upstream-mi…\"\n     - two remotes pairing once\n   - `src/ui/style.ts`:\n     - Lanes extended from 6 to 12 colors: after ansi1, added ansi12 #79c0ff, ansi10 #56d364, ansi13 #d2a8ff, ansi11 #e3b341, ansi14 #56d4dd, ansi9 #ff7b72.\n     - ICONS gained `check`, `cloud` and `tag` (`mods/gitdeck/icons/*.svg`).\n     - Existing helpers: `icon(path,color,size)`, `monoFont()`, `Palette` (surface, foreground, muted, dim, accent, changed, lanes …).\n   - `src/ui/graph.ts`:\n     - Imports `refLabels, type RefLabel` and `ICONS, icon, monoFont, type Palette`.\n     - New `GLYPH = {branch: ICONS.branch, remote: ICONS.cloud, tag: ICONS.tag}`.\n     - New `label(l: RefLabel, p, color, mono)`:\n       - an h_flex 18 px high, rounded(5), border in the edge color (tag → p.changed, else the lane color)\n       - filled with the lane color when current\n       - tooltip of the full names\n       - each part: px(5), gap(3); first part gets an icon (the check icon when current) at size 10\n       - riders get `border_l_1` and a bg of `${p.surface}33` (current) or `${edge}1f`\n       - text uses the mono font, size 11; fg is p.surface when current, p.changed for tags, p.muted for riders, else p.foreground\n     - `labels(refs,p,color,mono)` uses refLabels with MAX_LABELS 3 and shows \"+N\" for the rest.\n     - `row(...)` now takes `mono`. Merge commits (`commit.parents.length > 1`) use the p.dim subject color.\n     - `graphList` computes `const mono = monoFont();`.\n   - NEW icons in `mod/icons/`: check.svg, cloud.svg, tag.svg. These are Lucide icons copied from my-git-graph/icons; LICENSE-lucide.txt already exists. The existing `mod/icons/branch.svg` is kept, a different 16 px design.\n   - Read for the next step:\n     - `src/core/history.ts`: `loadHistory(git, target, limit, knownRefs?)` returns History {commits, lanes, refs, byCommit, stashes, limited, error}.\n     - `src/core/git/refs.ts`: Ref {kind, full, name, hash, upstream, ahead, behind, current}; `refsByCommit`.\n     - `src/core/git/log.ts`: Commit has hash, parents, author, email, time, subject.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - `layout.show --id graph` returned ok but didn't switch panels. Fixed with `layout.select --stack panel-body --child graph`. The first try used `--id`, which errored \"valid arguments: stack, child\".\n   - Running `node --test` without strip-types printed nothing. `node --experimental-strip-types --test` worked; `pnpm verify` runs the full suite.\n   - After `pnpm -s dev` the panel reset to the Changes tab. Ran `herdr-app do gitdeck.tab:history` again before the screenshot.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Verified, Git-panel style:\n     - `pnpm verify` exit 0, 408 tests passing, coverage 99.67% lines.\n     - `herdr-app status` errors `[]`.\n     - The screenshot `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-WorkSpace-vogle-herdr-gitdeck/c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29/scratchpad/after-crop.png` matches the Git panel:\n       - ✓ filled current label `feat/agent-centered-p… | origin`\n       - cloud icons on lone remotes\n       - tag icon v0.2.0 in yellow\n       - dimmed merge titles\n   - Herdr's right panel was restored to GitDeck. The scratchpad holds earlier screenshots: now.png, gitpanel-crop.png.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"히스토리에서 그래프로나오는데 아이콘이랑 좀 색상이랑.. 지금 git패널에서 보여주는거 참조해서 업데이트해줄래\"\n   - Answer to the commit question: \"More changes first\".\n   - Rejected the follow-up multi-select question, then interrupted. Then: \"음.. 좋은에 fork 스타일로 해줄수 있을까? [Image #3: Fork history screenshot] 깃허브인지,깃렙인지 보여주고, 아니면 공용git 아이콘으로 해주는식으로. 커밋한유저 아이콘도 가져올수 있을까? 이렇게까지는 힘든가?\"\n   - Answer to the avatar privacy question: \"사진 없이\". No external avatar requests; show the initial in a colored circle; do the rest of the Fork style.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Remote forge icons:\n     - Per remote name, decide github, gitlab or generic git.\n     - Read remote URLs, e.g. `git config --get-regexp '^remote\\..*\\.url$'` or `git remote -v`, in the history load.\n     - Use parseRemote. A host containing github → github, gitlab → gitlab.\n     - Origin follows the known forge or the `gitdeck.forge` override, so self-hosted bsp-git.uzen.io is GitLab.\n     - Otherwise git.\n     - Add GitHub, GitLab and Git logo SVGs to `mod/icons/` (Simple Icons, CC0) and use them for remote parts instead of the cloud icon.\n   - Fork label look: fill with a tint of the lane color, outline in the lane color, forge icon in its own front box.\n   - Bold conventional-commit prefix: a pure core function splitting the subject, e.g. `^(\\w+(\\([^)]*\\))?!?:)\\s` → {prefix, rest}, with tests.\n   - Merge commit dot: a ring with a chevron, like Fork.\n   - Author initial avatar:\n     - a colored circle with the first letter, before the author name\n     - color from a stable hash of the name over the lane palette\n     - pure core function with tests\n   - Write tests first (RED), then implement.\n   - `pnpm verify`, then `pnpm -s dev`, then `herdr-app do gitdeck.tab:history`, then `herdr-app status` (errors []), then a screenshot crop.\n   - Then ask with AskUserQuestion whether to commit and push. Stage explicit paths only: graph.ts, style.ts, refLabels.ts, its test, the icons, and new files. Never `.claudeignore` or `.worktreeinclude`. No MoAI trailer.\n   - Push only on approval.\n   - Possibly later: update the PR #8 description.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   - Just started the Fork-style step after the user chose \"사진 없이\".\n   - Told the user: \"사진은 쓰지 않을게요. 외부 요청 없이 작성자 이름 첫 글자를 색 동그라미에 넣어 보여줄게요. 나머지 Fork 스타일은 그대로 진행해요.\" Then read `src/core/forge/remote.ts` and `src/core/history.ts` to plan remote-kind detection.\n   - Planned new core files with tests: `src/core/graph/remoteKind.ts` and an avatar/initials helper (e.g. `src/core/graph/avatar.ts`, initials and color index only).\n   - The Git-panel-style changes so far are uncommitted in the working tree.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   - Continue the Fork-style implementation the user asked for: \"깃허브인지,깃렙인지 보여주고, 아니면 공용git 아이콘으로 해주는식으로\", with initials instead of photos (\"사진 없이\").\n   - Next action: write failing tests for:\n     - remote-kind detection: remote URL plus origin override → \"github\" | \"gitlab\" | \"git\"\n     - conventional-prefix split\n     - author initials and color\n   - Then implement them: wire remote URLs into the history load, add forge SVG icons, update `src/ui/graph.ts` (tinted labels, forge icon box, bold prefix, merge ring dot, initial avatar), verify, take a screenshot, and ask about the commit through AskUserQuestion.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/allan/.claude/projects/-Volumes-WorkSpace-vogle-herdr-gitdeck/c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"44c43c42-aecf-49fa-ad94-926477427e73","timestamp":"2026-11-18T04:57:13.051Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":131,"turnIndex":133},"turnOrigin":"human","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["2bba8ea8-ac1e-49ed-9681-ab84b43f4080"],"session_id":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
{"parentUuid":"44c43c42-aecf-49fa-ad94-926477427e73","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"compact_file_reference","filename":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/main.ts","displayPath":"src/main.ts"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"cd3df9e5-1631-4b80-b0f8-cd48ee970d67","timestamp":"2026-11-18T05:03:16.545Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/main.ts was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
{"parentUuid":"cd3df9e5-1631-4b80-b0f8-cd48ee970d67","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"compact_file_reference","filename":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/review.ts","displayPath":"src/ui/review.ts"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9deb03f2-eba8-44a6-af62-965ae565d1fb","timestamp":"2026-11-18T05:03:16.545Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/review.ts was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
{"parentUuid":"9deb03f2-eba8-44a6-af62-965ae565d1fb","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/core/forge/index.ts","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/core/forge/index.ts","content":"// The repo's forge (GitHub or GitLab), read through its CLI. The CLI is pointed\n// at the project and run outside the repo, so it never reads the work tree or\n// the repo's config.\n\nimport type { Exec, Git, Target } from \"../git/runner.ts\";\nimport { parseBranchPr, parsePrs, prListArgs, prViewArgs } from \"./github.ts\";\nimport { failedJobsArgs, mrListArgs, mrViewArgs, parseBranchMr, parseFailedJobs, parseMrs, pipelineId } from \"./gitlab.ts\";\nimport { forgeOf, parseRemote } from \"./remote.ts\";\nimport { discussionsArgs, parseDiscussions, parseThreads, threadsArgs, type ReviewThread } from \"./reviewThreads.ts\";\nimport type { BranchPr, Forge, ForgeChoice, ForgeKind, PrList } from \"./types.ts\";\n\nexport type { BranchPr, Checks, Forge, ForgeChoice, ForgeKind, PrList, PullRequest } from \"./types.ts\";\nexport type { ReviewThread } from \"./reviewThreads.ts\";\n\n/** Where to ask the CLIs which hosts they are signed in to: outside the repo. */\ninterface Probe {\n  exec: Exec;\n  away: string;\n}\n\n/**\n * The forge whose CLI alone is signed in to `host` (the person logged in there\n * themselves, so pointing that CLI at it is safe); null when neither or both are.\n * The token each prints is only checked for being there, never kept.\n */\nasync function signedInForge(probe: Probe, target: Target, host: string): Promise<ForgeKind | null> {\n  const has = (cli: string, args: string[]): Promise<boolean> =>\n    probe.exec(cli, args, { cwd: probe.away, on: target.on }).then(\n      (r) => r.code === 0 && r.stdout.trim() !== \"\",\n      () => false,\n    );\n  const [gitlab, github] = await Promise.all([\n    has(\"glab\", [\"config\", \"get\", \"token\", \"--host\", host]),\n    has(\"gh\", [\"auth\", \"token\", \"--hostname\", host]),\n  ]);\n  return gitlab === github ? null : gitlab ? \"gitlab\" : \"github\";\n}\n\n/**\n * origin's host, and its forge; `git config gitdeck.forge github|gitlab|none` names\n * it for any host. With a probe, an unnamed host is read from the signed-in CLIs.\n * The host comes back only while it's unnamed: the person is asked which it is.\n */\nasync function readOrigin(git: Git, target: Target, probe?: Probe): Promise<{ forge: Forge | null; host: string | null }> {\n  const [url, override] = await Promise.all([\n    git(target, [\"remote\", \"get-url\", \"origin\"]).catch(() => \"\"),\n    git(target, [\"config\", \"--get\", \"gitdeck.forge\"]).then((v) => v.trim(), () => null),\n  ]);\n  const remote = parseRemote(url);\n  const forge = forgeOf(remote, override);\n  if (forge !== null || remote === null || override !== null || !probe) return { forge, host: forge === null && override === null ? (remote?.host ?? null) : null };\n  const kind = await signedInForge(probe, target, remote.host);\n  const found = kind === null ? null : forgeOf(remote, kind);\n  return { forge: found, host: found === null ? remote.host : null };\n}\n\nexport async function readForge(git: Git, target: Target): Promise<Forge | null> {\n  return (await readOrigin(git, target)).forge;\n}\n\n/** Names origin's forge for this repo (its own .git/config), for a host that isn't github.com or gitlab.com; \"none\" stops the asking. */\nexport async function setForge(git: Git, target: Target, kind: ForgeChoice): Promise<void> {\n  await git(target, [\"config\", \"--local\", \"gitdeck.forge\", kind]);\n}\n\nconst failure = (cli: string, error: unknown): string => `Can't run ${cli}: ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}`;\n\n/** `away` is a folder outside the repo (home) for the CLI to run in. */\nexport async function loadPrs(git: Git, exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string): Promise<PrList> {\n  const { forge, host } = await readOrigin(git, target, { exec, away });\n  if (forge === null) {\n    const error = host === null ? \"No GitHub or GitLab remote: origin isn't one\" : `origin is on ${host}: is it GitLab or GitHub?`;\n    return { items: [], error, repo: null, label: \"PR\", host };\n  }\n  const base = { repo: forge.repo, label: forge.label, host: null };\n  const args = forge.kind === \"github\" ? prListArgs(forge.repo) : mrListArgs(forge.repo);\n  try {\n    const r = await exec(forge.cli, args, { cwd: away, on: target.on });\n    if (r.code !== 0) return { ...base, items: [], error: r.stderr.split(\"\\n\")[0] || `${forge.cli} failed (${r.code})` };\n    return { ...base, items: forge.kind === \"github\" ? parsePrs(r.stdout) : parseMrs(r.stdout), error: null };\n  } catch (error) {\n    return { ...base, items: [], error: failure(forge.cli, error) };\n  }\n}\n\n/** A failed MR pipeline with its failed jobs in place of itself; as it was when they can't be read. */\nasync function withFailedJobs(exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string, repo: string, pr: BranchPr, pipeline: number | null): Promise<BranchPr> {\n  if (pr.checks.failed === 0 || pipeline === null) return pr;\n  try {\n    const r = await exec(\"glab\", failedJobsArgs(repo, pipeline), { cwd: away, on: target.on });\n    const jobs = r.code === 0 ? parseFailedJobs(r.stdout, repo) : [];\n    return jobs.length > 0 ? { ...pr, failed: jobs } : pr;\n  } catch {\n    return pr;\n  }\n}\n\n/** The CLIs' words for \"this branch has none\". */\nconst NONE = /no pull requests found|no (?:open )?merge requests? (?:available|found)/i;\n\nexport interface BranchPrState {\n  pr: BranchPr | null;\n  error: string | null;\n  label: \"PR\" | \"MR\";\n  /** origin's host when it isn't a known forge yet: the person names which it is. */\n  host: string | null;\n  /** The forge read, or null when origin isn't one (or isn't named yet). */\n  forge: ForgeKind | null;\n}\n\n/** The branch's PR or MR; none (and no error) without a forge or one to show. Without a branch, only the forge. */\nexport async function loadBranchPr(git: Git, exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string, branch: string | null): Promise<BranchPrState> {\n  const { forge, host: origin } = await readOrigin(git, target, { exec, away });\n  if (forge === null) return { pr: null, error: null, label: \"PR\", host: origin, forge: null };\n  const label = forge.label;\n  const host = null;\n  const known = { label, host, forge: forge.kind };\n  if (branch === null) return { pr: null, error: null, ...known };\n  const args = forge.kind === \"github\" ? prViewArgs(forge.repo, branch) : mrViewArgs(forge.repo, branch);\n  try {\n    const r = await exec(forge.cli, args, { cwd: away, on: target.on });\n    if (r.code === 0) {\n      const pr = forge.kind === \"github\" ? parseBranchPr(r.stdout, forge.repo) : parseBranchMr(r.stdout);\n      return { pr: pr && forge.kind === \"gitlab\" ? await withFailedJobs(exec, target, away, forge.repo, pr, pipelineId(r.stdout)) : pr, error: null, ...known };\n    }\n    if (NONE.test(r.stderr)) return { pr: null, error: null, ...known };\n    return { pr: null, error: r.stderr.split(\"\\n\")[0] || `${forge.cli} failed (${r.code})`, ...known };\n  } catch (error) {\n    return { pr: null, error: failure(forge.cli, error), ...known };\n  }\n}\n\n/** The open review threads on PR/MR `number`: read once, when the person asks for them. */\nexport async function loadReviewThreads(git: Git, exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string, number: number): Promise<{ threads: ReviewThread[]; error: string | null }> {\n  const { forge } = await readOrigin(git, target);\n  if (forge === null) return { threads: [], error: \"No GitHub or GitLab remote\" };\n  const args = forge.kind === \"github\" ? threadsArgs(forge.repo, number) : discussionsArgs(forge.repo, number);\n  try {\n    const r = await exec(forge.cli, args, { cwd: away, on: target.on });\n    if (r.code !== 0) return { threads: [], error: r.stderr.split(\"\\n\")[0] || `${forge.cli} failed (${r.code})` };\n    return { threads: forge.kind === \"github\" ? parseThreads(r.stdout) : parseDiscussions(r.stdout), error: null };\n  } catch (error) {\n    return { threads: [], error: failure(forge.cli, error) };\n  }\n}\n","numLines":146,"startLine":1,"totalLines":146}},"displayPath":"src/core/forge/index.ts","savedCopyFraming":{"enveloped":false}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a7abb58c-ff2b-4ab8-a79c-a445d8e05a44","timestamp":"2026-11-18T05:03:16.545Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/core/forge/index.ts\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t// The repo's forge (GitHub or GitLab), read through its CLI. The CLI is pointed\n2\t// at the project and run outside the repo, so it never reads the work tree or\n3\t// the repo's config.\n4\t\n5\timport type { Exec, Git, Target } from \"../git/runner.ts\";\n6\timport { parseBranchPr, parsePrs, prListArgs, prViewArgs } from \"./github.ts\";\n7\timport { failedJobsArgs, mrListArgs, mrViewArgs, parseBranchMr, parseFailedJobs, parseMrs, pipelineId } from \"./gitlab.ts\";\n8\timport { forgeOf, parseRemote } from \"./remote.ts\";\n9\timport { discussionsArgs, parseDiscussions, parseThreads, threadsArgs, type ReviewThread } from \"./reviewThreads.ts\";\n10\timport type { BranchPr, Forge, ForgeChoice, ForgeKind, PrList } from \"./types.ts\";\n11\t\n12\texport type { BranchPr, Checks, Forge, ForgeChoice, ForgeKind, PrList, PullRequest } from \"./types.ts\";\n13\texport type { ReviewThread } from \"./reviewThreads.ts\";\n14\t\n15\t/** Where to ask the CLIs which hosts they are signed in to: outside the repo. */\n16\tinterface Probe {\n17\t  exec: Exec;\n18\t  away: string;\n19\t}\n20\t\n21\t/**\n22\t * The forge whose CLI alone is signed in to `host` (the person logged in there\n23\t * themselves, so pointing that CLI 