{"parentUuid":"e9ed5549-c7d1-456f-9c19-393e102660cd","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"69f12d31-609e-45b2-abfe-cf2e60a6329c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Artifact, AskUserQuestion, Bash, Edit, Glob, Grep, ListAgents, Read, Skill, TaskCreate, TaskStop, TaskUpdate, ToolSearch, Write, mcp__firecrawl__firecrawl_search</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Earlier work, committed in 168b3fd and pushed to PR #8:\n     - The History graph drawn like Fork: forge logos, tinted labels, a bold conventional-commit prefix, a merge drawn as a ring with a chevron, and author initials on a colored circle.\n     - The user chose \"사진 없이\" (no photos, no external requests) for avatars.\n   - \"좋아 히스토리에서 하나 클릭해서 커밋 내용 들어가면 ... 옛날 디자인으로 뜨내 모두 체크해서 변경해줘\": update every old-design file list to the Changes-tab style. Done; the user chose \"Find the cause, then commit (Recommended)\" for the blank-list bug. Committed and pushed as e920dcf.\n   - \"한글로말해\": always reply in Korean.\n   - Latest question: \"깃허브나 깃랩 사용자 아이콘 보여주려면 이메일이 노출된다고 했나?\" The user is asking whether I said showing GitHub/GitLab user icons would expose emails.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Herdr mod (TypeScript bundled to `main.js`, no Node APIs, immutable state).\n   - Verification flow: `pnpm verify`, then `pnpm -s dev`, then `herdr-app status`, then screenshots.\n     - Screenshots: `herdr-app shot`, cropped with `sips -c H 1000 --cropOffset 0 2840`.\n     - Clicks: `orca computer click --app dev.herdr.app --x --y`.\n     - After a reload, `orca computer wait --text \"PR #8\"` before clicking, because a reload resets the tab to Changes.\n   - `v_virtual_list` rule: row elements must be built inside the render callback. Elements built outside it and attached later are not drawn.\n   - Commit rules:\n     - Stage explicit paths only.\n     - No MoAI trailer.\n     - Ask via AskUserQuestion before commit and push.\n     - Never commit `.claudeignore` or `.worktreeinclude`.\n   - Avatar privacy, as explained earlier:\n     - A GitHub noreply email sends only the account number to GitHub.\n     - Any other email sends its hash to Gravatar.\n     - A Gravatar hash can be guessed back by dictionary matching.\n     - Image requests also reveal the viewer's IP address.\n     - An alternative is the GitHub API by commit SHA, which returns `author.login` and `avatar_url`. It sends no email, and GitHub already holds pushed commits' emails, but it fails for unpushed commits.\n     - GitLab's avatar API needs the email itself sent to the GitLab server, and may fall back to Gravatar.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `src/ui/details.ts`:\n     - New `fileRow(id, letter, path, trailing: Element[], p, onOpen?)` using `kindIcon`, the name, a dim folder, `trailing`, and `statusLetter`.\n     - Exports `stagedTag` and `entryLetter`.\n     - `counts` is private and returns `lineCounts` (or \"binary\").\n   - `src/ui/summary.ts`: uses `detailRow`, `entryLetter` and `stagedTag` from `details.ts`.\n   - `src/ui/changeFiles.ts`: `letterColor` returns `p.removed` for \"D\" and \"!\".\n   - `src/ui/inspect.ts`:\n     - `interface Row { hash: string; cells: () => Element[] }`, with a comment saying the cells are built when the list lays the row out, because a virtual list draws only elements made inside its renderer.\n     - Every `cells: [` became `cells: () => [`.\n     - The renderer calls `.children(r.cells())`.\n     - Local narrowing fix: `const note = blob.note; if (note) return [{ hash: \"\", cells: () => [div().text_color(p.dim).child(note)] }];`\n     - Files-at-commit rows show `icon(FILE_ICONS[fileKind(f.path)], p.muted, 14)`, the name, a dim folder, and the size.\n   - `src/ui/graph.ts` and `src/core/forge/index.ts`: read only, for context.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Blank inspect lists, a bug that predated this work: cells were built outside the virtual-list renderer. Fixed with the thunk.\n   - The `h_full` guess did not help, so I removed it.\n   - TS2345 on `blob.note`: fixed with a local `note` variable.\n   - Clicks missed after reloads: waited with `orca wait` before clicking.\n   - The user was viewing a diff in the window: I stopped clicking until I had switched focus back to the terminal tab.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - All verified:\n     - `pnpm verify`: 415/415 tests pass, 99.67% line coverage.\n     - `herdr-app status`: errors [].\n     - Reflog and Files at commit render, confirmed by screenshot.\n   - Commit e920dcf was pushed and the branch is in sync.\n   - An empty `stash@{0}` was left untouched.\n   - Not checked visually: Blame, file history, PRs, statistics.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"히스토리에서 그래프로나오는데 아이콘이랑 좀 색상이랑.. 지금 git패널에서 보여주는거 참조해서 업데이트해줄래\"\n   - \"More changes first\" (an answer to a question).\n   - \"음.. 좋은에 fork 스타일로 해줄수 있을까? ... 깃허브인지,깃렙인지 보여주고, 아니면 공용git 아이콘으로 해주는식으로. 커밋한유저 아이콘도 가져올수 있을까?\"\n   - Avatar answer: \"사진 없이\" (no photos, no external requests).\n   - \"Commit and push (Recommended)\"\n   - \"좋아 히스토리에서 하나 클릭해서 커밋 내용 들어가면 [Image] 이렇게 파일 체인지가 나오는데 다른곳에서는 디자인이 다 바뀌었는대 여긴 아직도 옛날 디자인으로 뜨내 모두 체크해서 변경해줘\"\n   - \"Find the cause, then commit (Recommended)\" (an answer to a question).\n   - \"한글로말해\"\n   - \"깃허브나 깃랩 사용자 아이콘 보여주려면 이메일이 노출된다고 했나?\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Answer the latest question in Korean. No code change has been requested.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   - I grepped the transcript and found what I said earlier: \"이메일 정보가 외부로 나가요. GitHub noreply 이메일은 계정 번호만 GitHub에, 그 밖의 이메일은 해시 값을 Gravatar에 보내요. 사진을 어떻게 할까요?\"\n   - In English: email information goes outside; for a GitHub noreply email only the account number goes to GitHub, and for other emails a hash goes to Gravatar.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   - Answer in Korean.\n   - Yes, I said that, but precisely: the email itself isn't sent. A noreply email sends only the account number, and other emails send a hash to Gravatar, which can be matched back to the email by guessing. The image requests also reveal the viewer's IP address.\n   - Mention alternatives:\n     - GitHub API by commit SHA: no email is sent, but it only works for pushed commits.\n     - GitLab's avatar API sends the email to the GitLab server.\n   - Don't change code unless asked.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/allan/.claude/projects/-Volumes-WorkSpace-vogle-herdr-gitdeck/c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"c98b2097-5d27-4748-9e5d-9e80a96f2571","timestamp":"2026-11-18T06:24:37.606Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":133,"turnIndex":135},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
{"parentUuid":"c98b2097-5d27-4748-9e5d-9e80a96f2571","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"compact_file_reference","filename":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/changeFiles.ts","displayPath":"src/ui/changeFiles.ts"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1020e431-5fc1-4dfd-b3c8-4dedb931befc","timestamp":"2026-11-18T06:24:38.581Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/changeFiles.ts was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
{"parentUuid":"1020e431-5fc1-4dfd-b3c8-4dedb931befc","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/graph.ts","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/graph.ts","content":"// The commit graph: one row per commit with its lane lines, refs, subject,\n// author and age. A virtual list, so only the rows on screen are built.\n\nimport { div, PathBuilder, type Color, type Context, type Element } from \"gpui-kit\";\nimport { h_flex, v_flex, v_virtual_list, Scrollbar, type VirtualListScrollHandle } from \"gpui-base\";\nimport type { Commit } from \"../core/git/log.ts\";\nimport type { Ref } from \"../core/git/refs.ts\";\nimport type { LaneRow } from \"../core/graph/lanes.ts\";\nimport { UNCOMMITTED, type HistoryView } from \"../core/historyView.ts\";\nimport { ago } from \"../core/time.ts\";\nimport { refLabels, type RefLabel } from \"../core/graph/refLabels.ts\";\nimport { remoteKindOf, type RemoteKind } from \"../core/graph/remoteKind.ts\";\nimport { authorBadge, splitSubject } from \"../core/graph/rowText.ts\";\nimport { ICONS, icon, type Palette } from \"./style.ts\";\n\nexport const ROW = 24;\nconst LANE = 14;\nconst PAD = 6;\nconst MAX_LABELS = 3;\nexport const GRAPH_LIST = \"gitdeck-graph\";\nconst MORE = \"gitdeck:more\";\n\nconst laneX = (lane: number) => PAD + lane * LANE + LANE / 2;\nconst laneColor = (p: Palette, lane: number): Color => p.lanes[lane % p.lanes.length] ?? p.accent;\n\nfunction graphCell(row: LaneRow, uncommitted: boolean, merge: boolean, width: number, p: Palette): Element {\n  // One stroked path per color keeps a row to a few paints however many lanes pass.\n  const paths = new Map<string, { color: Color; path: PathBuilder }>();\n  for (const s of row.segments) {\n    const color = s.dashed ? p.dim : laneColor(p, s.to === s.from ? s.from : Math.max(s.from, s.to));\n    const key = `${color}${s.dashed ? \"-\" : \"\"}`;\n    const start = paths.get(key)?.path ?? (s.dashed ? PathBuilder.stroke(1.5).dash_array([3, 3]) : PathBuilder.stroke(1.5));\n    const [ax, ay, bx, by] = [laneX(s.from), s.fromY * ROW, laneX(s.to), s.toY * ROW];\n    const moved = start.move_to(ax, ay);\n    const mid = (ay + by) / 2;\n    paths.set(key, { color, path: ax === bx ? moved.line_to(bx, by) : moved.cubic_bezier_to(bx, by, ax, mid, bx, mid) });\n  }\n  const color = uncommitted ? p.dim : laneColor(p, row.lane);\n  const dot = div().absolute().left(laneX(row.lane) - 4).top(ROW / 2 - 4).w(8).h(8).rounded(4);\n  // A merge is a ring with a chevron in it, as Fork draws one.\n  const ring = div()\n    .absolute()\n    .left(laneX(row.lane) - 6)\n    .top(ROW / 2 - 6)\n    .w(12)\n    .h(12)\n    .rounded(6)\n    .border_2()\n    .border_color(color)\n    .bg(p.surface)\n    .flex()\n    .items_center()\n    .justify_center()\n    .child(icon(ICONS.chevron, color, 8));\n  return div()\n    .relative()\n    .flex_shrink_0()\n    .w(width)\n    .h(ROW)\n    .overflow_hidden()\n    .children([...paths.values()].map(({ color, path }) => window.paint_path(path.build(), color).absolute().top(0).left(0).size_full()))\n    .child(uncommitted ? dot.bg(p.surface).border_2().border_color(color) : merge ? ring : dot.bg(color));\n}\n\nconst FORGE_ICONS: Readonly<Record<RemoteKind, string>> = { github: ICONS.github, gitlab: ICONS.gitlab, git: ICONS.git };\n\n/** The icons in a label's first box: the forges its remotes are on, else what it is. */\nfunction glyphs(l: RefLabel, remotes: Readonly<Record<string, RemoteKind>>): string[] {\n  if (l.kind === \"tag\") return [ICONS.tag];\n  const forges = l.parts.filter((x) => x.kind === \"remote\").map((x) => FORGE_ICONS[remoteKindOf(x.name, remotes)]);\n  return forges.length > 0 ? [...new Set(forges)] : [ICONS.branch];\n}\n\n/**\n * A ref label as Fork draws one: the forge (or tag, or branch) icon in a box of\n * its own, then the name on a tint of the lane's color. A remote of the same\n * name shows only as its forge's icon; the tooltip names every ref.\n */\nfunction label(l: RefLabel, p: Palette, color: Color, remotes: Readonly<Record<string, RemoteKind>>): Element {\n  const edge = l.kind === \"tag\" ? tagColor(p) : color;\n  const name = l.parts[0]?.text ?? \"\";\n  const fg = l.current ? p.surface : p.foreground;\n  return h_flex()\n    .flex_shrink_0()\n    .h(18)\n    .gap(2)\n    .items_center()\n    .tooltip(l.parts.map((x) => x.name).join(\" · \"))\n    .child(\n      h_flex()\n        .h_full()\n        .px(3)\n        .gap(2)\n        .items_center()\n        .rounded(4)\n        .border_1()\n        .border_color(edge)\n        .children(glyphs(l, remotes).map((g) => icon(g, p.foreground, 11))),\n    )\n    .child(\n      h_flex()\n        .h_full()\n        .px(5)\n        .gap(3)\n        .items_center()\n        .rounded(4)\n        .border_1()\n        .border_color(edge)\n        .bg(l.current ? edge : (`${edge}33` as Color))\n        .when(l.current, (el) => el.child(icon(ICONS.check, fg, 10)))\n        .child(div().text_xs().text_color(fg).when(l.current, (el) => el.font_semibold()).child(name)),\n    );\n}\n\nconst tagColor = (p: Palette): Color => p.lanes[2] ?? p.accent;\n\nfunction labels(refs: readonly Ref[], p: Palette, color: Color, remotes: Readonly<Record<string, RemoteKind>>): Element[] {\n  const all = refLabels(refs);\n  const shown = all.slice(0, MAX_LABELS).map((l) => label(l, p, color, remotes));\n  const rest = all.length - MAX_LABELS;\n  return rest > 0 ? [...shown, div().flex_shrink_0().text_xs().text_color(p.dim).child(`+${rest}`)] : shown;\n}\n\n/** The subject, its conventional-commit type in bold. */\nfunction subject(text: string, color: Color): Element {\n  const { prefix, rest } = splitSubject(text);\n  return h_flex()\n    .flex_1()\n    .min_w_0()\n    .gap(3)\n    .overflow_hidden()\n    .text_color(color)\n    .when(prefix !== \"\", (el) => el.child(div().flex_shrink_0().font_weight(700).child(prefix)))\n    .child(div().min_w_0().truncate().child(rest.trimStart()));\n}\n\n/** The author as initials on a color of their own: no picture is fetched. */\nfunction author(name: string, p: Palette): Element {\n  const { initials, color } = authorBadge(name, p.lanes.length);\n  return h_flex()\n    .w(110)\n    .flex_shrink_0()\n    .gap(5)\n    .items_center()\n    .child(\n      div()\n        .w(16)\n        .h(16)\n        .flex_shrink_0()\n        .rounded(8)\n        .bg(p.lanes[color] ?? p.accent)\n        .flex()\n        .items_center()\n        .justify_center()\n        .text_size(initials.length > 1 ? 7.5 : 9)\n        .font_semibold()\n        .text_color(p.surface)\n        .child(initials),\n    )\n    .child(div().min_w_0().truncate().text_xs().text_color(p.muted).child(name));\n}\n\nfunction row(view: HistoryView, i: number, width: number, now: number, p: Palette): Element {\n  const commit = view.rows[i] as Commit;\n  const uncommitted = commit.hash === UNCOMMITTED;\n  const lane = view.lanes.rows[i];\n  const here = commit.hash === view.selected;\n  const color = lane ? laneColor(p, lane.lane) : p.accent;\n  const refs = view.history?.byCommit[commit.hash] ?? [];\n  const merge = commit.parents.length > 1;\n  return h_flex()\n    .h(ROW)\n    .pr(8)\n    .gap(6)\n    .items_center()\n    .cursor_pointer()\n    .when(here, (el) => el.bg(p.selected))\n    .hover((el) => el.bg(here ? p.selected : p.hover))\n    .child(lane && !view.searching ? graphCell(lane, uncommitted, merge, width, p) : div().w(PAD).flex_shrink_0())\n    .children(labels(refs, p, color, view.history?.remotes ?? {}))\n    // Merge commits are muted.\n    .child(subject(commit.subject, uncommitted ? p.muted : merge ? p.dim : p.foreground))\n    .when(!uncommitted, (el) => el.child(author(commit.author, p)))\n    .child(div().w(32).flex_shrink_0().text_right().text_xs().text_color(p.dim).child(ago(now, commit.time)));\n}\n\nfunction moreRow(p: Palette): Element {\n  return div().h(ROW).px(12).flex().items_center().text_xs().text_color(p.accent).cursor_pointer().child(\"Show older commits\");\n}\n\nexport interface GraphActions {\n  pick: (hash: string, cx: Context) => void;\n  more: (cx: Context) => void;\n}\n\nexport function graphList(view: HistoryView, p: Palette, scroll: VirtualListScrollHandle, actions: GraphActions): Element {\n  const limited = Boolean(view.history?.limited) && !view.searching;\n  const count = view.rows.length + (limited ? 1 : 0);\n  const width = PAD * 2 + Math.max(1, view.lanes.width) * LANE;\n  const now = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);\n  if (view.history === null) return v_flex().flex_1().items_center().justify_center().text_color(p.dim).child(\"Reading history…\");\n  if (view.history.error) return v_flex().flex_1().p(14).text_color(p.removed).child(view.history.error);\n  if (count === 0) {\n    const empty = view.searching ? \"No commit matches\" : \"No commits yet\";\n    return v_flex().flex_1().items_center().justify_center().text_color(p.dim).child(empty);\n  }\n  return div()\n    .relative()\n    .flex_1()\n    .min_h_0()\n    .child(\n      v_virtual_list(GRAPH_LIST, count, ROW, (i) => view.rows[i]?.hash ?? MORE, (range) =>\n        Array.from({ length: range.end - range.start }, (_x, k) => range.start + k).map((i) =>\n          i < view.rows.length ? row(view, i, width, now, p) : moreRow(p),\n        ),\n      )\n        // Rows of a virtual list can't hold handlers: the list reports the row's key.\n        .on_item_click((key, cx) => (key === MORE ? actions.more(cx) : actions.pick(key, cx)))\n        .track_scroll(scroll)\n        .size_full(),\n    )\n    .child(Scrollbar.vertical(GRAPH_LIST).absolute().inset_0());\n}\n","numLines":224,"startLine":1,"totalLines":224}},"displayPath":"src/ui/graph.ts","savedCopyFraming":{"enveloped":false}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7df7144a-2dc3-4957-952c-25688e506e6c","timestamp":"2026-11-18T06:24:38.581Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/graph.ts\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t// The commit graph: one row per commit with its lane lines, refs, subject,\n2\t// author and age. A virtual list, so only the rows on screen are built.\n3\t\n4\timport { div, PathBuilder, type Color, type Context, type Element } from \"gpui-kit\";\n5\timport { h_flex, v_flex, v_virtual_list, Scrollbar, type VirtualListScrollHandle } from \"gpui-base\";\n6\timport type { Commit } from \"../core/git/log.ts\";\n7\timport type { Ref } from \"../core/git/refs.ts\";\n8\timport type { LaneRow } from \"../core/graph/lanes.ts\";\n9\timport { UNCOMMITTED, type HistoryView } from \"../core/historyView.ts\";\n10\timport { ago } from \"../core/time.ts\";\n11\timport { refLabels, type RefLabel } from \"../core/graph/refLabels.ts\";\n12\timport { remoteKindOf, type RemoteKind } from \"../core/graph/remoteKind.ts\";\n13\timport { authorBadge, splitSubject } from \"../core/graph/rowText.ts\";\n14\timport { ICONS, icon, type Palette } from \"./style.ts\";\n15\t\n16\texport const ROW = 24;\n17\tconst LANE = 14;\n18\tconst PAD = 6;\n19\tconst MAX_LABELS = 3;\n20\texport const GRAPH_LIST = \"gitdeck-graph\";\n21\tconst MORE = \"gitdeck:more\";\n22\t\n23\tconst laneX = (lane: number) => PAD + lane * LANE + LANE / 2;\n24\tconst laneColor = (p: Palette, lane: number): Color => p.lanes[lane % p.lanes.length] ?? p.accent;\n25\t\n26\tfunction graphCell(row: LaneRow, uncommitted: boolean, merge: boolean, width: number, p: Palette): Element {\n27\t  // One stroked path per color keeps a row to a few paints however many lanes pass.\n28\t  const paths = new Map<string, { color: Color; path: PathBuilder }>();\n29\t  for (const s of row.segments) {\n30\t    const color = s.dashed ? p.dim : laneColor(p, s.to === s.from ? s.from : Math.max(s.from, s.to));\n31\t    const key = `${color}${s.dashed ? \"-\" : \"\"}`;\n32\t    const start = paths.get(key)?.path ?? (s.dashed ? PathBuilder.stroke(1.5).dash_array([3, 3]) : PathBuilder.stroke(1.5));\n33\t    const [ax, ay, bx, by] = [laneX(s.from), s.fromY * ROW, laneX(s.to), s.toY * ROW];\n34\t    const moved = start.move_to(ax, ay);\n35\t    const mid = (ay + by) / 2;\n36\t    paths.set(key, { color, path: ax === bx ? moved.line_to(bx, by) : moved.cubic_bezier_to(bx, by, ax, mid, bx, mid) });\n37\t  }\n38\t  const color = uncommitted ? p.dim : laneColor(p, row.lane);\n39\t  const dot = div().absolute().left(laneX(row.lane) - 4).top(ROW / 2 - 4).w(8).h(8).rounded(4);\n40\t  // A merge is a ring with a chevron in it, as Fork draws one.\n41\t  const ring = div()\n42\t    .absolute()\n43\t    .left(laneX(row.lane) - 6)\n44\t    .top(ROW / 2 - 6)\n45\t    .w(12)\n46\t    .h(12)\n47\t    .rounded(6)\n48\t    .border_2()\n49\t    .border_color(color)\n50\t    .bg(p.surface)\n51\t    .flex()\n52\t    .items_center()\n53\t    .justify_center()\n54\t    .child(icon(ICONS.chevron, color, 8));\n55\t  return div()\n56\t    .relative()\n57\t    .flex_shrink_0()\n58\t    .w(width)\n59\t    .h(ROW)\n60\t    .overflow_hidden()\n61\t    .children([...paths.values()].map(({ color, path }) => window.paint_path(path.build(), color).absolute().top(0).left(0).size_full()))\n62\t    .child(uncommitted ? dot.bg(p.surface).border_2().border_color(color) : merge ? ring : dot.bg(color));\n63\t}\n64\t\n65\tconst FORGE_ICONS: Readonly<Record<RemoteKind, string>> = { github: ICONS.github, gitlab: ICONS.gitlab, git: ICONS.git };\n66\t\n67\t/** The icons in a label's first box: the forges its remotes are on, else what it is. */\n68\tfunction glyphs(l: RefLabel, remotes: Readonly<Record<string, RemoteKind>>): string[] {\n69\t  if (l.kind === \"tag\") return [ICONS.tag];\n70\t  const forges = l.parts.filter((x) => x.kind === \"remote\").map((x) => FORGE_ICONS[remoteKindOf(x.name, remotes)]);\n71\t  return forges.length > 0 ? [...new Set(forges)] : [ICONS.branch];\n72\t}\n73\t\n74\t/**\n75\t * A ref label as Fork draws one: the forge (or tag, or branch) icon in a box of\n76\t * its own, then the name on a tint of the lane's color. A remote of the same\n77\t * name shows only as its forge's icon; the tooltip names every ref.\n78\t */\n79\tfunction label(l: RefLabel, p: Palette, color: Color, remotes: Readonly<Record<string, RemoteKind>>): Element {\n80\t  const edge = l.kind === \"tag\" ? tagColor(p) : color;\n81\t  const name = l.parts[0]?.text ?? \"\";\n82\t  const fg = l.current ? p.surface : p.foreground;\n83\t  return h_flex()\n84\t    .flex_shrink_0()\n85\t    .h(18)\n86\t    .gap(2)\n87\t    .items_center()\n88\t    .tooltip(l.parts.map((x) => x.name).join(\" · \"))\n89\t    .child(\n90\t      h_flex()\n91\t        .h_full()\n92\t        .px(3)\n93\t        .gap(2)\n94\t        .items_center()\n95\t        .rounded(4)\n96\t        .border_1()\n97\t        .border_color(edge)\n98\t        .children(glyphs(l, remotes).map((g) => icon(g, p.foreground, 11))),\n99\t    )\n100\t    .child(\n101\t      h_flex()\n102\t        .h_full()\n103\t        .px(5)\n104\t        .gap(3)\n105\t        .items_center()\n106\t        .rounded(4)\n107\t        .border_1()\n108\t        .border_color(edge)\n109\t        .bg(l.current ? edge : (`${edge}33` as Color))\n110\t        .when(l.current, (el) => el.child(icon(ICONS.check, fg, 10)))\n111\t        .child(div().text_xs().text_color(fg).when(l.current, (el) => el.font_semibold()).child(name)),\n112\t    );\n113\t}\n114\t\n115\tconst tagColor = (p: Palette): Color => p.lanes[2] ?? p.accent;\n116\t\n117\tfunction labels(refs: readonly Ref[], p: Palette, color: Color, remotes: Readonly<Record<string, RemoteKind>>): Element[] {\n118\t  const all = refLabels(refs);\n119\t  const shown = all.slice(0, MAX_LABELS).map((l) => label(l, p, color, remotes));\n120\t  const rest = all.length - MAX_LABELS;\n121\t  return rest > 0 ? [...shown, div().flex_shrink_0().text_xs().text_color(p.dim).child(`+${rest}`)] : shown;\n122\t}\n123\t\n124\t/** The subject, its conventional-commit type in bold. */\n125\tfunction subject(text: string, color: Color): Element {\n126\t  const { prefix, rest } = splitSubject(text);\n127\t  return h_flex()\n128\t    .flex_1()\n129\t    .min_w_0()\n130\t    .gap(3)\n131\t    .overflow_hidden()\n132\t    .text_color(color)\n133\t    .when(prefix !== \"\", (el) => el.child(div().flex_shrink_0().font_weight(700).child(prefix)))\n134\t    .child(div().min_w_0().truncate().child(rest.trimStart()));\n135\t}\n136\t\n137\t/** The author as initials on a color of their own: no picture is fetched. */\n138\tfunction author(name: string, p: Palette): Element {\n139\t  const { initials, color } = authorBadge(name, p.lanes.length);\n140\t  return h_flex()\n141\t    .w(110)\n142\t    .flex_shrink_0()\n143\t    .gap(5)\n144\t    .items_center()\n145\t    .child(\n146\t      div()\n147\t        .w(16)\n148\t        .h(16)\n149\t        .flex_shrink_0()\n150\t        .rounded(8)\n151\t        .bg(p.lanes[color] ?? p.accent)\n152\t        .flex()\n153\t        .items_center()\n154\t        .justify_center()\n155\t        .text_size(initials.length > 1 ? 7.5 : 9)\n156\t        .font_semibold()\n157\t        .text_color(p.surface)\n158\t        .child(initials),\n159\t    )\n160\t    .child(div().min_w_0().truncate().text_xs().text_color(p.muted).child(name));\n161\t}\n162\t\n163\tfunction row(view: HistoryView, i: number, width: number, now: number, p: Palette): Element {\n164\t  const commit = view.rows[i] as Commit;\n165\t  const uncommitted = commit.hash === UNCOMMITTED;\n166\t  const lane = view.lanes.rows[i];\n167\t  const here = commit.hash === view.selected;\n168\t  const color = lane ? laneColor(p, lane.lane) : p.accent;\n169\t  const refs = view.history?.byCommit[commit.hash] ?? [];\n170\t  const merge = commit.parents.length > 1;\n171\t  return h_flex()\n172\t    .h(ROW)\n173\t    .pr(8)\n174\t    .gap(6)\n175\t    .items_center()\n176\t    .cursor_pointer()\n177\t    .when(here, (el) => el.bg(p.selected))\n178\t    .hover((el) => el.bg(here ? p.selected : p.hover))\n179\t    .child(lane && !view.searching ? graphCell(lane, uncommitted, merge, width, p) : div().w(PAD).flex_shrink_0())\n180\t    .children(labels(refs, p, color, view.history?.remotes ?? {}))\n181\t    // Merge commits are muted.\n182\t    .child(subject(commit.subject, uncommitted ? p.muted : merge ? p.dim : p.foreground))\n183\t    .when(!uncommitted, (el) => el.child(author(commit.author, p)))\n184\t    .child(div().w(32).flex_shrink_0().text_right().text_xs().text_color(p.dim).child(ago(now, commit.time)));\n185\t}\n186\t\n187\tfunction moreRow(p: Palette): Element {\n188\t  return div().h(ROW).px(12).flex().items_center().text_xs().text_color(p.accent).cursor_pointer().child(\"Show older commits\");\n189\t}\n190\t\n191\texport interface GraphActions {\n192\t  pick: (hash: string, cx: Context) => void;\n193\t  more: (cx: Context) => void;\n194\t}\n195\t\n196\texport function graphList(view: HistoryView, p: Palette, scroll: VirtualListScrollHandle, actions: GraphActions): Element {\n197\t  const limited = Boolean(view.history?.limited) && !view.searching;\n198\t  const count = view.rows.length + (limited ? 1 : 0);\n199\t  const width = PAD * 2 + Math.max(1, view.lanes.width) * LANE;\n200\t  const now = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);\n201\t  if (view.history === null) return v_flex().flex_1().items_center().justify_center().text_color(p.dim).child(\"Reading history…\");\n202\t  if (view.history.error) return v_flex().flex_1().p(14).text_color(p.removed).child(view.history.error);\n203\t  if (count === 0) {\n204\t    const empty = view.searching ? \"No commit matches\" : \"No commits yet\";\n205\t    return v_flex().flex_1().items_center().justify_center().text_color(p.dim).child(empty);\n206\t  }\n207\t  return div()\n208\t    .relative()\n209\t    .flex_1()\n210\t    .min_h_0()\n211\t    .child(\n212\t      v_virtual_list(GRAPH_LIST, count, ROW, (i) => view.rows[i]?.hash ?? MORE, (range) =>\n213\t        Array.from({ length: range.end - range.start }, (_x, k) => range.start + k).map((i) =>\n214\t          i < view.rows.length ? row(view, i, width, now, p) : moreRow(p),\n215\t        ),\n216\t      )\n217\t        // Rows of a virtual list can't hold handlers: the list reports the row's key.\n218\t        .on_item_click((key, cx) => (key === MORE ? actions.more(cx) : actions.pick(key, cx)))\n219\t        .track_scroll(scroll)\n220\t        .size_full(),\n221\t    )\n222\t    .child(Scrollbar.vertical(GRAPH_LIST).absolute().inset_0());\n223\t}\n224\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
