":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
{"parentUuid":"ce88d155-2763-405a-b9b4-d74334506323","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b4b60722-6547-40a7-85a8-6bd2671f97a5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Artifact, AskUserQuestion, Bash, Edit, Glob, Grep, ListAgents, Read, Skill, TaskCreate, TaskStop, TaskUpdate, ToolSearch, Write, mcp__firecrawl__firecrawl_search</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Earlier work, committed and pushed to PR #8 on branch `feat/agent-centered-panel`:\n     - 168b3fd: the History graph drawn like Fork.\n     - e920dcf: file rows drawn like the Changes tab, and the inspect lists fixed.\n   - Earlier avatar choice: \"사진 없이\" (no photos, no external requests). Avatars are currently initials on a colored circle.\n   - \"한글로말해\": always reply in Korean.\n   - \"깃허브나 깃랩 사용자 아이콘 보여주려면 이메일이 노출된다고 했나?\" (Did I say showing GitHub/GitLab user icons exposes emails?) This was answered in Korean.\n   - Latest request: \"그럼 어떤 식으로 사진을 가져오는것이 좋을지 제안해줘\" (Then suggest how it would be best to fetch the photos). The user wants a proposal for the best way to fetch avatar photos. No code change has been requested yet.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Herdr mod rules:\n     - TypeScript bundled to `main.js`.\n     - No Node APIs.\n     - `exec` has no stdin and a 30-second limit.\n     - State is immutable.\n     - No work in `render`.\n   - Verification flow: `pnpm verify`, then `pnpm -s dev`, then `herdr-app status`, then a screenshot.\n   - Forge CLIs (`gh`/`glab`) run in a folder outside the repo, in the home directory. `readOrigin` in `src/core/forge/index.ts` gives the forge's kind and repo. `git config gitdeck.forge` already exists as a per-repo setting.\n   - Herdr UI image APIs:\n     - `image(path)` and `AvatarImage.new(path)` resolve against the application root only.\n     - There is no remote URL loading.\n     - An `Avatar` component exists with `.image(...)` and `.fallback(...)` slots.\n     - Implication: a downloaded image must be saved to a file under the app root, for example with curl via `exec`. This is unverified.\n   - Privacy facts:\n     - A GitHub noreply email (`123+name@users.noreply.github.com`) contains the account ID, so the avatar URL can be built locally without sending the email. The image fetch still reaches GitHub.\n     - Gravatar receives an email hash, which can be guessed back to the email.\n     - Any image fetch reveals the viewer's IP address and when they viewed the commit.\n     - GitHub API lookup:\n       - REST: `gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits/{sha}` returns `author.login` and `avatar_url`.\n       - GraphQL: `history(first:100)` returns up to 100 commits' `author{user{login avatarUrl}}` in one call.\n       - It sends nothing new, since GitHub already holds pushed commits, but it fails for unpushed commits.\n     - GitLab's avatar API (`/avatar?email=`) sends the email to the GitLab server, which already has pushed commits. On gitlab.com it may return a Gravatar URL, which should be skipped.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `src/ui/graph.ts`, read only. The current author badge, which a photo would replace or fall back to:\n     ```ts\n     function author(name: string, p: Palette): Element {\n       const { initials, color } = authorBadge(name, p.lanes.length);\n       return h_flex().w(110).flex_shrink_0().gap(5).items_center()\n         .child(div().w(16).h(16).flex_shrink_0().rounded(8).bg(p.lanes[color] ?? p.accent)\n           .flex().items_center().justify_center()\n           .text_size(initials.length > 1 ? 7.5 : 9).font_semibold().text_color(p.surface).child(initials))\n         .child(div().min_w_0().truncate().text_xs().text_color(p.muted).child(name));\n     }\n     ```\n     `row()` calls `author(commit.author, p)`. Only the author's name is passed, not their email.\n   - `src/core/forge/index.ts`, read only:\n     - `readOrigin(git, target, probe?)` returns `{forge, host}`.\n     - `loadPrs` and `loadBranchPr` run `exec(forge.cli, args, { cwd: away, on: target.on })`.\n     - This is the pattern to reuse for a `gh api` or `glab api` avatar lookup.\n   - `~/.config/herdr-app/gpui-kit.d.ts`, read only:\n     - `export function image(path: string): NativeElement;` is a full-color image \"from the application's own directory\".\n     - `export const AvatarImage: { new(path: string): Element };`\n     - Usage example: `.image(AvatarImage.new(\"avatars/ada.png\").size_full())`.\n     - `open_url` exists, but it only hands a URL to the system browser.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - None in this segment.\n   - Earlier fixes, already committed:\n     - Virtual-list rows were blank because cells were built outside the renderer. Fixed with a thunk, `cells: () => [...]`.\n     - TS2345 on `blob.note`. Fixed with a local `note` variable.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Finding: the UI can't load images from a URL, so any avatar feature needs to download each image to a file inside the app directory, keep it there, and fall back to initials.\n   - Whether a mod can write files there (curl through `exec` into the app root) has not been verified. The app root path is also unknown.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"히스토리에서 그래프로나오는데 아이콘이랑 좀 색상이랑.. 지금 git패널에서 보여주는거 참조해서 업데이트해줄래\"\n   - \"More changes first\" (an answer to a question).\n   - \"음.. 좋은에 fork 스타일로 해줄수 있을까? ... 깃허브인지,깃렙인지 보여주고, 아니면 공용git 아이콘으로 해주는식으로. 커밋한유저 아이콘도 가져올수 있을까?\"\n   - \"사진 없이\" (an answer to the avatar question).\n   - \"Commit and push (Recommended)\"\n   - \"좋아 히스토리에서 하나 클릭해서 커밋 내용 들어가면 [Image] 이렇게 파일 체인지가 나오는데 다른곳에서는 디자인이 다 바뀌었는대 여긴 아직도 옛날 디자인으로 뜨내 모두 체크해서 변경해줘\"\n   - \"Find the cause, then commit (Recommended)\" (an answer to a question).\n   - \"한글로말해\"\n   - \"깃허브나 깃랩 사용자 아이콘 보여주려면 이메일이 노출된다고 했나?\"\n   - \"그럼 어떤 식으로 사진을 가져오는것이 좋을지 제안해줘\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Deliver the avatar-fetching proposal in Korean, in the MoAI-Easy style, explaining terms plainly.\n   - Make no code changes unless the user approves.\n   - Commit rules:\n     - Ask via AskUserQuestion before any commit or push.\n     - Stage explicit paths only.\n     - Never commit `.claudeignore` or `.worktreeinclude`.\n     - No MoAI trailer.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   - I was researching feasibility for the proposal answering \"그럼 어떤 식으로 사진을 가져오는것이 좋을지 제안해줘\".\n   - The last tool results confirmed that `AvatarImage.new(path)` and `image(path)` take app-relative file paths only.\n   - The planned recommendation, in layers:\n     1. An on/off setting, default off, matching the earlier \"사진 없이\" choice. For example `git config gitdeck.avatars on`, like the existing `gitdeck.forge`.\n     2. GitHub:\n        - Use the signed-in `gh` CLI with one GraphQL call per page of history (up to 100 commits) to map each author's email to their login and `avatarUrl`. No email is sent.\n        - A noreply email gives the account ID locally.\n        - Cache by email, so one lookup covers all of that author's commits, including unpushed commits by a known author.\n     3. GitLab: the server is the repo's own host, so sending the email there reveals little new. Never use a Gravatar URL. This path is weaker; the fallback is initials.\n     4. Never call Gravatar directly.\n     5. Download each image once with `exec` (curl, small `size`) into a cache folder inside the app root. Render it with `Avatar` plus `AvatarImage`, falling back to initials.\n     6. Show initials until the image is ready, or when the lookup fails.\n   - Open caveats to state:\n     - Writing files into the app root is unverified.\n     - Image fetches reveal the viewer's IP address to GitHub.\n     - Unpushed commits by unknown authors still show initials.\n     - `author()` currently receives only the author's name, so the email must be threaded through `Commit`. Whether `Commit` has an email field is unverified.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   - Reply in Korean with the proposal above, as the deliverable for \"그럼 어떤 식으로 사진을 가져오는것이 좋을지 제안해줘\".\n   - Give one clear recommendation: GitHub GraphQL through `gh`, an email-to-avatar cache, a local file cache, initials as the fallback, an opt-in setting, and no Gravatar.\n   - Note the verification gaps listed above.\n   - End without a prose question. If a decision is truly needed, use AskUserQuestion after loading it with ToolSearch. Do not start implementation without approval.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/allan/.claude/projects/-Volumes-WorkSpace-vogle-herdr-gitdeck/c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"ccf1b013-8c67-4b46-86e7-15ae19e7e607","timestamp":"2026-11-18T15:42:15.204Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":134,"turnIndex":136},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
{"parentUuid":"ccf1b013-8c67-4b46-86e7-15ae19e7e607","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"compact_file_reference","filename":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/changeFiles.ts","displayPath":"src/ui/changeFiles.ts"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c5ea6bb1-9564-4045-9cd4-5837f8468a80","timestamp":"2026-11-18T15:42:16.077Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/changeFiles.ts was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
{"parentUuid":"c5ea6bb1-9564-4045-9cd4-5837f8468a80","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/graph.ts","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/graph.ts","content":"// The commit graph: one row per commit with its lane lines, refs, subject,\n// author and age. A virtual list, so only the rows on screen are built.\n\nimport { div, PathBuilder, type Color, type Context, type Element } from \"gpui-kit\";\nimport { h_flex, v_flex, v_virtual_list, Scrollbar, type VirtualListScrollHandle } from \"gpui-base\";\nimport type { Commit } from \"../core/git/log.ts\";\nimport type { Ref } from \"../core/git/refs.ts\";\nimport type { LaneRow } from \"../core/graph/lanes.ts\";\nimport { UNCOMMITTED, type HistoryView } from \"../core/historyView.ts\";\nimport { ago } from \"../core/time.ts\";\nimport { refLabels, type RefLabel } from \"../core/graph/refLabels.ts\";\nimport { remoteKindOf, type RemoteKind } from \"../core/graph/remoteKind.ts\";\nimport { authorBadge, splitSubject } from \"../core/graph/rowText.ts\";\nimport { ICONS, icon, type Palette } from \"./style.ts\";\n\nexport const ROW = 24;\nconst LANE = 14;\nconst PAD = 6;\nconst MAX_LABELS = 3;\nexport const GRAPH_LIST = \"gitdeck-graph\";\nconst MORE = \"gitdeck:more\";\n\nconst laneX = (lane: number) => PAD + lane * LANE + LANE / 2;\nconst laneColor = (p: Palette, lane: number): Color => p.lanes[lane % p.lanes.length] ?? p.accent;\n\nfunction graphCell(row: LaneRow, uncommitted: boolean, merge: boolean, width: number, p: Palette): Element {\n  // One stroked path per color keeps a row to a few paints however many lanes pass.\n  const paths = new Map<string, { color: Color; path: PathBuilder }>();\n  for (const s of row.segments) {\n    const color = s.dashed ? p.dim : laneColor(p, s.to === s.from ? s.from : Math.max(s.from, s.to));\n    const key = `${color}${s.dashed ? \"-\" : \"\"}`;\n    const start = paths.get(key)?.path ?? (s.dashed ? PathBuilder.stroke(1.5).dash_array([3, 3]) : PathBuilder.stroke(1.5));\n    const [ax, ay, bx, by] = [laneX(s.from), s.fromY * ROW, laneX(s.to), s.toY * ROW];\n    const moved = start.move_to(ax, ay);\n    const mid = (ay + by) / 2;\n    paths.set(key, { color, path: ax === bx ? moved.line_to(bx, by) : moved.cubic_bezier_to(bx, by, ax, mid, bx, mid) });\n  }\n  const color = uncommitted ? p.dim : laneColor(p, row.lane);\n  const dot = div().absolute().left(laneX(row.lane) - 4).top(ROW / 2 - 4).w(8).h(8).rounded(4);\n  // A merge is a ring with a chevron in it, as Fork draws one.\n  const ring = div()\n    .absolute()\n    .left(laneX(row.lane) - 6)\n    .top(ROW / 2 - 6)\n    .w(12)\n    .h(12)\n    .rounded(6)\n    .border_2()\n    .border_color(color)\n    .bg(p.surface)\n    .flex()\n    .items_center()\n    .justify_center()\n    .child(icon(ICONS.chevron, color, 8));\n  return div()\n    .relative()\n    .flex_shrink_0()\n    .w(width)\n    .h(ROW)\n    .overflow_hidden()\n    .children([...paths.values()].map(({ color, path }) => window.paint_path(path.build(), color).absolute().top(0).left(0).size_full()))\n    .child(uncommitted ? dot.bg(p.surface).border_2().border_color(color) : merge ? ring : dot.bg(color));\n}\n\nconst FORGE_ICONS: Readonly<Record<RemoteKind, string>> = { github: ICONS.github, gitlab: ICONS.gitlab, git: ICONS.git };\n\n/** The icons in a label's first box: the forges its remotes are on, else what it is. */\nfunction glyphs(l: RefLabel, remotes: Readonly<Record<string, RemoteKind>>): string[] {\n  if (l.kind === \"tag\") return [ICONS.tag];\n  const forges = l.parts.filter((x) => x.kind === \"remote\").map((x) => FORGE_ICONS[remoteKindOf(x.name, remotes)]);\n  return forges.length > 0 ? [...new Set(forges)] : [ICONS.branch];\n}\n\n/**\n * A ref label as Fork draws one: the forge (or tag, or branch) icon in a box of\n * its own, then the name on a tint of the lane's color. A remote of the same\n * name shows only as its forge's icon; the tooltip names every ref.\n */\nfunction label(l: RefLabel, p: Palette, color: Color, remotes: Readonly<Record<string, RemoteKind>>): Element {\n  const edge = l.kind === \"tag\" ? tagColor(p) : color;\n  const name = l.parts[0]?.text ?? \"\";\n  const fg = l.current ? p.surface : p.foreground;\n  return h_flex()\n    .flex_shrink_0()\n    .h(18)\n    .gap(2)\n    .items_center()\n    .tooltip(l.parts.map((x) => x.name).join(\" · \"))\n    .child(\n      h_flex()\n        .h_full()\n        .px(3)\n        .gap(2)\n        .items_center()\n        .rounded(4)\n        .border_1()\n        .border_color(edge)\n        .children(glyphs(l, remotes).map((g) => icon(g, p.foreground, 11))),\n    )\n    .child(\n      h_flex()\n        .h_full()\n        .px(5)\n        .gap(3)\n        .items_center()\n        .rounded(4)\n        .border_1()\n        .border_color(edge)\n        .bg(l.current ? edge : (`${edge}33` as Color))\n        .when(l.current, (el) => el.child(icon(ICONS.check, fg, 10)))\n        .child(div().text_xs().text_color(fg).when(l.current, (el) => el.font_semibold()).child(name)),\n    );\n}\n\nconst tagColor = (p: Palette): Color => p.lanes[2] ?? p.accent;\n\nfunction labels(refs: readonly Ref[], p: Palette, color: Color, remotes: Readonly<Record<string, RemoteKind>>): Element[] {\n  const all = refLabels(refs);\n  const shown = all.slice(0, MAX_LABELS).map((l) => label(l, p, color, remotes));\n  const rest = all.length - MAX_LABELS;\n  return rest > 0 ? [...shown, div().flex_shrink_0().text_xs().text_color(p.dim).child(`+${rest}`)] : shown;\n}\n\n/** The subject, its conventional-commit type in bold. */\nfunction subject(text: string, color: Color): Element {\n  const { prefix, rest } = splitSubject(text);\n  return h_flex()\n    .flex_1()\n    .min_w_0()\n    .gap(3)\n    .overflow_hidden()\n    .text_color(color)\n    .when(prefix !== \"\", (el) => el.child(div().flex_shrink_0().font_weight(700).child(prefix)))\n    .child(div().min_w_0().truncate().child(rest.trimStart()));\n}\n\n/** The author as initials on a color of their own: no picture is fetched. */\nfunction author(name: string, p: Palette): Element {\n  const { initials, color } = authorBadge(name, p.lanes.length);\n  return h_flex()\n    .w(110)\n    .flex_shrink_0()\n    .gap(5)\n    .items_center()\n    .child(\n      div()\n        .w(16)\n        .h(16)\n        .flex_shrink_0()\n        .rounded(8)\n        .bg(p.lanes[color] ?? p.accent)\n        .flex()\n        .items_center()\n        .justify_center()\n        .text_size(initials.length > 1 ? 7.5 : 9)\n        .font_semibold()\n        .text_color(p.surface)\n        .child(initials),\n    )\n    .child(div().min_w_0().truncate().text_xs().text_color(p.muted).child(name));\n}\n\nfunction row(view: HistoryView, i: number, width: number, now: number, p: Palette): Element {\n  const commit = view.rows[i] as Commit;\n  const uncommitted = commit.hash === UNCOMMITTED;\n  const lane = view.lanes.rows[i];\n  const here = commit.hash === view.selected;\n  const color = lane ? laneColor(p, lane.lane) : p.accent;\n  const refs = view.history?.byCommit[commit.hash] ?? [];\n  const merge = commit.parents.length > 1;\n  return h_flex()\n    .h(ROW)\n    .pr(8)\n    .gap(6)\n    .items_center()\n    .cursor_pointer()\n    .when(here, (el) => el.bg(p.selected))\n    .hover((el) => el.bg(here ? p.selected : p.hover))\n    .child(lane && !view.searching ? graphCell(lane, uncommitted, merge, width, p) : div().w(PAD).flex_shrink_0())\n    .children(labels(refs, p, color, view.history?.remotes ?? {}))\n    // Merge commits are muted.\n    .child(subject(commit.subject, uncommitted ? p.muted : merge ? p.dim : p.foreground))\n    .when(!uncommitted, (el) => el.child(author(commit.author, p)))\n    .child(div().w(32).flex_shrink_0().text_right().text_xs().text_color(p.dim).child(ago(now, commit.time)));\n}\n\nfunction moreRow(p: Palette): Element {\n  return div().h(ROW).px(12).flex().items_center().text_xs().text_color(p.accent).cursor_pointer().child(\"Show older commits\");\n}\n\nexport interface GraphActions {\n  pick: (hash: string, cx: Context) => void;\n  more: (cx: Context) => void;\n}\n\nexport function graphList(view: HistoryView, p: Palette, scroll: VirtualListScrollHandle, actions: GraphActions): Element {\n  const limited = Boolean(view.history?.limited) && !view.searching;\n  const count = view.rows.length + (limited ? 1 : 0);\n  const width = PAD * 2 + Math.max(1, view.lanes.width) * LANE;\n  const now = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);\n  if (view.history === null) return v_flex().flex_1().items_center().justify_center().text_color(p.dim).child(\"Reading history…\");\n  if (view.history.error) return v_flex().flex_1().p(14).text_color(p.removed).child(view.history.error);\n  if (count === 0) {\n    const empty = view.searching ? \"No commit matches\" : \"No commits yet\";\n    return v_flex().flex_1().items_center().justify_center().text_color(p.dim).child(empty);\n  }\n  return div()\n    .relative()\n    .flex_1()\n    .min_h_0()\n    .child(\n      v_virtual_list(GRAPH_LIST, count, ROW, (i) => view.rows[i]?.hash ?? MORE, (range) =>\n        Array.from({ length: range.end - range.start }, (_x, k) => range.start + k).map((i) =>\n          i < view.rows.length ? row(view, i, width, now, p) : moreRow(p),\n        ),\n      )\n        // Rows of a virtual list can't hold handlers: the list reports the row's key.\n        .on_item_click((key, cx) => (key === MORE ? actions.more(cx) : actions.pick(key, cx)))\n        .track_scroll(scroll)\n        .size_full(),\n    )\n    .child(Scrollbar.vertical(GRAPH_LIST).absolute().inset_0());\n}\n","numLines":224,"startLine":1,"totalLines":224}},"displayPath":"src/ui/graph.ts","savedCopyFraming":{"enveloped":false}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3834904e-b0c0-44a8-b309-9ad379de95e1","timestamp":"2026-11-18T15:42:16.077Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/graph.ts\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t// The commit graph: one row per commit with its lane lines, refs, subject,\n2\t// author and age. A virtual list, so only the rows on screen are built.\n3\t\n4\timport { div, PathBuilder, type Color, type Context, type Element } from \"gpui-kit\";\n5\timport { h_flex, v_flex, v_virtual_list, Scrollbar, type VirtualListScrollHandle } from \"gpui-base\";\n6\timport type { Commit } from \"../core/git/log.ts\";\n7\timport type { Ref } from \"../core/git/refs.ts\";\n8\timport type { LaneRow } from \"../core/graph/lanes.ts\";\n9\timport { UNCOMMITTED, type HistoryView } from \"../core/historyView.ts\";\n10\timport { ago } from \"../core/time.ts\";\n11\timport { refLabels, type RefLabel } from \"../core/graph/refLabels.ts\";\n12\timport { remoteKindOf, type RemoteKind } from \"../core/graph/remoteKind.ts\";\n13\timport { authorBadge, splitSubject } from \"../core/graph/rowText.ts\";\n14\timport { ICONS, icon, type Palette } from \"./style.ts\";\n15\t\n16\texport const ROW = 24;\n17\tconst LANE = 14;\n18\tconst PAD = 6;\n19\tconst MAX_LABELS = 3;\n20\texport const GRAPH_LIST = \"gitdeck-graph\";\n21\tconst MORE = \"gitdeck:more\";\n22\t\n23\tconst laneX = (lane: number) => PAD + lane * LANE + LANE / 2;\n24\tconst laneColor = (p: Palette, lane: number): Color => p.lanes[lane % p.lanes.length] ?? p.accent;\n25\t\n26\tfunction graphCell(row: LaneRow, uncommitted: boolean, merge: boolean, width: number, p: Palette): Element {\n27\t  // One stroked path per color keeps a row to a few paints however many lanes pass.\n28\t  const paths = new Map<string, { color: Color; path: PathBuilder }>();\n29\t  for (const s of row.segments) {\n30\t    const color = s.dashed ? p.dim : laneColor(p, s.to === s.from ? s.from : Math.max(s.from, s.to));\n31\t    const key = `${color}${s.dashed ? \"-\" : \"\"}`;\n32\t    const start = paths.get(key)?.path ?? (s.dashed ? PathBuilder.stroke(1.5).dash_array([3, 3]) : PathBuilder.stroke(1.5));\n33\t    const [ax, ay, bx, by] = [laneX(s.from), s.fromY * ROW, laneX(s.to), s.toY * ROW];\n34\t    const moved = start.move_to(ax, ay);\n35\t    const mid = (ay + by) / 2;\n36\t    paths.set(key, { color, path: ax === bx ? moved.line_to(bx, by) : moved.cubic_bezier_to(bx, by, ax, mid, bx, mid) });\n37\t  }\n38\t  const color = uncommitted ? p.dim : laneColor(p, row.lane);\n39\t  const dot = div().absolute().left(laneX(row.lane) - 4).top(ROW / 2 - 4).w(8).h(8).rounded(4);\n40\t  // A merge is a ring with a chevron in it, as Fork draws one.\n41\t  const ring = div()\n42\t    .absolute()\n43\t    .left(laneX(row.lane) - 6)\n44\t    .top(ROW / 2 - 6)\n45\t    .w(12)\n46\t    .h(12)\n47\t    .rounded(6)\n48\t    .border_2()\n49\t    .border_color(color)\n50\t    .bg(p.surface)\n51\t    .flex()\n52\t    .items_center()\n53\t    .justify_center()\n54\t    .child(icon(ICONS.chevron, color, 8));\n55\t  return div()\n56\t    .relative()\n57\t    .flex_shrink_0()\n58\t    .w(width)\n59\t    .h(ROW)\n60\t    .overflow_hidden()\n61\t    .children([...paths.values()].map(({ color, path }) => window.paint_path(path.build(), color).absolute().top(0).left(0).size_full()))\n62\t    .child(uncommitted ? dot.bg(p.surface).border_2().border_color(color) : merge ? ring : dot.bg(color));\n63\t}\n64\t\n65\tconst FORGE_ICONS: Readonly<Record<RemoteKind, string>> = { github: ICONS.github, gitlab: ICONS.gitlab, git: ICONS.git };\n66\t\n67\t/** The icons in a label's first box: the forges its remotes are on, else what it is. */\n68\tfunction glyphs(l: RefLabel, remotes: Readonly<Record<string, RemoteKind>>): string[] {\n69\t  if (l.kind === \"tag\") return [ICONS.tag];\n70\t  const forges = l.parts.filter((x) => x.kind === \"remote\").map((x) => FORGE_ICONS[remoteKindOf(x.name, remotes)]);\n71\t  return forges.length > 0 ? [...new Set(forges)] : [ICONS.branch];\n72\t}\n73\t\n74\t/**\n75\t * A ref label as Fork draws one: the forge (or tag, or branch) icon in a box of\n76\t * its own, then the name on a tint of the lane's color. A remote of the same\n77\t * name shows only as its forge's icon; the tooltip names every ref.\n78\t */\n79\tfunction label(l: RefLabel, p: Palette, color: Color, remotes: Readonly<Record<string, RemoteKind>>): Element {\n80\t  const edge = l.kind === \"tag\" ? tagColor(p) : color;\n81\t  const name = l.parts[0]?.text ?? \"\";\n82\t  const fg = l.current ? p.surface : p.foreground;\n83\t  return h_flex()\n84\t    .flex_shrink_0()\n85\t    .h(18)\n86\t    .gap(2)\n87\t    .items_center()\n88\t    .tooltip(l.parts.map((x) => x.name).join(\" · \"))\n89\t    .child(\n90\t      h_flex()\n91\t        .h_full()\n92\t        .px(3)\n93\t        .gap(2)\n94\t        .items_center()\n95\t        .rounded(4)\n96\t        .border_1()\n97\t        .border_color(edge)\n98\t        .children(glyphs(l, remotes).map((g) => icon(g, p.foreground, 11))),\n99\t    )\n100\t    .child(\n101\t      h_flex()\n102\t        .h_full()\n103\t        .px(5)\n104\t        .gap(3)\n105\t        .items_center()\n106\t        .rounded(4)\n107\t        .border_1()\n108\t        .border_color(edge)\n109\t        .bg(l.current ? edge : (`${edge}33` as Color))\n110\t        .when(l.current, (el) => el.child(icon(ICONS.check, fg, 10)))\n111\t        .child(div().text_xs().text_color(fg).when(l.current, (el) => el.font_semibold()).child(name)),\n112\t    );\n113\t}\n114\t\n115\tconst tagColor = (p: Palette): Color => p.lanes[2] ?? p.accent;\n116\t\n117\tfunction labels(refs: readonly Ref[], p: Palette, color: Color, remotes: Readonly<Record<string, RemoteKind>>): Element[] {\n118\t  const all = refLabels(refs);\n119\t  const shown = all.slice(0, MAX_LABELS).map((l) => label(l, p, color, remotes));\n120\t  const rest = all.length - MAX_LABELS;\n121\t  return rest > 0 ? [...shown, div().flex_shrink_0().text_xs().text_color(p.dim).child(`+${rest}`)] : shown;\n122\t}\n123\t\n124\t/** The subject, its conventional-commit type in bold. */\n125\tfunction subject(text: string, color: Color): Element {\n126\t  const { prefix, rest } = splitSubject(text);\n127\t  return h_flex()\n128\t    .flex_1()\n129\t    .min_w_0()\n130\t    .gap(3)\n131\t    .overflow_hidden()\n132\t    .text_color(color)\n133\t    .when(prefix !== \"\", (el) => el.child(div().flex_shrink_0().font_weight(700).child(prefix)))\n134\t    .child(div().min_w_0().truncate().child(rest.trimStart()));\n135\t}\n136\t\n137\t/** The author as initials on a color of their own: no picture is fetched. */\n138\tfunction author(name: string, p: Palette): Element {\n139\t  const { initials, color } = authorBadge(name, p.lanes.length);\n140\t  return h_flex()\n141\t    .w(110)\n142\t    .flex_shrink_0()\n143\t    .gap(5)\n144\t    .items_center()\n145\t    .child(\n146\t      div()\n147\t        .w(16)\n148\t        .h(16)\n149\t        .flex_shrink_0()\n150\t        .rounded(8)\n151\t        .bg(p.lanes[color] ?? p.accent)\n152\t        .flex()\n153\t        .items_center()\n154\t        .justify_center()\n155\t        .text_size(initials.length > 1 ? 7.5 : 9)\n156\t        .font_semibold()\n157\t        .text_color(p.surface)\n158\t        .child(initials),\n159\t    )\n160\t    .child(div().min_w_0().truncate().text_xs().text_color(p.muted).child(name));\n161\t}\n162\t\n163\tfunction row(view: HistoryView, i: number, width: number, now: number, p: Palette): Element {\n164\t  const commit = view.rows[i] as Commit;\n165\t  const uncommitted = commit.hash === UNCOMMITTED;\n166\t  const lane = view.lanes.rows[i];\n167\t  const here = commit.hash === view.selected;\n168\t  const color = lane ? laneColor(p, lane.lane) : p.accent;\n169\t  const refs = view.history?.byCommit[commit.hash] ?? [];\n170\t  const merge = commit.parents.length > 1;\n171\t  return h_flex()\n172\t    .h(ROW)\n173\t    .pr(8)\n174\t    .gap(6)\n175\t    .items_center()\n176\t    .cursor_pointer()\n177\t    .when(here, (el) => el.bg(p.selected))\n178\t    .hover((el) => el.bg(here ? p.selected : p.hover))\n179\t    .child(lane && !view.searching ? graphCell(lane, uncommitted, merge, width, p) : div().w(PAD).flex_shrink_0())\n180\t    .children(labels(refs, p, color, view.history?.remotes ?? {}))\n181\t    // Merge commits are muted.\n182\t    .child(subject(commit.subject, uncommitted ? p.muted : merge ? p.dim : p.foreground))\n183\t    .when(!uncommitted, (el) => el.child(author(commit.author, p)))\n184\t    .child(div().w(32).flex_shrink_0().text_right().text_xs().text_color(p.dim).child(ago(now, commit.time)));\n185\t}\n186\t\n187\tfunction moreRow(p: Palette): Element {\n188\t  return div().h(ROW).px(12).flex().items_center().text_xs().text_color(p.accent).cursor_pointer().child(\"Show older commits\");\n189\t}\n190\t\n191\texport interface GraphActions {\n192\t  pick: (hash: string, cx: Context) => void;\n193\t  more: (cx: Context) => void;\n194\t}\n195\t\n196\texport function graphList(view: HistoryView, p: Palette, scroll: VirtualListScrollHandle, actions: GraphActions): Element {\n197\t  const limited = Boolean(view.history?.limited) && !view.searching;\n198\t  const count = view.rows.length + (limited ? 1 : 0);\n199\t  const width = PAD * 2 + Math.max(1, view.lanes.width) * LANE;\n200\t  const now = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);\n201\t  if (view.history === null) return v_flex().flex_1().items_center().justify_center().text_color(p.dim).child(\"Reading history…\");\n202\t  if (view.history.error) return v_flex().flex_1().p(14).text_color(p.removed).child(view.history.error);\n203\t  if (count === 0) {\n204\t    const empty = view.searching ? \"No commit matches\" : \"No commits yet\";\n205\t    return v_flex().flex_1().items_center().justify_center().text_color(p.dim).child(empty);\n206\t  }\n207\t  return div()\n208\t    .relative()\n209\t    .flex_1()\n210\t    .min_h_0()\n211\t    .child(\n212\t      v_virtual_list(GRAPH_LIST, count, ROW, (i) => view.rows[i]?.hash ?? MORE, (range) =>\n213\t        Array.from({ length: range.end - range.start }, (_x, k) => range.start + k).map((i) =>\n214\t          i < view.rows.length ? row(view, i, width, now, p) : moreRow(p),\n215\t        ),\n216\t      )\n217\t        // Rows of a virtual list can't hold handlers: the list reports the row's key.\n218\t        .on_item_click((key, cx) => (key === MORE ? actions.more(cx) : actions.pick(key, cx)))\n219\t        .track_scroll(scroll)\n220\t        .size_full(),\n221\t    )\n222\t    .child(Scrollbar.vertical(GRAPH_LIST).absolute().inset_0());\n223\t}\n224\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
{"parentUuid":"3834904e-b0c0-44a8-b309-9ad379de95e1","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"compact_file_reference","filename":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/main.ts","displayPath":"src/main.ts"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"fa31da58-2427-4ed4-88ed-e0bf468a967d","timestamp":"2026-11-18T15:42:16.077Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/main.ts was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
{"parentUuid":"fa31da58-2427-4ed4-88ed-e0bf468a967d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"compact_file_reference","filename":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/review.ts","displayPath":"src/ui/review.ts"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d3f48a25-a3ee-4b3a-b4a6-290ced0b943c","timestamp":"2026-11-18T15:42:16.077Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/review.ts was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
{"parentUuid":"d3f48a25-a3ee-4b3a-b4a6-290ced0b943c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/core/forge/index.ts","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/core/forge/index.ts","content":"// The repo's forge (GitHub or GitLab), read through its CLI. The CLI is pointed\n// at the project and run outside the repo, so it never reads the work tree or\n// the repo's config.\n\nimport type { Exec, Git, Target } from \"../git/runner.ts\";\nimport { parseBranchPr, parsePrs, prListArgs, prViewArgs } from \"./github.ts\";\nimport { failedJobsArgs, mrListArgs, mrViewArgs, parseBranchMr, parseFailedJobs, parseMrs, pipelineId } from \"./gitlab.ts\";\nimport { forgeOf, parseRemote } from \"./remote.ts\";\nimport { discussionsArgs, parseDiscussions, parseThreads, threadsArgs, type ReviewThread } from \"./reviewThreads.ts\";\nimport type { BranchPr, Forge, ForgeChoice, ForgeKind, PrList } from \"./types.ts\";\n\nexport type { BranchPr, Checks, Forge, ForgeChoice, ForgeKind, PrList, PullRequest } from \"./types.ts\";\nexport type { ReviewThread } from \"./reviewThreads.ts\";\n\n/** Where to ask the CLIs which hosts they are signed in to: outside the repo. */\ninterface Probe {\n  exec: Exec;\n  away: string;\n}\n\n/**\n * The forge whose CLI alone is signed in to `host` (the person logged in there\n * themselves, so pointing that CLI at it is safe); null when neither or both are.\n * The token each prints is only checked for being there, never kept.\n */\nasync function signedInForge(probe: Probe, target: Target, host: string): Promise<ForgeKind | null> {\n  const has = (cli: string, args: string[]): Promise<boolean> =>\n    probe.exec(cli, args, { cwd: probe.away, on: target.on }).then(\n      (r) => r.code === 0 && r.stdout.trim() !== \"\",\n      () => false,\n    );\n  const [gitlab, github] = await Promise.all([\n    has(\"glab\", [\"config\", \"get\", \"token\", \"--host\", host]),\n    has(\"gh\", [\"auth\", \"token\", \"--hostname\", host]),\n  ]);\n  return gitlab === github ? null : gitlab ? \"gitlab\" : \"github\";\n}\n\n/**\n * origin's host, and its forge; `git config gitdeck.forge github|gitlab|none` names\n * it for any host. With a probe, an unnamed host is read from the signed-in CLIs.\n * The host comes back only while it's unnamed: the person is asked which it is.\n */\nasync function readOrigin(git: Git, target: Target, probe?: Probe): Promise<{ forge: Forge | null; host: string | null }> {\n  const [url, override] = await Promise.all([\n    git(target, [\"remote\", \"get-url\", \"origin\"]).catch(() => \"\"),\n    git(target, [\"config\", \"--get\", \"gitdeck.forge\"]).then((v) => v.trim(), () => null),\n  ]);\n  const remote = parseRemote(url);\n  const forge = forgeOf(remote, override);\n  if (forge !== null || remote === null || override !== null || !probe) return { forge, host: forge === null && override === null ? (remote?.host ?? null) : null };\n  const kind = await signedInForge(probe, target, remote.host);\n  const found = kind === null ? null : forgeOf(remote, kind);\n  return { forge: found, host: found === null ? remote.host : null };\n}\n\nexport async function readForge(git: Git, target: Target): Promise<Forge | null> {\n  return (await readOrigin(git, target)).forge;\n}\n\n/** Names origin's forge for this repo (its own .git/config), for a host that isn't github.com or gitlab.com; \"none\" stops the asking. */\nexport async function setForge(git: Git, target: Target, kind: ForgeChoice): Promise<void> {\n  await git(target, [\"config\", \"--local\", \"gitdeck.forge\", kind]);\n}\n\nconst failure = (cli: string, error: unknown): string => `Can't run ${cli}: ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}`;\n\n/** `away` is a folder outside the repo (home) for the CLI to run in. */\nexport async function loadPrs(git: Git, exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string): Promise<PrList> {\n  const { forge, host } = await readOrigin(git, target, { exec, away });\n  if (forge === null) {\n    const error = host === null ? \"No GitHub or GitLab remote: origin isn't one\" : `origin is on ${host}: is it GitLab or GitHub?`;\n    return { items: [], error, repo: null, label: \"PR\", host };\n  }\n  const base = { repo: forge.repo, label: forge.label, host: null };\n  const args = forge.kind === \"github\" ? prListArgs(forge.repo) : mrListArgs(forge.repo);\n  try {\n    const r = await exec(forge.cli, args, { cwd: away, on: target.on });\n    if (r.code !== 0) return { ...base, items: [], error: r.stderr.split(\"\\n\")[0] || `${forge.cli} failed (${r.code})` };\n    return { ...base, items: forge.kind === \"github\" ? parsePrs(r.stdout) : parseMrs(r.stdout), error: null };\n  } catch (error) {\n    return { ...base, items: [], error: failure(forge.cli, error) };\n  }\n}\n\n/** A failed MR pipeline with its failed jobs in place of itself; as it was when they can't be read. */\nasync function withFailedJobs(exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string, repo: string, pr: BranchPr, pipeline: number | null): Promise<BranchPr> {\n  if (pr.checks.failed === 0 || pipeline === null) return pr;\n  try {\n    const r = await exec(\"glab\", failedJobsArgs(repo, pipeline), { cwd: away, on: target.on });\n    const jobs = r.code === 0 ? parseFailedJobs(r.stdout, repo) : [];\n    return jobs.length > 0 ? { ...pr, failed: jobs } : pr;\n  } catch {\n    return pr;\n  }\n}\n\n/** The CLIs' words for \"this branch has none\". */\nconst NONE = /no pull requests found|no (?:open )?merge requests? (?:available|found)/i;\n\nexport interface BranchPrState {\n  pr: BranchPr | null;\n  error: string | null;\n  label: \"PR\" | \"MR\";\n  /** origin's host when it isn't a known forge yet: the person names which it is. */\n  host: string | null;\n  /** The forge read, or null when origin isn't one (or isn't named yet). */\n  forge: ForgeKind | null;\n}\n\n/** The branch's PR or MR; none (and no error) without a forge or one to show. Without a branch, only the forge. */\nexport async function loadBranchPr(git: Git, exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string, branch: string | null): Promise<BranchPrState> {\n  const { forge, host: origin } = await readOrigin(git, target, { exec, away });\n  if (forge === null) return { pr: null, error: null, label: \"PR\", host: origin, forge: null };\n  const label = forge.label;\n  const host = null;\n  const known = { label, host, forge: forge.kind };\n  if (branch === null) return { pr: null, error: null, ...known };\n  const args = forge.kind === \"github\" ? prViewArgs(forge.repo, branch) : mrViewArgs(forge.repo, branch);\n  try {\n    const r = await exec(forge.cli, args, { cwd: away, on: target.on });\n    if (r.code === 0) {\n      const pr = forge.kind === \"github\" ? parseBranchPr(r.stdout, forge.repo) : parseBranchMr(r.stdout);\n      return { pr: pr && forge.kind === \"gitlab\" ? await withFailedJobs(exec, target, away, forge.repo, pr, pipelineId(r.stdout)) : pr, error: null, ...known };\n    }\n    if (NONE.test(r.stderr)) return { pr: null, error: null, ...known };\n    return { pr: null, error: r.stderr.split(\"\\n\")[0] || `${forge.cli} failed (${r.code})`, ...known };\n  } catch (error) {\n    return { pr: null, error: failure(forge.cli, error), ...known };\n  }\n}\n\n/** The open review threads on PR/MR `number`: read once, when the person asks for them. */\nexport async function loadReviewThreads(git: Git, exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string, number: number): Promise<{ threads: ReviewThread[]; error: string | null }> {\n  const { forge } = await readOrigin(git, target);\n  if (forge === null) return { threads: [], error: \"No GitHub or GitLab remote\" };\n  const args = forge.kind === \"github\" ? threadsArgs(forge.repo, number) : discussionsArgs(forge.repo, number);\n  try {\n    const r = await exec(forge.cli, args, { cwd: away, on: target.on });\n    if (r.code !== 0) return { threads: [], error: r.stderr.split(\"\\n\")[0] || `${forge.cli} failed (${r.code})` };\n    return { threads: forge.kind === \"github\" ? parseThreads(r.stdout) : parseDiscussions(r.stdout), error: null };\n  } catch (error) {\n    return { threads: [], error: failure(forge.cli, error) };\n  }\n}\n","numLines":146,"startLine":1,"totalLines":146}},"displayPath":"src/core/forge/index.ts","savedCopyFraming":{"enveloped":false}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ce69b378-b644-473b-a4f5-948dbe3650fa","timestamp":"2026-11-18T15:42:16.077Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/core/forge/index.ts\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t// The repo's forge (GitHub or GitLab), read through its CLI. The CLI is pointed\n2\t// at the project and run outside the repo, so it never reads the work tree or\n3\t// the repo's config.\n4\t\n5\timport type { Exec, Git, Target } from \"../git/runner.ts\";\n6\timport { parseBranchPr, parsePrs, prListArgs, prViewArgs } from \"./github.ts\";\n7\timport { failedJobsArgs, mrListArgs, mrViewArgs, parseBranchMr, parseFailedJobs, parseMrs, pipelineId } from \"./gitlab.ts\";\n8\timport { forgeOf, parseRemote } from \"./remote.ts\";\n9\timport { discussionsArgs, parseDiscussions, parseThreads, threadsArgs, type ReviewThread } from \"./reviewThreads.ts\";\n10\timport type { BranchPr, Forge, ForgeChoice, ForgeKind, PrList } from \"./types.ts\";\n11\t\n12\texport type { BranchPr, Checks, Forge, ForgeChoice, ForgeKind, PrList, PullRequest } from \"./types.ts\";\n13\texport type { ReviewThread } from \"./reviewThreads.ts\";\n14\t\n15\t/** Where to ask the CLIs which hosts they are signed in to: outside the repo. */\n16\tinterface Probe {\n17\t  exec: Exec;\n18\t  away: string;\n19\t}\n20\t\n21\t/**\n22\t * The forge whose CLI alone is signed in to `host` (the person logged in there\n23\t * themselves, so pointing that CLI at it is safe); null when neither or both are.\n24\t * The token each prints is only checked for being there, never kept.\n25\t */\n26\tasync function signedInForge(probe: Probe, target: Target, host: string): Promise<ForgeKind | null> {\n27\t  const has = (cli: string, args: string[]): Promise<boolean> =>\n28\t    probe.exec(cli, args, { cwd: probe.away, on: target.on }).then(\n29\t      (r) => r.code === 0 && r.stdout.trim() !== \"\",\n30\t      () => false,\n31\t    );\n32\t  const [gitlab, github] = await Promise.all([\n33\t    has(\"glab\", [\"config\", \"get\", \"token\", \"--host\", host]),\n34\t    has(\"gh\", [\"auth\", \"token\", \"--hostname\", host]),\n35\t  ]);\n36\t  return gitlab === github ? null : gitlab ? \"gitlab\" : \"github\";\n37\t}\n38\t\n39\t/**\n40\t * origin's host, and its forge; `git config gitdeck.forge github|gitlab|none` names\n41\t * it for any host. With a probe, an unnamed host is read from the signed-in CLIs.\n42\t * The host comes back only while it's unnamed: the person is asked which it is.\n43\t */\n44\tasync function readOrigin(git: Git, target: Target, probe?: Probe): Promise<{ forge: Forge | null; host: string | null }> {\n45\t  const [url, override] = await Promise.all([\n46\t    git(target, [\"remote\", \"get-url\", \"origin\"]).catch(() => \"\"),\n47\t    git(target, [\"config\", \"--get\", \"gitdeck.forge\"]).then((v) => v.trim(), () => null),\n48\t  ]);\n49\t  const remote = parseRemote(url);\n50\t  const forge = forgeOf(remote, override);\n51\t  if (forge !== null || remote === null || override !== null || !probe) return { forge, host: forge === null && override === null ? (remote?.host ?? null) : null };\n52\t  const kind = await signedInForge(probe, target, remote.host);\n53\t  const found = kind === null ? null : forgeOf(remote, kind);\n54\t  return { forge: found, host: found === null ? remote.host : null };\n55\t}\n56\t\n57\texport async function readForge(git: Git, target: Target): Promise<Forge | null> {\n58\t  return (await readOrigin(git, target)).forge;\n59\t}\n60\t\n61\t/** Names origin's forge for this repo (its own .git/config), for a host that isn't github.com or gitlab.com; \"none\" stops the asking. */\n62\texport async function setForge(git: Git, target: Target, kind: ForgeChoice): Promise<void> {\n63\t  await git(target, [\"config\", \"--local\", \"gitdeck.forge\", kind]);\n64\t}\n65\t\n66\tconst failure = (cli: string, error: unknown): string => `Can't run ${cli}: ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}`;\n67\t\n68\t/** `away` is a folder outside the repo (home) for the CLI to run in. */\n69\texport async function loadPrs(git: Git, exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string): Promise<PrList> {\n70\t  const { forge, host } = await readOrigin(git, target, { exec, away });\n71\t  if (forge === null) {\n72\t    const error = host === null ? \"No GitHub or GitLab remote: origin isn't one\" : `origin is on ${host}: is it GitLab or GitHub?`;\n73\t    return { items: [], error, repo: null, label: \"PR\", host };\n74\t  }\n75\t  const base = { repo: forge.repo, label: forge.label, host: null };\n76\t  const args = forge.kind === \"github\" ? prListArgs(forge.repo) : mrListArgs(forge.repo);\n77\t  try {\n78\t    const r = await exec(forge.cli, args, { cwd: away, on: target.on });\n79\t    if (r.code !== 0) return { ...base, items: [], error: r.stderr.split(\"\\n\")[0] || `${forge.cli} failed (${r.code})` };\n80\t    return { ...base, items: forge.kind === \"github\" ? parsePrs(r.stdout) : parseMrs(r.stdout), error: null };\n81\t  } catch (error) {\n82\t    return { ...base, items: [], error: failure(forge.cli, error) };\n83\t  }\n84\t}\n85\t\n86\t/** A failed MR pipeline with its failed jobs in place of itself; as it was when they can't be read. */\n87\tasync function withFailedJobs(exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string, repo: string, pr: BranchPr, pipeline: number | null): Promise<BranchPr> {\n88\t  if (pr.checks.failed === 0 || pipeline === null) return pr;\n89\t  try {\n90\t    const r = await exec(\"glab\", failedJobsArgs(repo, pipeline), { cwd: away, on: target.on });\n91\t    const jobs = r.code === 0 ? parseFailedJobs(r.stdout, repo) : [];\n92\t    return jobs.length > 0 ? { ...pr, failed: jobs } : pr;\n93\t  } catch {\n94\t    return pr;\n95\t  }\n96\t}\n97\t\n98\t/** The CLIs' words for \"this branch has none\". */\n99\tconst NONE = /no pull requests found|no (?:open )?merge requests? (?:available|found)/i;\n100\t\n101\texport interface BranchPrState {\n102\t  pr: BranchPr | null;\n103\t  error: string | null;\n104\t  label: \"PR\" | \"MR\";\n105\t  /** origin's host when it isn't a known forge yet: the person names which it is. */\n106\t  host: string | null;\n107\t  /** The forge read, or null when origin isn't one (or isn't named yet). */\n108\t  forge: ForgeKind | null;\n109\t}\n110\t\n111\t/** The branch's PR or MR; none (and no error) without a forge or one to show. Without a branch, only the forge. */\n112\texport async function loadBranchPr(git: Git, exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string, branch: string | null): Promise<BranchPrState> {\n113\t  const { forge, host: origin } = await readOrigin(git, target, { exec, away });\n114\t  if (forge === null) return { pr: null, error: null, label: \"PR\", host: origin, forge: null };\n115\t  const label = forge.label;\n116\t  const host = null;\n117\t  const known = { label, host, forge: forge.kind };\n118\t  if (branch === null) return { pr: null, error: null, ...known };\n119\t  const args = forge.kind === \"github\" ? prViewArgs(forge.repo, branch) : mrViewArgs(forge.repo, branch);\n120\t  try {\n121\t    const r = await exec(forge.cli, args, { cwd: away, on: target.on });\n122\t    if (r.code === 0) {\n123\t      const pr = forge.kind === \"github\" ? parseBranchPr(r.stdout, forge.repo) : parseBranchMr(r.stdout);\n124\t      return { pr: pr && forge.kind === \"gitlab\" ? await withFailedJobs(exec, target, away, forge.repo, pr, pipelineId(r.stdout)) : pr, error: null, ...known };\n125\t    }\n126\t    if (NONE.test(r.stderr)) return { pr: null, error: null, ...known };\n127\t    return { pr: null, error: r.stderr.split(\"\\n\")[0] || `${forge.cli} failed (${r.code})`, ...known };\n128\t  } catch (error) {\n129\t    return { pr: null, error: failure(forge.cli, error), ...known };\n130\t  }\n131\t}\n132\t\n133\t/** The open review threads on PR/MR `number`: read once, when the person asks for them. */\n134\texport async function loadReviewThreads(git: Git, exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string, number: number): Promise<{ threads: ReviewThread[]; error: string | null }> {\n135\t  const { forge } = await readOrigin(git, target);\n136\t  if (forge === null) return { threads: [], error: \"No GitHub or GitLab remote\" };\n137\t  const args = forge.kind === \"github\" ? threadsArgs(forge.repo, number) : discussionsArgs(forge.repo, number);\n138\t  try {\n139\t    const r = await exec(forge.cli, args, { cwd: away, on: target.on });\n140\t    if (r.code !== 0) return { threads: [], error: r.stderr.split(\"\\n\")[0] || `${forge.cli} failed (${r.code})` };\n141\t    return { threads: forge.kind === \"github\" ? parseThreads(r.stdout) : parseDiscussions(r.stdout), error: null };\n142\t  } catch (error) {\n143\t    return { threads: [], error: failure(forge.cli, error) };\n144\t  }\n145\t}\n146\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
