{"parentUuid":"b1eff1fc-f4a6-4896-9064-2b773fa3740a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"43eb4842-444d-4542-9f2c-31b194183d64","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BtKCFDweTEWiK7HvSrAE54","type":"tool_result","content":"  on `globalThis` out of the module's top level.\n- A copy starts the first time it shows, then stays alive while its block is in\n  the layout, shown or not (a hidden column, the other child of a stack, a pane\n  in another tab or behind a zoom): switching back finds it as it was. Its\n  timers keep running while hidden, so poll gently. Another layout starts its\n  mods fresh (pane mods belong to their tab and stay); a block removed or given\n  another mod or props starts over. `<mod>.<command>` reaches shown copies only.\n- Images and SVGs are referenced from `~/.config/herdr-app`:\n  `image(\"mods/<name>/logo.svg\")` (full color), `svg(\"mods/<name>/icon.svg\")`\n  (tinted with the text color). Saving an asset under `mods/` updates every\n  mod showing it, including images that were missing or invalid on first load.\n- The defaults are mods too, read them as examples: `spaces`, `agents`,\n  `tabs` (the tab bar), `menu`, `prompt`, `confirm`, `help`, `toast`,\n  Terminals' `picker`, `peek`, and `pane` (an\n  example pane header, not used by the default layouts), and `worktree`\n  (git worktrees as spaces: the space menu's and the + menu's New worktree,\n  export const platform: string;\n  export const arch: string;\n  const process: { run: typeof run; exit: typeof exit; nextTick: typeof nextTick; platform: string; arch: string };\n  export default process;\n}\ndeclare module \"os\" {\n  export function platform(): string;\n  export function arch(): string;\n  export const EOL: string;\n  const os: { platform: typeof platform; arch: typeof arch; EOL: string };\n  export default os;\n}\ndeclare module \"fs/promises\" {\n  export interface Dirent { name: string; isDirectory(): boolean; }\n  export interface MakeDirectoryOptions { recursive?: boolean; }\n  export function readFile(path: string): Promise<Uint8Array>;\n  export function readFile(path: string, encoding: \"utf8\" | { encoding: \"utf8\" }): Promise<string>;\n  export function writeFile(path: string, contents: string | Uint8Array): Promise<void>;\n  export function readdir(path: string): Promise<string[]>;\n  export function readdir(path: string, options: { withFileTypes: true }): Promise<Dirent[]>;\n  export function exists(path: string): Promise<boolean>;\n  export function unlink(path: string): Promise<void>;\n  export function rmdir(path: string): Promise<void>;\n  export function mkdir(path: string, options?: MakeDirectoryOptions): Promise<void>;\n}\ndeclare module \"net\" {\n  export interface Socket {\n    write(data: string): Promise<void>;\n    /** Reads raw bytes. Resolves to null after the peer reaches EOF. */\n    read(maxBytes?: number): Promise<Uint8Array | null>;\n    close(): void;\n  }\n  export function connect(host: string, port: number): Promise<Socket>;\n  const net: { connect: typeof connect };\n  export default net;\n}\n// The style surface here is generated from the same tables the runtime\n// dispatches through, so a style method that type-checks exists at run time,\n// and a length or color the compiler refuses is one the runtime would refuse\n// too. Put `// @ts-check` at the top of a script to have an editor check it.\n//\n// What is not expressed: capability grants (a denied `fs.readFile` still\n// type-checks), element and `cx` lifetimes (both belong to one call), and\n// which component a method suits (all elements share one prototype).\n\ndeclare module \"gpui-kit\" {\n  /**\n{\n  \"place\": \"none\",\n  \"title\": \"GitDeck\"\n}\nShell cwd was reset to /Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3422d19e-b426-4a57-a06a-d02a8d5ed768","timestamp":"2026-11-19T00:43:57.879Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"  on `globalThis` out of the module's top level.\n- A copy starts the first time it shows, then stays alive while its block is in\n  the layout, shown or not (a hidden column, the other child of a stack, a pane\n  in another tab or behind a zoom): switching back finds it as it was. Its\n  timers keep running while hidden, so poll gently. Another layout starts its\n  mods fresh (pane mods belong to their tab and stay); a block removed or given\n  another mod or props starts over. `<mod>.<command>` reaches shown copies only.\n- Images and SVGs are referenced from `~/.config/herdr-app`:\n  `image(\"mods/<name>/logo.svg\")` (full color), `svg(\"mods/<name>/icon.svg\")`\n  (tinted with the text color). Saving an asset under `mods/` updates every\n  mod showing it, including images that were missing or invalid on first load.\n- The defaults are mods too, read them as examples: `spaces`, `agents`,\n  `tabs` (the tab bar), `menu`, `prompt`, `confirm`, `help`, `toast`,\n  Terminals' `picker`, `peek`, and `pane` (an\n  example pane header, not used by the default layouts), and `worktree`\n  (git worktrees as spaces: the space menu's and the + menu's New worktree,\n  export const platform: string;\n  export const arch: string;\n  const process: { run: typeof run; exit: typeof exit; nextTick: typeof nextTick; platform: string; arch: string };\n  export default process;\n}\ndeclare module \"os\" {\n  export function platform(): string;\n  export function arch(): string;\n  export const EOL: string;\n  const os: { platform: typeof platform; arch: typeof arch; EOL: string };\n  export default os;\n}\ndeclare module \"fs/promises\" {\n  export interface Dirent { name: string; isDirectory(): boolean; }\n  export interface MakeDirectoryOptions { recursive?: boolean; }\n  export function readFile(path: string): Promise<Uint8Array>;\n  export function readFile(path: string, encoding: \"utf8\" | { encoding: \"utf8\" }): Promise<string>;\n  export function writeFile(path: string, contents: string | Uint8Array): Promise<void>;\n  export function readdir(path: string): Promise<string[]>;\n  export function readdir(path: string, options: { withFileTypes: true }): Promise<Dirent[]>;\n  export function exists(path: string): Promise<boolean>;\n  export function unlink(path: string): Promise<void>;\n  export function rmdir(path: string): Promise<void>;\n  export function mkdir(path: string, options?: MakeDirectoryOptions): Promise<void>;\n}\ndeclare module \"net\" {\n  export interface Socket {\n    write(data: string): Promise<void>;\n    /** Reads raw bytes. Resolves to null after the peer reaches EOF. */\n    read(maxBytes?: number): Promise<Uint8Array | null>;\n    close(): void;\n  }\n  export function connect(host: string, port: number): Promise<Socket>;\n  const net: { connect: typeof connect };\n  export default net;\n}\n// The style surface here is generated from the same tables the runtime\n// dispatches through, so a style method that type-checks exists at run time,\n// and a length or color the compiler refuses is one the runtime would refuse\n// too. Put `// @ts-check` at the top of a script to have an editor check it.\n//\n// What is not expressed: capability grants (a denied `fs.readFile` still\n// type-checks), element and `cx` lifetimes (both belong to one call), and\n// which component a method suits (all elements share one prototype).\n\ndeclare module \"gpui-kit\" {\n  /**\n{\n  \"place\": \"none\",\n  \"title\": \"GitDeck\"\n}","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b1eff1fc-f4a6-4896-9064-2b773fa3740a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"hook","reasonType":"hook"},"session_id":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
