{"parentUuid":"d159b15c-5b55-457a-8672-133cec51923e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1966b8c8-4566-430c-b019-a30dab143dae","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Artifact, AskUserQuestion, Bash, Edit, Glob, Grep, ListAgents, Read, Skill, TaskCreate, TaskStop, TaskUpdate, ToolSearch, Write, mcp__firecrawl__firecrawl_search</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Always reply in Korean. The user corrected me once: \"한글로 말하라고..\".\n   - Narrow the gap between the author name and the date in History. Done.\n   - Make the forge icon show GitLab for a company GitLab host whose name lacks \"gitlab\". The user first chose \"설정만 안내\", then asked that once gh/glab detection decides, gitdeck save `git config gitdeck.forge`. Done.\n   - Fix the graph still showing the git icon after the setting was saved. Done: history now reloads when remote settings change.\n   - Test whether the mod folder can hold saved files. Done and reported.\n   - Latest request: \"그럼 유저 사진 보여주는 거 구현해줘\" (implement showing user photos). Implemented and verified on the herdr-gitdeck repo. The final Korean report to the user has not been given yet.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Herdr mod rules:\n     - Code runs in QuickJS: no Node APIs, and no `URL` global.\n     - `exec(cmd, args[], {cwd,on,timeout})` takes an argument array (no shell), with a 30 s limit and no stdin.\n     - `fs/promises` (`readdir`, `writeFile`) can write under `~/.config/herdr-app`.\n     - `image(path)` resolves relative to `~/.config/herdr-app`.\n     - Saving any file in a mod folder reloads the mod, except hidden files and folders.\n   - Image behavior found by testing:\n     - A path drawn while its file is missing is remembered as missing.\n     - Overwriting a file in a hidden folder doesn't refresh the screen.\n     - So draw only after the download finishes, and save each picture once under a fixed name.\n     - The `Avatar` and `AvatarImage` components (from gpui-base) blank the virtual list; use `image(...).w(16).h(16).rounded(8)` instead.\n   - `AsyncContext` extends `Context`, so it has `cx.spawn`.\n   - Verification flow:\n     - `pnpm verify` (typecheck, coverage, build).\n     - `pnpm -s dev` (installs into `~/.config/herdr-app/mods/gitdeck`).\n     - `herdr-app status` for errors.\n     - `herdr-app shot <file>` for screenshots.\n     - `herdr-app do gitdeck.tab:history` to switch tabs.\n   - Privacy:\n     - No Gravatar.\n     - Picture files are named by a hash of the email.\n     - CLIs run in the home folder (`away`).\n     - Downloads are https-only, both direct and on redirect.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - `src/ui/graph.ts` (modified):\n     - The author column is now `.w(96)` and the age column `.w(26)`.\n     - It imports `image` from \"gpui-kit\".\n     - `author(name, picture: string | null, p)` draws `image(picture).w(16).h(16).flex_shrink_0().rounded(8)` when a picture exists, otherwise the initials `div`.\n     - New: `export type AvatarOf = (email: string) => string | null;`\n     - `row(..., avatar: AvatarOf)` uses `author(commit.author, avatar(commit.email), p)`.\n     - `graphList(view, p, scroll, actions, avatar: AvatarOf)`.\n\n   - `src/ui/historyPane.ts` (modified):\n     - `HistoryParts` gains `avatar: (email: string) => string | null;`.\n     - It calls `graphList(view, p, parts.scroll, actions, parts.avatar)`.\n\n   - `src/main.ts` (modified; already 893+ lines):\n     - Added the import `import { Avatars } from \"./avatars.ts\";`.\n     - Added the field `readonly avatars = new Avatars();`.\n     - In `readHistory`, after `withHistory`:\n       ```ts\n       const history = read.history;\n       // Its own task: looking up pictures never holds up the git task.\n       if (history.avatars) cx.spawn(async (cx) => this.avatars.load(this.git, target, await this.homeFor(target), history.commits, cx));\n       ```\n     - In the `historyPane` parts: `avatar: (email) => (this.view.history?.avatars ? this.avatars.path(email) : null),`.\n\n   - `src/avatars.ts` (new): an `Avatars` class.\n     - `SHOWN_DIR = \"mods/gitdeck/.avatars\"` and `MAX_NEW = 60`.\n     - Private state: `files` (base → file), `asked` set, `listed`, `busy`.\n     - `path(email)` returns `${SHOWN_DIR}/${file}` or null.\n     - `dir()` is `${home()}/.config/herdr-app/${SHOWN_DIR}`.\n     - `list()` runs `mkdir -p`, reads the folder with `readdir`, and loads it via `knownAvatars`.\n     - `wanted(commits)` picks one commit per new email.\n     - `load(git, target, away, commits, cx)`:\n       1. Lists the saved files.\n       2. Marks the new authors as asked.\n       3. Reads the source with `readAvatarSource`.\n       4. Finds URLs with `findAvatarUrls`.\n       5. Downloads each with `downloadAvatar`, updating `files` immutably and calling `cx.notify()` after each.\n\n   - `src/core/avatars.ts` (new):\n     - `AvatarSource {kind:\"github\"|\"gitlab\", host, path}` and `AvatarWanted {email, hash}`.\n     - `avatarsOn(configOut)` returns true when the `gitdeck.avatars` line is true, yes, on or 1.\n     - `avatarBase(email)` is a 16-hex double FNV-1a hash of the trimmed, lowercased email.\n     - `noreplyAvatar(email)` turns `123+x@users.noreply.github.com` into `https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123?s=64`.\n     - `knownAvatars(names)` keeps `^[0-9a-f]{16}\\.(png|jpg|gif|webp)$`.\n     - `githubQuery(owner, name, hashes)` builds GraphQL aliases `cN: object(oid:\"…\"){... on Commit{author{email user{avatarUrl(size: 64)}}}}`. It validates names against `^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$` and hashes against `^[0-9a-f]{4,64}$`.\n     - `parseGithubAvatars(stdout)`.\n     - `parseGitlabAvatar(stdout)` accepts https only, rejects hosts matching `/(^|\\.)gravatar\\.com$/i`, and uses a regex for the host instead of `URL`.\n     - `findAvatarUrls(exec, target, away, source, wanted)`:\n       - GitHub: `gh api graphql --hostname <host> -f query=…`, in batches of 50.\n       - GitLab: `glab api \"avatar?email=<enc>&size=64\" --hostname <host>`, once per email.\n     - `downloadAvatar(exec, dir, url, base)`:\n       - Accepts https only.\n       - Runs `curl -fsSL --proto =https --proto-redir =https --max-time 15 --max-filesize 2000000 -o <dir>/<base>.tmp -w %{content_type} -- url`.\n       - If the content type is an image, runs `mv -f` to `<base>.<ext>`; otherwise runs `rm -f` on the tmp file and returns null.\n\n   - `src/core/forge/index.ts` (modified):\n     - In `readOrigin` after `signedInForge`:\n       ```ts\n       // Kept as gitdeck.forge, so what reads only the config (the graph's icons) knows it too.\n       if (kind !== null) await setForge(git, target, kind).catch(() => undefined);\n       ```\n     - New `readAvatarSource(git, target)` reads the origin URL and `gitdeck.forge`, then calls `forgeOf`. It returns `{kind, host: remote.host, path: remote.path}` or null.\n     - Imports `type AvatarSource`.\n\n   - `src/core/history.ts` (modified):\n     - `History` gains `avatars: boolean` (EMPTY_HISTORY has `avatars: false`), set from `avatarsOn(remotesOut)`.\n     - New `readRemotes` helper.\n     - `loadHistory(git, target, limit, knownRefs?, knownRemotes?)`.\n     - `refreshHistory` reads refs and remotes in parallel and builds the key as `${limit}\\x1e${extra}\\x1e${refsOut}\\x1e${remotesOut}`.\n\n   - `src/core/graph/remoteKind.ts` (modified): `REMOTES_ARGS = [\"config\",\"--get-regexp\",\"^(remote\\\\..*\\\\.url|gitdeck\\\\.(forge|avatars))$\"]`.\n\n   - Tests:\n     - `tests/avatars.test.ts` (new, 9 tests).\n     - `tests/forge.test.ts`: tests that the detected forge is saved, and a `readAvatarSource` test.\n     - `tests/history.test.ts`: a reload test for when the forge is named, and a test for the `avatars` setting.\n     - `tests/rowStyle.test.ts`: the `REMOTES_ARGS` assertion and test name updated.\n\n   - Other repo found: `bsp-display-service` is at `/Volumes/WorkSpace/uzen/bsp/bsp-display-service`, with origin `https://bsp-git.uzen.io/bsp/bsp-display-service.git` and `gitdeck.forge gitlab` now set. A worktree is at `/Users/allan/orca/workspaces/bsp/BNKR-3710/bsp-display-service`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - I replied in English once. The user said \"한글로 말하라고..\". I apologized and now always reply in Korean.\n   - The `Avatar` component made the History list render blank, so I used `image()` instead.\n   - `AvatarImage.new` failed the type check (TS2339); it's a constructor. This became moot once I dropped the component.\n   - Avatar exports come from \"gpui-base\", not \"gpui-kit\" (TS2305).\n   - `URL` is undefined in the type environment (TS2552). I replaced it with a regex for the host.\n   - The old `REMOTES_ARGS` test failed after the regex change. I updated the test.\n   - A Bash call with `rm -rf ~/...` was blocked by the PreToolUse hook. I used an absolute path with `rm -f` and `rmdir`.\n   - The graph didn't reload after the config changed, because the reload key lacked the remote config. Fixed in `refreshHistory`.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Confirmed by screenshots on herdr-gitdeck: with `gitdeck.avatars true`, pictures were saved and shown. The folder `.avatars/` got 3 files: 2 png and 1 jpg.\n   - Setting it to false showed initials again right away. The setting was then set back to true (`git config --local gitdeck.avatars true` in herdr-gitdeck).\n   - Final `pnpm verify` passed: exit 0, 428 tests pass, 0 fail. Coverage is 99.65% overall; `src/core/avatars.ts` is at 98.94%, with lines 123-124 uncovered.\n   - `herdr-app status` shows `errors: []`.\n   - Not tested: the GitLab picture path on the company server, and a commit that isn't on GitHub.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"[Image #5] 이름하고 날짜하고 간격이 너무 넓음거 같은대 적당히 줄여줘\"\n   - \"한글로 말하라고..\"\n   - \"[Image #6] 이게 gitlab 아이콘이야?\"\n   - The answer to the question \"설정만 안내\" (just tell me the setting).\n   - \"[Image #7] 여기 어딘가에 git config gitdeck.forge 설정이 없으면 github or gitlab? 뭐 이런식으로 선택하라고 뜬다고 하지 않았나?\"\n   - \"gh glab 어느쪽인지 판별을 한다면 판별후에 git config gitdeck.forge 을 지정해주면 좋을것 같은데\"\n   - \"[Image #8] 이거 업데이트됬으면 여기서는 gitlab 아이콘이 나와야 하는거 아니야?\"\n   - \"유저 사진 보여주는거 코스트가 많이 들까?\"\n   - \"모드 폴더에 파일 저장되는지 먼저 시험해봐\"\n   - \"그럼 유저 사진 보여주는 거 구현해줘\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Give the user a completion report in Korean, MoAI-Easy style:\n     - What was built.\n     - How to turn it on: `git config gitdeck.avatars true` for one repo, or `--global` for all.\n     - Evidence: verify output and screenshots.\n     - Gaps: GitLab not tested on the company server, Avatar component avoided, `main.ts` is over 800 lines.\n   - Nothing is committed. All changes are uncommitted:\n     - The spacing change.\n     - Saving the detected forge.\n     - The history reload key.\n     - The whole avatar feature.\n   - Commit rules: ask with AskUserQuestion before committing or pushing; stage explicit paths only; never commit `.claudeignore` or `.worktreeinclude`; no MoAI trailer.\n   - The setting `gitdeck.avatars true` is now on in the herdr-gitdeck repo's local config. Mention this to the user.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished implementing and verifying \"그럼 유저 사진 보여주는 거 구현해줘\". The last actions:\n   - Turned the setting off (`git config --local gitdeck.avatars false`), took screenshot ca2, then turned it back on.\n   - Screenshot ca2 confirmed initials (\"AI\" badges) when the setting is off.\n   - The earlier screenshot ca1 confirmed real profile pictures beside \"Allan Im\" rows when it is on.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Report the finished avatar feature to the user in Korean. Cover:\n   - Files changed.\n   - How it works: opt-in, GitHub via one GraphQL call per 50 commits, GitLab via `/avatar` once per email, no Gravatar, a hashed filename in the hidden `.avatars` folder, initials until the picture is saved.\n   - How to enable or disable it.\n   - Evidence: verify passes with 428 tests and 99.65% coverage; screenshots in both on and off states.\n   - Not verified: the company GitLab server path, and how it behaves for `bsp-display-service`.\n   - That nothing is committed.\n   Do not start a commit without asking.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/allan/.claude/projects/-Volumes-WorkSpace-vogle-herdr-gitdeck/c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"6032a928-df06-4b6f-af17-ad68c61d1ffc","timestamp":"2026-11-19T02:59:47.247Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":143,"turnIndex":145},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
{"parentUuid":"6032a928-df06-4b6f-af17-ad68c61d1ffc","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/avatars.ts","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/avatars.ts","content":"// Authors' pictures for the history graph (on with `git config gitdeck.avatars true`).\n// The pictures live in a hidden folder of the mod, where Herdr can draw them and\n// saving one reloads nothing. A path is handed to the graph only once its file\n// is whole: Herdr remembers a path it once found missing.\n\nimport type { AsyncContext } from \"gpui-kit\";\nimport { readdir } from \"fs/promises\";\nimport { exec, home } from \"herdr\";\nimport { avatarBase, downloadAvatar, findAvatarUrls, knownAvatars, type AvatarWanted } from \"./core/avatars.ts\";\nimport { readAvatarSource } from \"./core/forge/index.ts\";\nimport type { Commit } from \"./core/git/log.ts\";\nimport type { Git, Target } from \"./core/git/runner.ts\";\n\n/** Where the pictures are, as `image()` takes it (from Herdr's own folder). */\nconst SHOWN_DIR = \"mods/gitdeck/.avatars\";\n/** At most this many new authors are looked up per history read. */\nconst MAX_NEW = 60;\n\nexport class Avatars {\n  /** base name (a hash of the email) → saved file. */\n  private files: Readonly<Record<string, string>> = {};\n  /** Authors already looked up this session, found or not: not asked again. */\n  private asked: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set();\n  private listed = false;\n  private busy = false;\n\n  /** The picture to draw for an email, once it is saved; null keeps the initials. */\n  path(email: string): string | null {\n    const file = this.files[avatarBase(email)];\n    return file ? `${SHOWN_DIR}/${file}` : null;\n  }\n\n  private dir(): string {\n    return `${home()}/.config/herdr-app/${SHOWN_DIR}`;\n  }\n\n  /** The pictures saved by earlier sessions. */\n  private async list(): Promise<void> {\n    if (this.listed) return;\n    this.listed = true;\n    await exec(\"mkdir\", [\"-p\", this.dir()]).catch(() => null);\n    const names = await readdir(this.dir()).catch(() => [] as string[]);\n    this.files = knownAvatars(names);\n  }\n\n  /** One commit per author not yet saved or asked about. */\n  private wanted(commits: readonly Commit[]): AvatarWanted[] {\n    const seen = new Set<string>();\n    const out: AvatarWanted[] = [];\n    for (const c of commits) {\n      const base = avatarBase(c.email);\n      if (c.email === \"\" || seen.has(base) || this.files[base] || this.asked.has(base)) continue;\n      seen.add(base);\n      out.push({ email: c.email, hash: c.hash });\n      if (out.length >= MAX_NEW) break;\n    }\n    return out;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Looks up and saves the pictures of the authors in `commits`, redrawing as\n   * each one lands. One run at a time; `away` is where the forge CLI runs.\n   */\n  async load(git: Git, target: Target, away: string, commits: readonly Commit[], cx: AsyncContext): Promise<void> {\n    if (this.busy) return;\n    this.busy = true;\n    try {\n      await this.list();\n      const before = Object.keys(this.files).length;\n      const wanted = this.wanted(commits);\n      if (Object.keys(this.files).length !== before || wanted.length === 0) cx.notify();\n      if (wanted.length === 0) return;\n      this.asked = new Set([...this.asked, ...wanted.map((w) => avatarBase(w.email))]);\n      const source = await readAvatarSource(git, target);\n      if (source === null) return;\n      const urls = await findAvatarUrls(exec, target, away, source, wanted);\n      for (const [email, url] of Object.entries(urls)) {\n        const base = avatarBase(email);\n        const file = await downloadAvatar(exec, this.dir(), url, base);\n        if (file === null) continue;\n        this.files = { ...this.files, [base]: file };\n        cx.notify();\n      }\n    } finally {\n      this.busy = false;\n    }\n  }\n}\n","numLines":89,"startLine":1,"totalLines":89}},"displayPath":"src/avatars.ts","savedCopyFraming":{"enveloped":false}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"429464c3-da53-422e-a8be-ba65836997b9","timestamp":"2026-11-19T02:59:48.101Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/avatars.ts\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t// Authors' pictures for the history graph (on with `git config gitdeck.avatars true`).\n2\t// The pictures live in a hidden folder of the mod, where Herdr can draw them and\n3\t// saving one reloads nothing. A path is handed to the graph only once its file\n4\t// is whole: Herdr remembers a path it once found missing.\n5\t\n6\timport type { AsyncContext } from \"gpui-kit\";\n7\timport { readdir } from \"fs/promises\";\n8\timport { exec, home } from \"herdr\";\n9\timport { avatarBase, downloadAvatar, findAvatarUrls, knownAvatars, type AvatarWanted } from \"./core/avatars.ts\";\n10\timport { readAvatarSource } from \"./core/forge/index.ts\";\n11\timport type { Commit } from \"./core/git/log.ts\";\n12\timport type { Git, Target } from \"./core/git/runner.ts\";\n13\t\n14\t/** Where the pictures are, as `image()` takes it (from Herdr's own folder). */\n15\tconst SHOWN_DIR = \"mods/gitdeck/.avatars\";\n16\t/** At most this many new authors are looked up per history read. */\n17\tconst MAX_NEW = 60;\n18\t\n19\texport class Avatars {\n20\t  /** base name (a hash of the email) → saved file. */\n21\t  private files: Readonly<Record<string, string>> = {};\n22\t  /** Authors already looked up this session, found or not: not asked again. */\n23\t  private asked: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set();\n24\t  private listed = false;\n25\t  private busy = false;\n26\t\n27\t  /** The picture to draw for an email, once it is saved; null keeps the initials. */\n28\t  path(email: string): string | null {\n29\t    const file = this.files[avatarBase(email)];\n30\t    return file ? `${SHOWN_DIR}/${file}` : null;\n31\t  }\n32\t\n33\t  private dir(): string {\n34\t    return `${home()}/.config/herdr-app/${SHOWN_DIR}`;\n35\t  }\n36\t\n37\t  /** The pictures saved by earlier sessions. */\n38\t  private async list(): Promise<void> {\n39\t    if (this.listed) return;\n40\t    this.listed = true;\n41\t    await exec(\"mkdir\", [\"-p\", this.dir()]).catch(() => null);\n42\t    const names = await readdir(this.dir()).catch(() => [] as string[]);\n43\t    this.files = knownAvatars(names);\n44\t  }\n45\t\n46\t  /** One commit per author not yet saved or asked about. */\n47\t  private wanted(commits: readonly Commit[]): AvatarWanted[] {\n48\t    const seen = new Set<string>();\n49\t    const out: AvatarWanted[] = [];\n50\t    for (const c of commits) {\n51\t      const base = avatarBase(c.email);\n52\t      if (c.email === \"\" || seen.has(base) || this.files[base] || this.asked.has(base)) continue;\n53\t      seen.add(base);\n54\t      out.push({ email: c.email, hash: c.hash });\n55\t      if (out.length >= MAX_NEW) break;\n56\t    }\n57\t    return out;\n58\t  }\n59\t\n60\t  /**\n61\t   * Looks up and saves the pictures of the authors in `commits`, redrawing as\n62\t   * each one lands. One run at a time; `away` is where the forge CLI runs.\n63\t   */\n64\t  async load(git: Git, target: Target, away: string, commits: readonly Commit[], cx: AsyncContext): Promise<void> {\n65\t    if (this.busy) return;\n66\t    this.busy = true;\n67\t    try {\n68\t      await this.list();\n69\t      const before = Object.keys(this.files).length;\n70\t      const wanted = this.wanted(commits);\n71\t      if (Object.keys(this.files).length !== before || wanted.length === 0) cx.notify();\n72\t      if (wanted.length === 0) return;\n73\t      this.asked = new Set([...this.asked, ...wanted.map((w) => avatarBase(w.email))]);\n74\t      const source = await readAvatarSource(git, target);\n75\t      if (source === null) return;\n76\t      const urls = await findAvatarUrls(exec, target, away, source, wanted);\n77\t      for (const [email, url] of Object.entries(urls)) {\n78\t        const base = avatarBase(email);\n79\t        const file = await downloadAvatar(exec, this.dir(), url, base);\n80\t        if (file === null) continue;\n81\t        this.files = { ...this.files, [base]: file };\n82\t        cx.notify();\n83\t      }\n84\t    } finally {\n85\t      this.busy = false;\n86\t    }\n87\t  }\n88\t}\n89\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
{"parentUuid":"429464c3-da53-422e-a8be-ba65836997b9","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/core/forge/index.ts","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/core/forge/index.ts","content":"// The repo's forge (GitHub or GitLab), read through its CLI. The CLI is pointed\n// at the project and run outside the repo, so it never reads the work tree or\n// the repo's config.\n\nimport type { AvatarSource } from \"../avatars.ts\";\nimport type { Exec, Git, Target } from \"../git/runner.ts\";\nimport { parseBranchPr, parsePrs, prListArgs, prViewArgs } from \"./github.ts\";\nimport { failedJobsArgs, mrListArgs, mrViewArgs, parseBranchMr, parseFailedJobs, parseMrs, pipelineId } from \"./gitlab.ts\";\nimport { forgeOf, parseRemote } from \"./remote.ts\";\nimport { discussionsArgs, parseDiscussions, parseThreads, threadsArgs, type ReviewThread } from \"./reviewThreads.ts\";\nimport type { BranchPr, Forge, ForgeChoice, ForgeKind, PrList } from \"./types.ts\";\n\nexport type { BranchPr, Checks, Forge, ForgeChoice, ForgeKind, PrList, PullRequest } from \"./types.ts\";\nexport type { ReviewThread } from \"./reviewThreads.ts\";\n\n/** Where to ask the CLIs which hosts they are signed in to: outside the repo. */\ninterface Probe {\n  exec: Exec;\n  away: string;\n}\n\n/**\n * The forge whose CLI alone is signed in to `host` (the person logged in there\n * themselves, so pointing that CLI at it is safe); null when neither or both are.\n * The token each prints is only checked for being there, never kept.\n */\nasync function signedInForge(probe: Probe, target: Target, host: string): Promise<ForgeKind | null> {\n  const has = (cli: string, args: string[]): Promise<boolean> =>\n    probe.exec(cli, args, { cwd: probe.away, on: target.on }).then(\n      (r) => r.code === 0 && r.stdout.trim() !== \"\",\n      () => false,\n    );\n  const [gitlab, github] = await Promise.all([\n    has(\"glab\", [\"config\", \"get\", \"token\", \"--host\", host]),\n    has(\"gh\", [\"auth\", \"token\", \"--hostname\", host]),\n  ]);\n  return gitlab === github ? null : gitlab ? \"gitlab\" : \"github\";\n}\n\n/**\n * origin's host, and its forge; `git config gitdeck.forge github|gitlab|none` names\n * it for any host. With a probe, an unnamed host is read from the signed-in CLIs.\n * The host comes back only while it's unnamed: the person is asked which it is.\n */\nasync function readOrigin(git: Git, target: Target, probe?: Probe): Promise<{ forge: Forge | null; host: string | null }> {\n  const [url, override] = await Promise.all([\n    git(target, [\"remote\", \"get-url\", \"origin\"]).catch(() => \"\"),\n    git(target, [\"config\", \"--get\", \"gitdeck.forge\"]).then((v) => v.trim(), () => null),\n  ]);\n  const remote = parseRemote(url);\n  const forge = forgeOf(remote, override);\n  if (forge !== null || remote === null || override !== null || !probe) return { forge, host: forge === null && override === null ? (remote?.host ?? null) : null };\n  const kind = await signedInForge(probe, target, remote.host);\n  // Kept as gitdeck.forge, so what reads only the config (the graph's icons) knows it too.\n  if (kind !== null) await setForge(git, target, kind).catch(() => undefined);\n  const found = kind === null ? null : forgeOf(remote, kind);\n  return { forge: found, host: found === null ? remote.host : null };\n}\n\n/** origin as the source of authors' pictures: its forge's kind, host and project; null when it isn't a known forge. */\nexport async function readAvatarSource(git: Git, target: Target): Promise<AvatarSource | null> {\n  const [url, override] = await Promise.all([\n    git(target, [\"remote\", \"get-url\", \"origin\"]).catch(() => \"\"),\n    git(target, [\"config\", \"--get\", \"gitdeck.forge\"]).then((v) => v.trim(), () => null),\n  ]);\n  const remote = parseRemote(url);\n  const forge = forgeOf(remote, override);\n  return forge && remote ? { kind: forge.kind, host: remote.host, path: remote.path } : null;\n}\n\nexport async function readForge(git: Git, target: Target): Promise<Forge | null> {\n  return (await readOrigin(git, target)).forge;\n}\n\n/** Names origin's forge for this repo (its own .git/config), for a host that isn't github.com or gitlab.com; \"none\" stops the asking. */\nexport async function setForge(git: Git, target: Target, kind: ForgeChoice): Promise<void> {\n  await git(target, [\"config\", \"--local\", \"gitdeck.forge\", kind]);\n}\n\nconst failure = (cli: string, error: unknown): string => `Can't run ${cli}: ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}`;\n\n/** `away` is a folder outside the repo (home) for the CLI to run in. */\nexport async function loadPrs(git: Git, exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string): Promise<PrList> {\n  const { forge, host } = await readOrigin(git, target, { exec, away });\n  if (forge === null) {\n    const error = host === null ? \"No GitHub or GitLab remote: origin isn't one\" : `origin is on ${host}: is it GitLab or GitHub?`;\n    return { items: [], error, repo: null, label: \"PR\", host };\n  }\n  const base = { repo: forge.repo, label: forge.label, host: null };\n  const args = forge.kind === \"github\" ? prListArgs(forge.repo) : mrListArgs(forge.repo);\n  try {\n    const r = await exec(forge.cli, args, { cwd: away, on: target.on });\n    if (r.code !== 0) return { ...base, items: [], error: r.stderr.split(\"\\n\")[0] || `${forge.cli} failed (${r.code})` };\n    return { ...base, items: forge.kind === \"github\" ? parsePrs(r.stdout) : parseMrs(r.stdout), error: null };\n  } catch (error) {\n    return { ...base, items: [], error: failure(forge.cli, error) };\n  }\n}\n\n/** A failed MR pipeline with its failed jobs in place of itself; as it was when they can't be read. */\nasync function withFailedJobs(exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string, repo: string, pr: BranchPr, pipeline: number | null): Promise<BranchPr> {\n  if (pr.checks.failed === 0 || pipeline === null) return pr;\n  try {\n    const r = await exec(\"glab\", failedJobsArgs(repo, pipeline), { cwd: away, on: target.on });\n    const jobs = r.code === 0 ? parseFailedJobs(r.stdout, repo) : [];\n    return jobs.length > 0 ? { ...pr, failed: jobs } : pr;\n  } catch {\n    return pr;\n  }\n}\n\n/** The CLIs' words for \"this branch has none\". */\nconst NONE = /no pull requests found|no (?:open )?merge requests? (?:available|found)/i;\n\nexport interface BranchPrState {\n  pr: BranchPr | null;\n  error: string | null;\n  label: \"PR\" | \"MR\";\n  /** origin's host when it isn't a known forge yet: the person names which it is. */\n  host: string | null;\n  /** The forge read, or null when origin isn't one (or isn't named yet). */\n  forge: ForgeKind | null;\n}\n\n/** The branch's PR or MR; none (and no error) without a forge or one to show. Without a branch, only the forge. */\nexport async function loadBranchPr(git: Git, exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string, branch: string | null): Promise<BranchPrState> {\n  const { forge, host: origin } = await readOrigin(git, target, { exec, away });\n  if (forge === null) return { pr: null, error: null, label: \"PR\", host: origin, forge: null };\n  const label = forge.label;\n  const host = null;\n  const known = { label, host, forge: forge.kind };\n  if (branch === null) return { pr: null, error: null, ...known };\n  const args = forge.kind === \"github\" ? prViewArgs(forge.repo, branch) : mrViewArgs(forge.repo, branch);\n  try {\n    const r = await exec(forge.cli, args, { cwd: away, on: target.on });\n    if (r.code === 0) {\n      const pr = forge.kind === \"github\" ? parseBranchPr(r.stdout, forge.repo) : parseBranchMr(r.stdout);\n      return { pr: pr && forge.kind === \"gitlab\" ? await withFailedJobs(exec, target, away, forge.repo, pr, pipelineId(r.stdout)) : pr, error: null, ...known };\n    }\n    if (NONE.test(r.stderr)) return { pr: null, error: null, ...known };\n    return { pr: null, error: r.stderr.split(\"\\n\")[0] || `${forge.cli} failed (${r.code})`, ...known };\n  } catch (error) {\n    return { pr: null, error: failure(forge.cli, error), ...known };\n  }\n}\n\n/** The open review threads on PR/MR `number`: read once, when the person asks for them. */\nexport async function loadReviewThreads(git: Git, exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string, number: number): Promise<{ threads: ReviewThread[]; error: string | null }> {\n  const { forge } = await readOrigin(git, target);\n  if (forge === null) return { threads: [], error: \"No GitHub or GitLab remote\" };\n  const args = forge.kind === \"github\" ? threadsArgs(forge.repo, number) : discussionsArgs(forge.repo, number);\n  try {\n    const r = await exec(forge.cli, args, { cwd: away, on: target.on });\n    if (r.code !== 0) return { threads: [], error: r.stderr.split(\"\\n\")[0] || `${forge.cli} failed (${r.code})` };\n    return { threads: forge.kind === \"github\" ? parseThreads(r.stdout) : parseDiscussions(r.stdout), error: null };\n  } catch (error) {\n    return { threads: [], error: failure(forge.cli, error) };\n  }\n}\n","numLines":160,"startLine":1,"totalLines":160}},"displayPath":"src/core/forge/index.ts","savedCopyFraming":{"enveloped":false}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c944126d-3a51-49c8-96b3-e6aa8aaf65a3","timestamp":"2026-11-19T02:59:48.101Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/core/forge/index.ts\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t// The repo's forge (GitHub or GitLab), read through its CLI. The CLI is pointed\n2\t// at the project and run outside the repo, so it never reads the work tree or\n3\t// the repo's config.\n4\t\n5\timport type { AvatarSource } from \"../avatars.ts\";\n6\timport type { Exec, Git, Target } from \"../git/runner.ts\";\n7\timport { parseBranchPr, parsePrs, prListArgs, prViewArgs } from \"./github.ts\";\n8\timport { failedJobsArgs, mrListArgs, mrViewArgs, parseBranchMr, parseFailedJobs, parseMrs, pipelineId } from \"./gitlab.ts\";\n9\timport { forgeOf, parseRemote } from \"./remote.ts\";\n10\timport { discussionsArgs, parseDiscussions, parseThreads, threadsArgs, type ReviewThread } from \"./reviewThreads.ts\";\n11\timport type { BranchPr, Forge, ForgeChoice, ForgeKind, PrList } from \"./types.ts\";\n12\t\n13\texport type { BranchPr, Checks, Forge, ForgeChoice, ForgeKind, PrList, PullRequest } from \"./types.ts\";\n14\texport type { ReviewThread } from \"./reviewThreads.ts\";\n15\t\n16\t/** Where to ask the CLIs which hosts they are signed in to: outside the repo. */\n17\tinterface Probe {\n18\t  exec: Exec;\n19\t  away: string;\n20\t}\n21\t\n22\t/**\n23\t * The forge whose CLI alone is signed in to `host` (the person logged in there\n24\t * themselves, so pointing that CLI at it is safe); null when neither or both are.\n25\t * The token each prints is only checked for being there, never kept.\n26\t */\n27\tasync function signedInForge(probe: Probe, target: Target, host: string): Promise<ForgeKind | null> {\n28\t  const has = (cli: string, args: string[]): Promise<boolean> =>\n29\t    probe.exec(cli, args, { cwd: probe.away, on: target.on }).then(\n30\t      (r) => r.code === 0 && r.stdout.trim() !== \"\",\n31\t      () => false,\n32\t    );\n33\t  const [gitlab, github] = await Promise.all([\n34\t    has(\"glab\", [\"config\", \"get\", \"token\", \"--host\", host]),\n35\t    has(\"gh\", [\"auth\", \"token\", \"--hostname\", host]),\n36\t  ]);\n37\t  return gitlab === github ? null : gitlab ? \"gitlab\" : \"github\";\n38\t}\n39\t\n40\t/**\n41\t * origin's host, and its forge; `git config gitdeck.forge github|gitlab|none` names\n42\t * it for any host. With a probe, an unnamed host is read from the signed-in CLIs.\n43\t * The host comes back only while it's unnamed: the person is asked which it is.\n44\t */\n45\tasync function readOrigin(git: Git, target: Target, probe?: Probe): Promise<{ forge: Forge | null; host: string | null }> {\n46\t  const [url, override] = await Promise.all([\n47\t    git(target, [\"remote\", \"get-url\", \"origin\"]).catch(() => \"\"),\n48\t    git(target, [\"config\", \"--get\", \"gitdeck.forge\"]).then((v) => v.trim(), () => null),\n49\t  ]);\n50\t  const remote = parseRemote(url);\n51\t  const forge = forgeOf(remote, override);\n52\t  if (forge !== null || remote === null || override !== null || !probe) return { forge, host: forge === null && override === null ? (remote?.host ?? null) : null };\n53\t  const kind = await signedInForge(probe, target, remote.host);\n54\t  // Kept as gitdeck.forge, so what reads only the config (the graph's icons) knows it too.\n55\t  if (kind !== null) await setForge(git, target, kind).catch(() => undefined);\n56\t  const found = kind === null ? null : forgeOf(remote, kind);\n57\t  return { forge: found, host: found === null ? remote.host : null };\n58\t}\n59\t\n60\t/** origin as the source of authors' pictures: its forge's kind, host and project; null when it isn't a known forge. */\n61\texport async function readAvatarSource(git: Git, target: Target): Promise<AvatarSource | null> {\n62\t  const [url, override] = await Promise.all([\n63\t    git(target, [\"remote\", \"get-url\", \"origin\"]).catch(() => \"\"),\n64\t    git(target, [\"config\", \"--get\", \"gitdeck.forge\"]).then((v) => v.trim(), () => null),\n65\t  ]);\n66\t  const remote = parseRemote(url);\n67\t  const forge = forgeOf(remote, override);\n68\t  return forge && remote ? { kind: forge.kind, host: remote.host, path: remote.path } : null;\n69\t}\n70\t\n71\texport async function readForge(git: Git, target: Target): Promise<Forge | null> {\n72\t  return (await readOrigin(git, target)).forge;\n73\t}\n74\t\n75\t/** Names origin's forge for this repo (its own .git/config), for a host that isn't github.com or gitlab.com; \"none\" stops the asking. */\n76\texport async function setForge(git: Git, target: Target, kind: ForgeChoice): Promise<void> {\n77\t  await git(target, [\"config\", \"--local\", \"gitdeck.forge\", kind]);\n78\t}\n79\t\n80\tconst failure = (cli: string, error: unknown): string => `Can't run ${cli}: ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}`;\n81\t\n82\t/** `away` is a folder outside the repo (home) for the CLI to run in. */\n83\texport async function loadPrs(git: Git, exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string): Promise<PrList> {\n84\t  const { forge, host } = await readOrigin(git, target, { exec, away });\n85\t  if (forge === null) {\n86\t    const error = host === null ? \"No GitHub or GitLab remote: origin isn't one\" : `origin is on ${host}: is it GitLab or GitHub?`;\n87\t    return { items: [], error, repo: null, label: \"PR\", host };\n88\t  }\n89\t  const base = { repo: forge.repo, label: forge.label, host: null };\n90\t  const args = forge.kind === \"github\" ? prListArgs(forge.repo) : mrListArgs(forge.repo);\n91\t  try {\n92\t    const r = await exec(forge.cli, args, { cwd: away, on: target.on });\n93\t    if (r.code !== 0) return { ...base, items: [], error: r.stderr.split(\"\\n\")[0] || `${forge.cli} failed (${r.code})` };\n94\t    return { ...base, items: forge.kind === \"github\" ? parsePrs(r.stdout) : parseMrs(r.stdout), error: null };\n95\t  } catch (error) {\n96\t    return { ...base, items: [], error: failure(forge.cli, error) };\n97\t  }\n98\t}\n99\t\n100\t/** A failed MR pipeline with its failed jobs in place of itself; as it was when they can't be read. */\n101\tasync function withFailedJobs(exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string, repo: string, pr: BranchPr, pipeline: number | null): Promise<BranchPr> {\n102\t  if (pr.checks.failed === 0 || pipeline === null) return pr;\n103\t  try {\n104\t    const r = await exec(\"glab\", failedJobsArgs(repo, pipeline), { cwd: away, on: target.on });\n105\t    const jobs = r.code === 0 ? parseFailedJobs(r.stdout, repo) : [];\n106\t    return jobs.length > 0 ? { ...pr, failed: jobs } : pr;\n107\t  } catch {\n108\t    return pr;\n109\t  }\n110\t}\n111\t\n112\t/** The CLIs' words for \"this branch has none\". */\n113\tconst NONE = /no pull requests found|no (?:open )?merge requests? (?:available|found)/i;\n114\t\n115\texport interface BranchPrState {\n116\t  pr: BranchPr | null;\n117\t  error: string | null;\n118\t  label: \"PR\" | \"MR\";\n119\t  /** origin's host when it isn't a known forge yet: the person names which it is. */\n120\t  host: string | null;\n121\t  /** The forge read, or null when origin isn't one (or isn't named yet). */\n122\t  forge: ForgeKind | null;\n123\t}\n124\t\n125\t/** The branch's PR or MR; none (and no error) without a forge or one to show. Without a branch, only the forge. */\n126\texport async function loadBranchPr(git: Git, exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string, branch: string | null): Promise<BranchPrState> {\n127\t  const { forge, host: origin } = await readOrigin(git, target, { exec, away });\n128\t  if (forge === null) return { pr: null, error: null, label: \"PR\", host: origin, forge: null };\n129\t  const label = forge.label;\n130\t  const host = null;\n131\t  const known = { label, host, forge: forge.kind };\n132\t  if (branch === null) return { pr: null, error: null, ...known };\n133\t  const args = forge.kind === \"github\" ? prViewArgs(forge.repo, branch) : mrViewArgs(forge.repo, branch);\n134\t  try {\n135\t    const r = await exec(forge.cli, args, { cwd: away, on: target.on });\n136\t    if (r.code === 0) {\n137\t      const pr = forge.kind === \"github\" ? parseBranchPr(r.stdout, forge.repo) : parseBranchMr(r.stdout);\n138\t      return { pr: pr && forge.kind === \"gitlab\" ? await withFailedJobs(exec, target, away, forge.repo, pr, pipelineId(r.stdout)) : pr, error: null, ...known };\n139\t    }\n140\t    if (NONE.test(r.stderr)) return { pr: null, error: null, ...known };\n141\t    return { pr: null, error: r.stderr.split(\"\\n\")[0] || `${forge.cli} failed (${r.code})`, ...known };\n142\t  } catch (error) {\n143\t    return { pr: null, error: failure(forge.cli, error), ...known };\n144\t  }\n145\t}\n146\t\n147\t/** The open review threads on PR/MR `number`: read once, when the person asks for them. */\n148\texport async function loadReviewThreads(git: Git, exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string, number: number): Promise<{ threads: ReviewThread[]; error: string | null }> {\n149\t  const { forge } = await readOrigin(git, target);\n150\t  if (forge === null) return { threads: [], error: \"No GitHub or GitLab remote\" };\n151\t  const args = forge.kind === \"github\" ? threadsArgs(forge.repo, number) : discussionsArgs(forge.repo, number);\n152\t  try {\n153\t    const r = await exec(forge.cli, args, { cwd: away, on: target.on });\n154\t    if (r.code !== 0) return { threads: [], error: r.stderr.split(\"\\n\")[0] || `${forge.cli} failed (${r.code})` };\n155\t    return { threads: forge.kind === \"github\" ? parseThreads(r.stdout) : parseDiscussions(r.stdout), error: null };\n156\t  } catch (error) {\n157\t    return { threads: [], error: failure(forge.cli, error) };\n158\t  }\n159\t}\n160\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
{"parentUuid":"c944126d-3a51-49c8-96b3-e6aa8aaf65a3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/core/avatars.ts","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/core/avatars.ts","content":"// Authors' pictures for the history graph, from the repo's own forge only (no\n// Gravatar). GitHub is asked through `gh` which commit authors are which users,\n// a GitLab server through `glab` for each email's avatar; both already hold the\n// pushed commits. Each picture is saved once, under a hash of the email, in a\n// hidden folder Herdr doesn't watch; the graph draws a file only once it is\n// whole, since Herdr remembers a path it found missing.\n\nimport type { Exec, Target } from \"./git/runner.ts\";\n\nexport interface AvatarSource {\n  kind: \"github\" | \"gitlab\";\n  host: string;\n  /** owner/name (GitHub), group/project (GitLab). */\n  path: string;\n}\n\n/** A commit by the author, to ask GitHub about. */\nexport interface AvatarWanted {\n  email: string;\n  hash: string;\n}\n\n/** Whether `git config gitdeck.avatars` (repo or global) turns pictures on, from the graph's config read; off unless set. */\nexport function avatarsOn(configOut: string): boolean {\n  const line = configOut.split(\"\\n\").find((l) => l.startsWith(\"gitdeck.avatars \"));\n  return /^(true|yes|on|1)$/i.test(line?.slice(\"gitdeck.avatars \".length).trim() ?? \"\");\n}\n\nconst SIZE = 64;\nconst BATCH = 50;\nconst IMAGE_TYPES: Readonly<Record<string, string>> = { \"image/png\": \"png\", \"image/jpeg\": \"jpg\", \"image/gif\": \"gif\", \"image/webp\": \"webp\" };\n\nconst normal = (email: string): string => email.trim().toLowerCase();\n\nfunction fnv1a(text: string, seed: number): string {\n  let h = seed >>> 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i += 1) {\n    h ^= text.charCodeAt(i);\n    h = Math.imul(h, 0x01000193) >>> 0;\n  }\n  return h.toString(16).padStart(8, \"0\");\n}\n\n/** The file name (without extension) an email's picture is saved under: a hash, so no email is on disk. */\nexport function avatarBase(email: string): string {\n  const e = normal(email);\n  return fnv1a(e, 0x811c9dc5) + fnv1a(e, 0x050c5d1f);\n}\n\n/** `123+name@users.noreply.github.com` names account 123: its picture is known without asking. */\nexport function noreplyAvatar(email: string): string | null {\n  const m = /^(\\d+)\\+[^@]+@users\\.noreply\\.github\\.com$/.exec(normal(email));\n  return m ? `https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/${m[1]}?s=${SIZE}` : null;\n}\n\n/** The saved pictures (a folder listing) as base name → file; half-written `.tmp` files are not pictures. */\nexport function knownAvatars(names: readonly string[]): Readonly<Record<string, string>> {\n  const exts = new Set(Object.values(IMAGE_TYPES));\n  const entries = names.flatMap((n): Array<[string, string]> => {\n    const m = /^([0-9a-f]{16})\\.([a-z]+)$/.exec(n);\n    return m?.[1] && m[2] && exts.has(m[2]) ? [[m[1], n]] : [];\n  });\n  return Object.fromEntries(entries);\n}\n\nconst SAFE_NAME = /^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$/;\nconst OID = /^[0-9a-f]{4,64}$/;\n\n/** One GraphQL query asking for several commits' authors, each under an alias. */\nexport function githubQuery(owner: string, name: string, hashes: readonly string[]): string {\n  if (!SAFE_NAME.test(owner) || !SAFE_NAME.test(name)) throw new Error(`not a GitHub repo name: ${owner}/${name}`);\n  const parts = hashes.map((h, i) => {\n    if (!OID.test(h)) throw new Error(`not a commit hash: ${h}`);\n    return `c${i}: object(oid: \"${h}\") { ... on Commit { author { email user { avatarUrl(size: ${SIZE}) } } } }`;\n  });\n  return `query { repository(owner: \"${owner}\", name: \"${name}\") { ${parts.join(\" \")} } }`;\n}\n\ninterface GithubAnswer {\n  data?: { repository?: Record<string, { author?: { email?: string; user?: { avatarUrl?: string } | null } } | null> };\n}\n\n/** email → picture for the commits GitHub knows a user for; unpushed commits come back null. */\nexport function parseGithubAvatars(stdout: string): Readonly<Record<string, string>> {\n  let answer: GithubAnswer;\n  try {\n    answer = JSON.parse(stdout) as GithubAnswer;\n  } catch {\n    return {};\n  }\n  const found = Object.values(answer.data?.repository ?? {}).flatMap((c): Array<[string, string]> => {\n    const email = c?.author?.email;\n    const url = c?.author?.user?.avatarUrl;\n    return email && url ? [[normal(email), url]] : [];\n  });\n  return Object.fromEntries(found);\n}\n\nconst GRAVATAR = /(^|\\.)gravatar\\.com$/i;\n\n/** GitLab's `/avatar` answer: the server's own picture; Gravatar's stands for no picture. */\nexport function parseGitlabAvatar(stdout: string): string | null {\n  try {\n    const url = (JSON.parse(stdout) as { avatar_url?: unknown }).avatar_url;\n    const host = typeof url === \"string\" ? /^https:\\/\\/([^/:?#]+)/.exec(url)?.[1] : undefined;\n    return host && !GRAVATAR.test(host) ? (url as string) : null;\n  } catch {\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n\nasync function githubUrls(exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string, source: AvatarSource, wanted: readonly AvatarWanted[]): Promise<Record<string, string>> {\n  const [owner = \"\", name = \"\"] = source.path.split(\"/\");\n  const found: Record<string, string> = {};\n  for (let i = 0; i < wanted.length; i += BATCH) {\n    const batch = wanted.slice(i, i + BATCH);\n    try {\n      const query = githubQuery(owner, name, batch.map((w) => w.hash));\n      const r = await exec(\"gh\", [\"api\", \"graphql\", \"--hostname\", source.host, \"-f\", `query=${query}`], { cwd: away, on: target.on });\n      // Some commits not on GitHub still answer the rest.\n      Object.assign(found, parseGithubAvatars(r.stdout));\n    } catch {\n      return found;\n    }\n  }\n  return found;\n}\n\nasync function gitlabUrls(exec: Exec, target: Target, away: string, source: AvatarSource, wanted: readonly AvatarWanted[]): Promise<Record<string, string>> {\n  const found: Record<string, string> = {};\n  for (const w of wanted) {\n    const args = [\"api\", `avatar?email=${encodeURIComponent(normal(w.email))}&size=${SIZE}`, \"--hostname\", source.host];\n    const r = await exec(\"glab\", args, { cwd: away, on: target.on }).catch(() => null);\n    const url = r && r.code === 0 ? parseGitlabAvatar(r.stdout) : null;\n    if (url) found[normal(w.email)] = url;\n  }\n  return found;\n}\n\n/**\n * email → picture URL for the authors the forge knows; the rest are left out\n * (the graph keeps their initials). The CLIs run outside the repo, in `away`.\n */\nexport async function findAvatarUrls(\n  exec: Exec,\n  target: Target,\n  away: string,\n  source: AvatarSource,\n  wanted: readonly AvatarWanted[],\n): Promise<Readonly<Record<string, string>>> {\n  const known: Record<string, string> = {};\n  const ask: AvatarWanted[] = [];\n  for (const w of wanted) {\n    const url = source.kind === \"github\" ? noreplyAvatar(w.email) : null;\n    if (url) known[w.email] = url;\n    else ask.push(w);\n  }\n  if (ask.length === 0) return known;\n  const asked = source.kind === \"github\" ? await githubUrls(exec, target, away, source, ask) : await gitlabUrls(exec, target, away, source, ask);\n  for (const w of ask) {\n    const url = asked[normal(w.email)];\n    if (url) known[w.email] = url;\n  }\n  return known;\n}\n\n/**\n * Saves the picture at `url` as `<dir>/<base>.<ext>` and returns that file name;\n * null when it isn't an image (a sign-in page, an error). It is written to a\n * `.tmp` first and renamed, so the graph never finds half a file.\n */\nexport async function downloadAvatar(exec: Exec, dir: string, url: string, base: string): Promise<string | null> {\n  if (!url.startsWith(\"https://\")) return null;\n  const tmp = `${dir}/${base}.tmp`;\n  try {\n    const r = await exec(\"curl\", [\"-fsSL\", \"--proto\", \"=https\", \"--proto-redir\", \"=https\", \"--max-time\", \"15\", \"--max-filesize\", \"2000000\", \"-o\", tmp, \"-w\", \"%{content_type}\", \"--\", url], {});\n    const ext = r.code === 0 ? IMAGE_TYPES[r.stdout.split(\";\")[0]?.trim().toLowerCase() ?? \"\"] : undefined;\n    if (!ext) {\n      await exec(\"rm\", [\"-f\", tmp], {});\n      return null;\n    }\n    const file = `${base}.${ext}`;\n    const moved = await exec(\"mv\", [\"-f\", tmp, `${dir}/${file}`], {});\n    return moved.code === 0 ? file : null;\n  } catch {\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n","numLines":189,"startLine":1,"totalLines":189}},"displayPath":"src/core/avatars.ts","savedCopyFraming":{"enveloped":false}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"87822313-dc2e-4ff7-8e0c-0fbd60c70540","timestamp":"2026-11-19T02:59:48.102Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/core/avatars.ts\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t// Authors' pictures for the history graph, from the repo's own forge only (no\n2\t// Gravatar). GitHub is asked through `gh` which commit authors are which users,\n3\t// a GitLab server through `glab` for each email's avatar; both already hold the\n4\t// pushed commits. Each picture is saved once, under a hash of the email, in a\n5\t// hidden folder Herdr doesn't watch; the graph draws a file only once it is\n6\t// whole, since Herdr remembers a path it found missing.\n7\t\n8\timport type { Exec, Target } from \"./git/runner.ts\";\n9\t\n10\texport interface AvatarSource {\n11\t  kind: \"github\" | \"gitlab\";\n12\t  host: string;\n13\t  /** owner/name (GitHub), group/project (GitLab). */\n14\t  path: string;\n15\t}\n16\t\n17\t/** A commit by the author, to ask GitHub about. */\n18\texport interface AvatarWanted {\n19\t  email: string;\n20\t  hash: string;\n21\t}\n22\t\n23\t/** Whether `git config gitdeck.avatars` (repo or global) turns pictures on, from the graph's config read; off unless set. */\n24\texport function avatarsOn(configOut: string): boolean {\n25\t  const line =