{"parentUuid":"a2b68397-f30d-4619-8a48-d1bdcaa0f891","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f8bb2b8b-aff1-44bc-ae11-7238d3e2fb33","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EQgtKX9zUtCPa282BaaiwZ","type":"tool_result","content":"herdr-app: the Herdr desktop app. With no arguments it opens the window.\n\nUsage:\n  herdr-app                        open the window\n  herdr-app ls                     spaces, their tabs and terminals, in the open window\n  herdr-app do <command> [args]    run a command: --name api --argv '[\"pi\"]', or one JSON object\n  herdr-app feedback <text>        draft feedback for the person to review and send\n  herdr-app commands               every command, its arguments, what it does\n  herdr-app status                 what the window shows, and any errors\n  herdr-app shot [file.png]        save the current window frame (default: herdr-shot.png)\n  herdr-app check <mod folder>     load a mod once and report what's wrong\n  herdr-app --skill                Agent Skill: driving the window, and where hc fits\n  herdr-app --version\n\nThe terminals run in herdr-core (`hc`), which keeps them alive when the\nwindow closes. `hc --help`: start, read, wait on and talk to terminals and\nagents. The app shows them and arranges them in spaces and tabs.\n\nHome: ~/.config/herdr-app (HERDR_APP_HOME picks another).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c1c54073-3764-4611-a6ee-f6c5efb0e7f8","timestamp":"2026-11-19T03:06:27.497Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"herdr-app: the Herdr desktop app. With no arguments it opens the window.\n\nUsage:\n  herdr-app                        open the window\n  herdr-app ls                     spaces, their tabs and terminals, in the open window\n  herdr-app do <command> [args]    run a command: --name api --argv '[\"pi\"]', or one JSON object\n  herdr-app feedback <text>        draft feedback for the person to review and send\n  herdr-app commands               every command, its arguments, what it does\n  herdr-app status                 what the window shows, and any errors\n  herdr-app shot [file.png]        save the current window frame (default: herdr-shot.png)\n  herdr-app check <mod folder>     load a mod once and report what's wrong\n  herdr-app --skill                Agent Skill: driving the window, and where hc fits\n  herdr-app --version\n\nThe terminals run in herdr-core (`hc`), which keeps them alive when the\nwindow closes. `hc --help`: start, read, wait on and talk to terminals and\nagents. The app shows them and arranges them in spaces and tabs.\n\nHome: ~/.config/herdr-app (HERDR_APP_HOME picks another).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a2b68397-f30d-4619-8a48-d1bdcaa0f891","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"hook","reasonType":"hook"},"session_id":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
