{"parentUuid":"60dc8ea7-3966-4bc2-8f85-b1bce83065ba","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"50fe025f-7260-472e-aa9f-9655f28ff164","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SCsN2jpNibFMjxoxUGLLx2","type":"tool_result","content":"gpui-kit.d.ts  herdr.d.ts\n1140:     * How far a `resizable_panel()` may be dragged, in pixels.\n1149:     * `handler(sizes, cx)` on an `h_resizable()` or `v_resizable()`, once a drag\n21036:   * A row of panes with draggable dividers between them. `v_resizable` is the\n21040:   * Children are `resizable_panel()` calls. Anything else is wrapped in a panel\n21046:   * the Rust does, so give it a height (for `h_resizable`) or a width. Styles\n21055:   * h_resizable(\"workspace\").h(400)\n21056:   *   .child(resizable_panel().size(220).size_range(160, 320).child(sidebar))\n21057:   *   .child(resizable_panel().child(editor));\n21060:  export function h_resizable(id: string): NativeElement;\n21061:  /** A column of panes with draggable dividers. See `h_resizable`. */\n21062:  export function v_resizable(id: string): NativeElement;\n21064:   * One pane of an `h_resizable()` or `v_resizable()`, and only there: a panel\n21079:  export function resizable_panel(): NativeElement;\nShell cwd was reset to /Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8866f61b-4c4b-4342-8dab-8e83824c800d","timestamp":"2026-11-19T03:18:32.193Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"gpui-kit.d.ts  herdr.d.ts\n1140:     * How far a `resizable_panel()` may be dragged, in pixels.\n1149:     * `handler(sizes, cx)` on an `h_resizable()` or `v_resizable()`, once a drag\n21036:   * A row of panes with draggable dividers between them. `v_resizable` is the\n21040:   * Children are `resizable_panel()` calls. Anything else is wrapped in a panel\n21046:   * the Rust does, so give it a height (for `h_resizable`) or a width. Styles\n21055:   * h_resizable(\"workspace\").h(400)\n21056:   *   .child(resizable_panel().size(220).size_range(160, 320).child(