{"parentUuid":"2c688872-065e-43f1-90d8-6274122282e1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9ad5ee23-cd34-4870-aff4-4673f76ae14b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Artifact, AskUserQuestion, Bash, Edit, Glob, Grep, ListAgents, Read, Skill, TaskCreate, TaskStop, TaskUpdate, ToolSearch, Write, mcp__firecrawl__firecrawl_search</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Always reply in Korean, in MoAI-Easy colloquial 해요체 style. The user once corrected me: \"한글로 말하라고..\".\n   - Commit rules:\n     - Ask with AskUserQuestion before any commit or push.\n     - Stage explicit paths only.\n     - Never commit `.claudeignore` or `.worktreeinclude`.\n     - No \"🗿 MoAI\" trailer.\n   - Done this session (all uncommitted):\n     - Fork-style commit detail view.\n     - Right-click context menu for commit actions; the button bar is removed.\n     - History tab shows the commit detail in a resizable bottom pane under the list, so history and commit are visible together. This came from the user's request \"하단에 창이 열리는것처럼 하단에 나오고 크기를 조절할수 있게…위아래로 히스트로랑 커밋내용을 같이 볼수 있음 좋겠는대\".\n   - Latest request: \"파일트리는 트리로 나와야하지 않을까 그리고 여기마 파일 보여주는 디자인 포멧이 다른거 같기도 하고..\"\n     - The File Tree (from the detail pane's \"File Tree\" tab) should be a real folder tree, not a flat list.\n     - Its rows should look like the other file lists, especially the Changes tab.\n     - The screenshot showed a flat list with header \"Files at d3a055c42e (188)\", rows of icon + name + dim folder + size like \"458 B\", and a × close button.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Herdr mod in QuickJS: no Node APIs.\n   - UI toolkit: gpui-kit / gpui-base (`h_flex`, `v_flex`, `v_virtual_list`, `Scrollbar`, `v_resizable(id)`, `resizable_panel()`).\n     - `resizable_panel` supports `.size(px)`, `.size_range(min,max?)` and `on_resize`.\n     - Panel sizes are remembered by the window, keyed by the group id.\n     - The typed `visible()` takes no argument, so panels are added conditionally instead.\n   - Virtual list rows can't hold handlers. Use the list-level `on_item_click` and `on_item_secondary_click(key, e, cx)` instead.\n   - Pure logic goes in `src/core` with test-first development, immutable state and an 80% coverage gate.\n   - Verification loop:\n     1. `pnpm verify`.\n     2. `pnpm -s dev` to install.\n     3. `herdr-app status`.\n     4. `herdr-app do gitdeck.tab:history`.\n     5. Click the \"fix: blame a deleted…\" commit row with `orca computer click --app dev.herdr.app --x 1595 --y 287 --no-screenshot --json`.\n     6. Screenshot with `herdr-app shot <file>`.\n     7. Crop with `sips -c H W --cropOffset Y 2840`.\n     - Screenshot pixels are 2× the point coordinates.\n   - Right-click and drag need `--restore-window`. The user approved bringing the window to the front for checks.\n   - Scratchpad: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-WorkSpace-vogle-herdr-gitdeck/c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29/scratchpad\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **src/core/opsView.ts**\n     - `OpsView` drops `expanded` and gains:\n       - `menu: {hash; x: number|null; y: number|null} | null`\n       - `subject: string | null`\n     - New functions: `openMenu`, `placeMenu`, `closeMenu`, `chooseFromMenu`, and `fitMenu(x, y, pane{width,height}, width, height)`.\n     - `splitActions` and `toggleMore` were removed.\n   - **tests/opsView.test.ts**\n     - Replaced the More tests with 3 menu tests.\n   - **src/ops.ts**\n     - `OpsHost` gains `commit(hash)`.\n     - New private `subject()` returns the menu's commit, else the subject, else the selected commit.\n     - `parts()` returns `menu: {x, y, actions} | null` instead of `commit`.\n     - `commitAction` calls `chooseFromMenu`.\n     - Actions `openMenu`, `placeMenu(e)` and `closeMenu` were added. `placeMenu` uses `e.local_position`, `e.bounds` and `fitMenu` with `MENU_WIDTH`, `MENU_ITEM` and `MENU_PAD`.\n   - **src/ui/ops.ts**\n     - Exports `MENU_WIDTH = 200`, `MENU_ITEM = 24`, `MENU_PAD = 4`.\n     - `commitBar` now shows only the plan editor, the naming row for branch/tag, or the reset mode row. Otherwise it returns null.\n     - New `commitMenu` draws an absolute-positioned menu with `on_mouse_down_out` to close it.\n   - **src/ui/graph.ts**\n     - `graphList(..., menu?: OpenMenu)` adds `on_item_secondary_click`, skipping `MORE` and `UNCOMMITTED`.\n   - **src/ui/historyPane.ts**\n     - `wide` was removed from `HistoryParts`.\n     - New constants:\n       - `SPLIT = \"gitdeck-history-split\"`\n       - `DETAIL_PX = 340`\n     - `historyTab` body:\n       ```ts\n       const body = v_resizable(SPLIT).flex_1().min_h_0()\n         .child(resizable_panel().size_range(120).child(list.size_full()))\n         .when(open, (el) => el.child(resizable_panel().size(DETAIL_PX).size_range(120).child(v_flex().size_full().min_w_0().overflow_hidden().child(details(view, parts.status, p, actions, parts.avatar) ?? div()))));\n       ```\n     - The list holds a right-press `placeMenu` and the menu overlay.\n   - **src/ui/details.ts**\n     - The close button is `textButton(\"details-close\", \"Close\", p, actions.close)`.\n     - The tab row is: Commit (active), File Tree (`actions.browseTree`), a spacer, then Close.\n   - **src/main.ts**\n     - Gained `commitOf(hash)`.\n     - `selectedCommit` uses `commitOf`.\n     - `wide`, `on_size_change` and the `isWide` import were removed.\n     - `browseTree` (about line 710) calls `this.openInspect({ kind: \"tree\", rev: sel.hash, data: null, file: null, blob: null }, cx)`.\n     - `treeFile: (index, cx) => this.treeFile(index, cx)`.\n   - **src/core/panel.ts, tests/panel.test.ts**\n     - Removed `WIDE_PX`, `isWide` and their test.\n   - **Read only, for the latest task:**\n     - `src/ui/inspect.ts` (194 lines): `inspectPane(v, p, a)`.\n       - Tree rows come from `rowsOf`: flat items, a 14px icon with `p.muted`, the name, the dim folder path, and size as `${f.size} B`.\n       - Row height is `ROW = 18`, with `text_xs`.\n       - `on_item_click` on a tree row calls `a.openTreeFile(Number(key))`.\n       - The title is `Files at <rev10> (count)`.\n       - The header has a \"← Files\" button and a \"×\" close button.\n       - `InspectActions` has `jump`, `close`, `openTreeFile(index)`, `closeTreeFile` and `setForge`.\n     - `src/core/inspect.ts`: tree view type:\n       ```ts\n       { kind: \"tree\"; rev: string; data: Loaded<TreeFile> | null; file: TreeFile | null; blob: BlobView | null }\n       ```\n     - `src/core/tree.ts`: `TreeFile {path, size, kind: \"file\"|\"link\"|\"submodule\", hash}`, plus `treeArgs` and `parseTree`.\n     - `src/core/fileGroups.ts`:\n       - `folderTree<T extends {path}>(files, newFolders = [])` returns a `FolderNode<T>`: `{folder, label, folders, files, all, isNew}`.\n       - Lone-folder chains are joined into one row.\n       - Also `foldKey`, `isOpen` (default open unless new, flipped by a set), `setAll`, `allOpen` and `matching`.\n     - `src/ui/changeFiles.ts`: Changes tab row style.\n       - Rows: `h(24)`, `pl(indent(depth))` where `indent = 10 + depth*14`, `pr(10)`, `gap(6)`, hover background.\n       - File row: `kindIcon` (16px `FILE_ICONS[fileKind]`), the name truncated, and at depth 0 a dim folder label as `text_xs` `p.dim`.\n       - Folder row: `icon(open ? ICONS.folderOpen : ICONS.folder, p.dim, 16)` plus the label in `p.muted`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Orca right-click failed with `background_unavailable`. I asked the user, who approved, and I used `--restore-window`.\n   - `resizable_panel().visible(open)` was a type error (TS2554: expected 0 args). Fixed by adding the panel conditionally with `.when(open, ...)`.\n   - The detail pane overflowed horizontally: Close was hidden and the body text was cut off. Fixed by wrapping it in `v_flex().size_full().min_w_0().overflow_hidden()`.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Verified the right-click menu appears at the click point, flips upward near the bottom, and closes on an outside click.\n   - Verified the bottom split shows the list and detail together, and the divider drag resizes them. Final `pnpm verify` exit 0: 428/428 passed, 99.64% coverage, `errors: []`.\n   - Not verified:\n     - Menu actions were not actually clicked.\n     - Split size persistence across an app restart.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Earlier messages, before the previous compaction:\n     - Spacing.\n     - \"한글로 말하라고..\".\n     - GitLab icon.\n     - Forge config.\n     - Avatars.\n     - \"history 에서 커밋된걸 클릭하면…fork 처럼 UI를 바꿔줄래…위에 매뉴가 많은대 이거 다 필요할까? 9개나 되는대\".\n     - AskUserQuestion answer: \"오른쪽 클릭 메뉴로 (권장)\".\n   - AskUserQuestion answer: \"네, 창 가져와서 확인 (권장)\". This approved bringing the Herdr window to the front for the right-click check.\n   - \"이게 보이는것이 히스토리 창이 전체 다 바뀌잖아,, 그러헥 말고 하단에 창이 열리는것처럼 하단에 나오고 크기를 조절할수 있게 했으면 하는데 가능한가? 그래서 위아래로 히스트로랑 커밋내용을 같이 볼수 있음 좋겠는대\"\n   - \"[Image #11] 파일트리는 트리로 나와야하지 않을까 그리고 여기마 파일 보여주는 디자인 포멧이 다른거 같기도 하고..\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Make File Tree a real collapsible folder tree, styled like the Changes tab file rows. Reuse `folderTree` from `fileGroups.ts`, the `ICONS.folder` / `ICONS.folderOpen` icons, the 24px rows, the 16px kind icons and the depth indent.\n   - Verify, then report in Korean.\n   - Nothing committed yet. Ask before committing.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I was investigating how to turn the File Tree into a real tree.\n   - The tree is rendered by `inspectPane` in `src/ui/inspect.ts`.\n   - It is a flat `v_virtual_list` whose `on_item_click` key is the index into `v.data.items` (`openTreeFile(Number(key))`).\n   - The plan:\n     1. Add tree-fold state, a set of flipped or opened folders, to the inspect tree view (immutable) or to main.\n     2. Flatten `folderTree(items)` into visible rows. Folder rows toggle; file rows open the file by its original index. A core helper can do this and should be tested first.\n     3. Render the rows in Changes style: 24px height, indent `10+depth*14`, folder icons, 16px `FILE_ICONS` icons, the name, with size kept dim on the right.\n     4. Keep the virtual list, keyed with prefixes like `fd:<folder>` or `f:<index>`.\n     5. Possibly start folders folded at the root level for 188 files. Decide a sensible default; the Changes tab defaults to open.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Implement the tree for File Tree in response to \"파일트리는 트리로 나와야하지 않을까 그리고 여기마 파일 보여주는 디자인 포멧이 다른거 같기도 하고..\":\n   1. Write a failing test for a core function that flattens `folderTree(TreeFile[])` with an open set into rows `{kind: folder|file, depth, …}`.\n   2. Implement that function.\n   3. Add fold toggling to the inspect tree view state and actions.\n   4. Restyle the tree rows in `src/ui/inspect.ts` to match `changeFiles.ts`.\n   5. Run `pnpm verify` and `pnpm -s dev`, open a commit, click \"File Tree\", and screenshot it.\n   6. Report in Korean, without committing.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/allan/.claude/projects/-Volumes-WorkSpace-vogle-herdr-gitdeck/c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"4a6e7d2f-5f6f-4815-97b3-28dfd9c582e1","timestamp":"2026-11-19T03:37:32.059Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":146,"turnIndex":148},"turnOrigin":"human","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["2c4a3767-ac1b-4a82-8820-ae52763df258"],"session_id":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
{"parentUuid":"4a6e7d2f-5f6f-4815-97b3-28dfd9c582e1","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/inspect.ts","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/inspect.ts","content":"// The inspect pane: a file's blame or history, or the reflog. A click on a\n// row jumps to its commit in the graph.\n\nimport { div, type Context, type Element } from \"gpui-kit\";\nimport { h_flex, v_flex, v_virtual_list, Scrollbar } from \"gpui-base\";\nimport type { ForgeChoice } from \"../core/forge/index.ts\";\nimport type { InspectView } from \"../core/inspect.ts\";\nimport { MAX_STATS, type Stats } from \"../core/stats.ts\";\nimport { ago } from \"../core/time.ts\";\nimport { monoFont, textButton, type Palette } from \"./style.ts\";\n\nconst LIST = \"gitdeck-inspect\";\nconst ROW = 18;\n\nexport interface InspectActions {\n  jump: (hash: string, cx: Context) => void;\n  close: (cx: Context) => void;\n  /** Names origin's forge, for a host gitdeck doesn't know. */\n  setForge: (kind: ForgeChoice, cx: Context) => void;\n}\n\ninterface Row {\n  /** The commit a click jumps to. */\n  hash: string;\n  /** Built when the list lays the row out: a virtual list draws only elements made inside its renderer. */\n  cells: () => Element[];\n}\n\nfunction rowsOf(v: InspectView, p: Palette, now: number): Row[] {\n  const dim = (text: string, w: number) => div().w(w).flex_shrink_0().truncate().text_color(p.dim).child(text);\n  if (v.kind === \"blame\") {\n    return (v.data?.items ?? []).map((l) => ({\n      hash: l.hash,\n      cells: () => [\n        dim(l.first ? `${l.hash.slice(0, 7)} ${l.author}` : \"\", 150),\n        dim(l.first ? ago(now, l.time) : \"\", 60),\n        div().w(36).flex_shrink_0().text_right().text_color(p.dim).child(String(l.line)),\n        div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().child(l.text === \"\" ? \" \" : l.text),\n      ],\n    }));\n  }\n  if (v.kind === \"file-log\") {\n    return (v.data?.items ?? []).map((c) => ({\n      hash: c.hash,\n      cells: () => [dim(c.hash.slice(0, 7), 60), div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().child(c.subject), dim(c.author, 120), dim(ago(now, c.time), 60)],\n    }));\n  }\n  if (v.kind === \"stats\") return statsRows(v.data, p, now);\n  if (v.kind === \"prs\") {\n    const color = (s: string) => (s === \"OPEN\" ? p.added : s === \"MERGED\" ? p.info : p.dim);\n    return (v.data?.items ?? []).map((pr) => ({\n      hash: pr.head,\n      cells: () => [\n        dim(`#${pr.number}`, 50),\n        div().w(60).flex_shrink_0().text_color(color(pr.state)).child(pr.draft ? \"DRAFT\" : pr.state),\n        div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().child(pr.title),\n        dim(pr.branch, 140),\n        dim(pr.author, 90),\n        dim(ago(now, pr.updated), 60),\n      ],\n    }));\n  }\n  // A commit's files show in the commit pane (treePane), not here.\n  if (v.kind === \"tree\") return [];\n  return (v.data?.items ?? []).map((e) => ({\n    hash: e.hash,\n    cells: () => [dim(e.name, 80), dim(e.hash.slice(0, 7), 60), div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().child(e.action), dim(ago(now, e.time), 60)],\n  }));\n}\n\nfunction bar(count: number, most: number, p: Palette): Element {\n  const width = most === 0 ? 0 : Math.max(2, Math.round((count / most) * 160));\n  return div().w(160).flex_shrink_0().child(div().h(8).w(width).rounded(2).bg(p.accent));\n}\n\n/** Totals, then authors and months, each with a bar against the largest. */\nfunction statsRows(s: Stats | null, p: Palette, now: number): Row[] {\n  if (!s) return [];\n  const text = (t: string, color = p.foreground) => ({ hash: \"\", cells: () => [div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().text_color(color).child(t)] });\n  const span = s.first !== null && s.last !== null ? `, first ${ago(now, s.first)}, last ${ago(now, s.last)}` : \"\";\n  const mostAuthor = s.authors[0]?.count ?? 0;\n  const mostMonth = Math.max(0, ...s.months.map((m) => m.count));\n  const months = s.months.slice(-24);\n  return [\n    text(`${s.commits}${s.commits >= MAX_STATS ? \"+\" : \"\"} commits (no merges) by ${s.authors.length} authors, ${s.files} files${span}`),\n    text(`Authors`, p.muted),\n    ...s.authors.slice(0, 50).map((a) => ({\n      hash: \"\",\n      cells: () => [div().w(200).flex_shrink_0().truncate().child(`${a.name} <${a.email}>`), bar(a.count, mostAuthor, p), div().text_color(p.dim).child(String(a.count))],\n    })),\n    text(months.length < s.months.length ? \"Commits per month (last 24)\" : \"Commits per month\", p.muted),\n    ...months.map((m) => ({ hash: \"\", cells: () => [div().w(200).flex_shrink_0().child(m.month), bar(m.count, mostMonth, p), div().text_color(p.dim).child(String(m.count))] })),\n  ];\n}\n\nfunction title(v: InspectView): string {\n  if (v.kind === \"blame\") return `Blame: ${v.path} at ${v.rev.slice(0, 10)}`;\n  if (v.kind === \"file-log\") return `History: ${v.path}`;\n  if (v.kind === \"stats\") return \"Repository statistics\";\n  if (v.kind === \"prs\") {\n    // Until a forge is read there's no telling which word (or CLI) it is.\n    if (v.data == null || v.data.repo === null) return \"Pull / merge requests (read-only)\";\n    const mr = v.data?.label === \"MR\";\n    return `${mr ? \"Merge requests\" : \"Pull requests\"}${v.data?.repo ? ` of ${v.data.repo}` : \"\"} (via ${mr ? \"glab\" : \"gh\"}, read-only): a click jumps to the head commit`;\n  }\n  return \"Reflog: where HEAD has been\";\n}\n\nexport function inspectPane(v: InspectView, p: Palette, a: InspectActions): Element {\n  const rows = rowsOf(v, p, Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000));\n  const error = v.data?.error ?? null;\n  const unnamed = v.kind === \"prs\" && v.data?.host != null;\n  const body =\n    v.data === null\n      ? div().p(12).text_color(p.dim).child(\"Reading…\")\n      : unnamed\n        ? h_flex()\n            .p(12)\n            .gap(8)\n            .items_center()\n            .child(div().flex_1().min_w_0().text_color(p.dim).child(error ?? \"\"))\n            .child(textButton(\"prs-forge-gitlab\", \"GitLab\", p, (cx) => a.setForge(\"gitlab\", cx)))\n            .child(textButton(\"prs-forge-github\", \"GitHub\", p, (cx) => a.setForge(\"github\", cx)))\n            .child(textButton(\"prs-forge-none\", \"Neither\", p, (cx) => a.setForge(\"none\", cx)))\n      : error !== null\n        ? div().p(12).text_color(p.removed).child(error)\n        : rows.length === 0\n          ? div().p(12).text_color(p.dim).child(\"Nothing to show\")\n          : div()\n            .relative()\n            .flex_1()\n            .min_h_0()\n            .when(v.kind === \"blame\", (el) => el.font_family(monoFont()))\n            .text_xs()\n            .child(\n              v_virtual_list(LIST, rows.length, ROW, (i) => String(i), (range) =>\n                rows.slice(range.start, range.end).map((r) =>\n                  h_flex().h(ROW).px(8).gap(8).items_center().whitespace_nowrap().cursor_pointer().hover((el) => el.bg(p.hover)).children(r.cells()),\n                ),\n              )\n                .on_item_click((key, cx) => {\n                  if (v.kind === \"stats\") return;\n                  const row = rows[Number(key)];\n                  if (row) a.jump(row.hash, cx);\n                })\n                .size_full(),\n            )\n            .child(Scrollbar.vertical(LIST).absolute().inset_0());\n  return v_flex()\n    .flex_1()\n    .min_h_0()\n    .border_t_1()\n    .border_color(p.border)\n    .bg(p.surface)\n    .child(\n      h_flex()\n        .h(28)\n        .px(8)\n        .gap(6)\n        .items_center()\n        .flex_shrink_0()\n        .border_b_1()\n        .border_color(p.border)\n        .child(div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().text_xs().text_color(p.muted).child(title(v)))\n        .child(textButton(\"inspect-close\", \"×\", p, a.close)),\n    )\n    .child(body);\n}\n","numLines":169,"startLine":1,"totalLines":169}},"displayPath":"src/ui/inspect.ts","savedCopyFraming":{"enveloped":false}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"11e6173e-67a1-4b46-b065-23da2b3ad0e3","timestamp":"2026-11-19T03:43:02.825Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/inspect.ts\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t// The inspect pane: a file's blame or history, or the reflog. A click on a\n2\t// row jumps to its commit in the graph.\n3\t\n4\timport { div, type Context, type Element } from \"gpui-kit\";\n5\timport { h_flex, v_flex, v_virtual_list, Scrollbar } from \"gpui-base\";\n6\timport type { ForgeChoice } from \"../core/forge/index.ts\";\n7\timport type { InspectView } from \"../core/inspect.ts\";\n8\timport { MAX_STATS, type Stats } from \"../core/stats.ts\";\n9\timport { ago } from \"../core/time.ts\";\n10\timport { monoFont, textButton, type Palette } from \"./style.ts\";\n11\t\n12\tconst LIST = \"gitdeck-inspect\";\n13\tconst ROW = 18;\n14\t\n15\texport interface InspectActions {\n16\t  jump: (hash: string, cx: Context) => void;\n17\t  close: (cx: Context) => void;\n18\t  /** Names origin's forge, for a host gitdeck doesn't know. */\n19\t  setForge: (kind: ForgeChoice, cx: Context) => void;\n20\t}\n21\t\n22\tinterface Row {\n23\t  /** The commit a click jumps to. */\n24\t  hash: string;\n25\t  /** Built when the list lays the row out: a virtual list draws only elements made inside its renderer. */\n26\t  cells: () => Element[];\n27\t}\n28\t\n29\tfunction rowsOf(v: InspectView, p: Palette, now: number): Row[] {\n30\t  const dim = (text: string, w: number) => div().w(w).flex_shrink_0().truncate().text_color(p.dim).child(text);\n31\t  if (v.kind === \"blame\") {\n32\t    return (v.data?.items ?? []).map((l) => ({\n33\t      hash: l.hash,\n34\t      cells: () => [\n35\t        dim(l.first ? `${l.hash.slice(0, 7)} ${l.author}` : \"\", 150),\n36\t        dim(l.first ? ago(now, l.time) : \"\", 60),\n37\t        div().w(36).flex_shrink_0().text_right().text_color(p.dim).child(String(l.line)),\n38\t        div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().child(l.text === \"\" ? \" \" : l.text),\n39\t      ],\n40\t    }));\n41\t  }\n42\t  if (v.kind === \"file-log\") {\n43\t    return (v.data?.items ?? []).map((c) => ({\n44\t      hash: c.hash,\n45\t      cells: () => [dim(c.hash.slice(0, 7), 60), div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().child(c.subject), dim(c.author, 120), dim(ago(now, c.time), 60)],\n46\t    }));\n47\t  }\n48\t  if (v.kind === \"stats\") return statsRows(v.data, p, now);\n49\t  if (v.kind === \"prs\") {\n50\t    const color = (s: string) => (s === \"OPEN\" ? p.added : s === \"MERGED\" ? p.info : p.dim);\n51\t    return (v.data?.items ?? []).map((pr) => ({\n52\t      hash: pr.head,\n53\t      cells: () => [\n54\t        dim(`#${pr.number}`, 50),\n55\t        div().w(60).flex_shrink_0().text_color(color(pr.state)).child(pr.draft ? \"DRAFT\" : pr.state),\n56\t        div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().child(pr.title),\n57\t        dim(pr.branch, 140),\n58\t        dim(pr.author, 90),\n59\t        dim(ago(now, pr.updated), 60),\n60\t      ],\n61\t    }));\n62\t  }\n63\t  // A commit's files show in the commit pane (treePane), not here.\n64\t  if (v.kind === \"tree\") return [];\n65\t  return (v.data?.items ?? []).map((e) => ({\n66\t    hash: e.hash,\n67\t    cells: () => [dim(e.name, 80), dim(e.hash.slice(0, 7), 60), div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().child(e.action), dim(ago(now, e.time), 60)],\n68\t  }));\n69\t}\n70\t\n71\tfunction bar(count: number, most: number, p: Palette): Element {\n72\t  const width = most === 0 ? 0 : Math.max(2, Math.round((count / most) * 160));\n73\t  return div().w(160).flex_shrink_0().child(div().h(8).w(width).rounded(2).bg(p.accent));\n74\t}\n75\t\n76\t/** Totals, then authors and months, each with a bar against the largest. */\n77\tfunction statsRows(s: Stats | null, p: Palette, now: number): Row[] {\n78\t  if (!s) return [];\n79\t  const text = (t: string, color = p.foreground) => ({ hash: \"\", cells: () => [div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().text_color(color).child(t)] });\n80\t  const span = s.first !== null && s.last !== null ? `, first ${ago(now, s.first)}, last ${ago(now, s.last)}` : \"\";\n81\t  const mostAuthor = s.authors[0]?.count ?? 0;\n82\t  const mostMonth = Math.max(0, ...s.months.map((m) => m.count));\n83\t  const months = s.months.slice(-24);\n84\t  return [\n85\t    text(`${s.commits}${s.commits >= MAX_STATS ? \"+\" : \"\"} commits (no merges) by ${s.authors.length} authors, ${s.files} files${span}`),\n86\t    text(`Authors`, p.muted),\n87\t    ...s.authors.slice(0, 50).map((a) => ({\n88\t      hash: \"\",\n89\t      cells: () => [div().w(200).flex_shrink_0().truncate().child(`${a.name} <${a.email}>`), bar(a.count, mostAuthor, p), div().text_color(p.dim).child(String(a.count))],\n90\t    })),\n91\t    text(months.length < s.months.length ? \"Commits per month (last 24)\" : \"Commits per month\", p.muted),\n92\t    ...months.map((m) => ({ hash: \"\", cells: () => [div().w(200).flex_shrink_0().child(m.month), bar(m.count, mostMonth, p), div().text_color(p.dim).child(String(m.count))] })),\n93\t  ];\n94\t}\n95\t\n96\tfunction title(v: InspectView): string {\n97\t  if (v.kind === \"blame\") return `Blame: ${v.path} at ${v.rev.slice(0, 10)}`;\n98\t  if (v.kind === \"file-log\") return `History: ${v.path}`;\n99\t  if (v.kind === \"stats\") return \"Repository statistics\";\n100\t  if (v.kind === \"prs\") {\n101\t    // Until a forge is read there's no telling which word (or CLI) it is.\n102\t    if (v.data == null || v.data.repo === null) return \"Pull / merge requests (read-only)\";\n103\t    const mr = v.data?.label === \"MR\";\n104\t    return `${mr ? \"Merge requests\" : \"Pull requests\"}${v.data?.repo ? ` of ${v.data.repo}` : \"\"} (via ${mr ? \"glab\" : \"gh\"}, read-only): a click jumps to the head commit`;\n105\t  }\n106\t  return \"Reflog: where HEAD has been\";\n107\t}\n108\t\n109\texport function inspectPane(v: InspectView, p: Palette, a: InspectActions): Element {\n110\t  const rows = rowsOf(v, p, Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000));\n111\t  const error = v.data?.error ?? null;\n112\t  const unnamed = v.kind === \"prs\" && v.data?.host != null;\n113\t  const body =\n114\t    v.data === null\n115\t      ? div().p(12).text_color(p.dim).child(\"Reading…\")\n116\t      : unnamed\n117\t        ? h_flex()\n118\t            .p(12)\n119\t            .gap(8)\n120\t            .items_center()\n121\t            .child(div().flex_1().min_w_0().text_color(p.dim).child(error ?? \"\"))\n122\t            .child(textButton(\"prs-forge-gitlab\", \"GitLab\", p, (cx) => a.setForge(\"gitlab\", cx)))\n123\t            .child(textButton(\"prs-forge-github\", \"GitHub\", p, (cx) => a.setForge(\"github\", cx)))\n124\t            .child(textButton(\"prs-forge-none\", \"Neither\", p, (cx) => a.setForge(\"none\", cx)))\n125\t      : error !== null\n126\t        ? div().p(12).text_color(p.removed).child(error)\n127\t        : rows.length === 0\n128\t          ? div().p(12).text_color(p.dim).child(\"Nothing to show\")\n129\t          : div()\n130\t            .relative()\n131\t            .flex_1()\n132\t            .min_h_0()\n133\t            .when(v.kind === \"blame\", (el) => el.font_family(monoFont()))\n134\t            .text_xs()\n135\t            .child(\n136\t              v_virtual_list(LIST, rows.length, ROW, (i) => String(i), (range) =>\n137\t                rows.slice(range.start, range.end).map((r) =>\n138\t                  h_flex().h(ROW).px(8).gap(8).items_center().whitespace_nowrap().cursor_pointer().hover((el) => el.bg(p.hover)).children(r.cells()),\n139\t                ),\n140\t              )\n141\t                .on_item_click((key, cx) => {\n142\t                  if (v.kind === \"stats\") return;\n143\t                  const row = rows[Number(key)];\n144\t                  if (row) a.jump(row.hash, cx);\n145\t                })\n146\t                .size_full(),\n147\t            )\n148\t            .child(Scrollbar.vertical(LIST).absolute().inset_0());\n149\t  return v_flex()\n150\t    .flex_1()\n151\t    .min_h_0()\n152\t    .border_t_1()\n153\t    .border_color(p.border)\n154\t    .bg(p.surface)\n155\t    .child(\n156\t      h_flex()\n157\t        .h(28)\n158\t        .px(8)\n159\t        .gap(6)\n160\t        .items_center()\n161\t        .flex_shrink_0()\n162\t        .border_b_1()\n163\t        .border_color(p.border)\n164\t        .child(div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().text_xs().text_color(p.muted).child(title(v)))\n165\t        .child(textButton(\"inspect-close\", \"×\", p, a.close)),\n166\t    )\n167\t    .child(body);\n168\t}\n169\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","session_id":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
{"parentUuid":"11e6173e-67a1-4b46-b065-23da2b3ad0e3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/treePane.ts","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/treePane.ts","content":"// A commit's files as a folder tree, in the commit pane under the History list\n// (Fork's File Tree tab). Rows are drawn as the Changes tab draws its files:\n// the kind's icon, the name, and here the size at the end. A click on a file\n// shows its content at the commit in the same pane.\n\nimport { div, type Context, type Element } from \"gpui-kit\";\nimport { h_flex, v_flex, v_virtual_list, Scrollbar } from \"gpui-base\";\nimport { fileKind } from \"../core/fileKind.ts\";\nimport type { InspectView } from \"../core/inspect.ts\";\nimport { sizeText, treeRows, type TreeRow } from \"../core/treeRows.ts\";\nimport { tabBar } from \"./details.ts\";\nimport { FILE_ICONS, ICONS, icon, monoFont, textButton, type Palette } from \"./style.ts\";\n\nconst LIST = \"gitdeck-tree\";\nconst ROW = 24;\nconst LINE = 18;\n\nexport interface TreeActions {\n  /** Back to the commit's own tab. */\n  commit: (cx: Context) => void;\n  /** Closes the commit pane. */\n  close: (cx: Context) => void;\n  toggleFolder: (folder: string, cx: Context) => void;\n  /** Opens a file (its place in the tree's list), or with null goes back to the tree. */\n  file: (index: number | null, cx: Context) => void;\n}\n\ntype TreeView = Extract<InspectView, { kind: \"tree\" }>;\n\n/** How far a row under depth folder rows is indented: the Changes tab's step. */\nconst indent = (depth: number): number => 10 + depth * 14;\n\nconst rowKey = (r: TreeRow): string => (r.kind === \"folder\" ? `d:${r.folder}` : `f:${r.index}`);\n\nfunction treeRow(r: TreeRow, p: Palette): Element {\n  const base = h_flex().h(ROW).pl(indent(r.depth)).pr(10).gap(6).items_center().whitespace_nowrap().cursor_pointer().hover((el) => el.bg(p.hover));\n  if (r.kind === \"folder\") {\n    return base\n      .child(icon(r.open ? ICONS.folderOpen : ICONS.folder, p.dim, 16))\n      .child(div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().text_color(p.muted).child(r.label))\n      .child(div().flex_shrink_0().text_xs().text_color(p.dim).child(String(r.count)));\n  }\n  const f = r.file;\n  return base\n    .child(icon(FILE_ICONS[fileKind(f.path)], p.muted, 16))\n    .child(div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().child(r.name))\n    .child(div().flex_shrink_0().text_xs().text_color(p.dim).child(f.kind === \"file\" ? sizeText(f.size) : f.kind));\n}\n\nfunction note(text: string, color: Palette[\"dim\"]): Element {\n  return div().p(12).text_xs().text_color(color).child(text);\n}\n\nfunction folders(v: TreeView, p: Palette, a: TreeActions): Element {\n  if (v.data === null) return note(\"Reading files…\", p.dim);\n  if (v.data.error !== null) return note(v.data.error, p.removed);\n  const rows = treeRows(v.data.items, v.open);\n  return div()\n    .relative()\n    .flex_1()\n    .min_h_0()\n    .child(\n      v_virtual_list(LIST, rows.length, ROW, (i) => (rows[i] ? rowKey(rows[i]) : String(i)), (range) => rows.slice(range.start, range.end).map((r) => treeRow(r, p)))\n        .on_item_click((key, cx) => (key.startsWith(\"d:\") ? a.toggleFolder(key.slice(2), cx) : a.file(Number(key.slice(2)), cx)))\n        .size_full(),\n    )\n    .child(Scrollbar.vertical(LIST).absolute().inset_0());\n}\n\nfunction content(v: TreeView, p: Palette): Element {\n  const blob = v.blob;\n  if (!blob) return note(\"Reading file…\", p.dim);\n  if (blob.note) return note(blob.note, p.dim);\n  const lines = blob.lines;\n  return div()\n    .relative()\n    .flex_1()\n    .min_h_0()\n    .font_family(monoFont())\n    .text_xs()\n    .child(\n      v_virtual_list(`${LIST}-file`, lines.length, LINE, (i) => String(i), (range) =>\n        lines.slice(range.start, range.end).map((text, i) =>\n          h_flex()\n            .h(LINE)\n            .px(8)\n            .gap(8)\n            .items_center()\n            .whitespace_nowrap()\n            .child(div().w(36).flex_shrink_0().text_right().text_color(p.dim).child(String(range.start + i + 1)))\n            .child(div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().child(text === \"\" ? \" \" : text)),\n        ),\n      ).size_full(),\n    )\n    .child(Scrollbar.vertical(`${LIST}-file`).absolute().inset_0());\n}\n\n/** The commit pane's File Tree tab: the tree, or one file of it. */\nexport function treePane(v: TreeView, p: Palette, a: TreeActions): Element {\n  const file = v.file;\n  const crumb = file\n    ? [textButton(\"tree-back\", \"← Files\", p, (cx) => a.file(null, cx)), div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().text_xs().text_color(p.dim).child(file.path)]\n    : [div().flex_1()];\n  return v_flex()\n    .flex_1()\n    .min_h_0()\n    .border_t_1()\n    .border_color(p.border)\n    .bg(p.surface)\n    .child(\n      tabBar(\n        p,\n        textButton(\"details-commit\", \"Commit\", p, a.commit),\n        textButton(\"details-tree\", \"File Tree\", p, () => {}, true),\n        ...crumb,\n        textButton(\"details-close\", \"Close\", p, a.close),\n      ),\n    )\n    .child(file ? content(v, p) : folders(v, p, a));\n}\n","numLines":121,"startLine":1,"totalLines":121}},"displayPath":"src/ui/treePane.ts","savedCopyFraming":{"enveloped":false}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7b9d98cd-c698-4e1f-930a-38219d81e712","timestamp":"2026-11-19T03:43:02.825Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/treePane.ts\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t// A commit's files as a folder tree, in the commit pane under the History list\n2\t// (Fork's File Tree tab). Rows are drawn as the Changes tab draws its files:\n3\t// the kind's icon, the name, and here the size at the end. A click on a file\n4\t// shows its content at the commit in the same pane.\n5\t\n6\timport { div, type Context, type Element } from \"gpui-kit\";\n7\timport { h_flex, v_flex, v_virtual_list, Scrollbar } from \"gpui-base\";\n8\timport { fileKind } from \"../core/fileKind.ts\";\n9\timport type { InspectView } from \"../core/inspect.ts\";\n10\timport { sizeText, treeRows, type TreeRow } from \"../core/treeRows.ts\";\n11\timport { tabBar } from \"./details.ts\";\n12\timport { FILE_ICONS, ICONS, icon, monoFont, textButton, type Palette } from \"./style.ts\";\n13\t\n14\tconst LIST = \"gitdeck-tree\";\n15\tconst ROW = 24;\n16\tconst LINE = 18;\n17\t\n18\texport interface TreeActions {\n19\t  /** Back to the commit's own tab. */\n20\t  commit: (cx: Context) => void;\n21\t  /** Closes the commit pane. */\n22\t  close: (cx: Context) => void;\n23\t  toggleFolder: (folder: string, cx: Context) => void;\n24\t  /** Opens a file (its place in the tree's list), or with null goes back to the tree. */\n25\t  file: (index: number | null, cx: Context) => void;\n26\t}\n27\t\n28\ttype TreeView = Extract<InspectView, { kind: \"tree\" }>;\n29\t\n30\t/** How far a row under depth folder rows is indented: the Changes tab's step. */\n31\tconst indent = (depth: number): number => 10 + depth * 14;\n32\t\n33\tconst rowKey = (r: TreeRow): string => (r.kind === \"folder\" ? `d:${r.folder}` : `f:${r.index}`);\n34\t\n35\tfunction treeRow(r: TreeRow, p: Palette): Element {\n36\t  const base = h_flex().h(ROW).pl(indent(r.depth)).pr(10).gap(6).items_center().whitespace_nowrap().cursor_pointer().hover((el) => el.bg(p.hover));\n37\t  if (r.kind === \"folder\") {\n38\t    return base\n39\t      .child(icon(r.open ? ICONS.folderOpen : ICONS.folder, p.dim, 16))\n40\t      .child(div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().text_color(p.muted).child(r.label))\n41\t      .child(div().flex_shrink_0().text_xs().text_color(p.dim).child(String(r.count)));\n42\t  }\n43\t  const f = r.file;\n44\t  return base\n45\t    .child(icon(FILE_ICONS[fileKind(f.path)], p.muted, 16))\n46\t    .child(div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().child(r.name))\n47\t    .child(div().flex_shrink_0().text_xs().text_color(p.dim).child(f.kind === \"file\" ? sizeText(f.size) : f.kind));\n48\t}\n49\t\n50\tfunction note(text: string, color: Palette[\"dim\"]): Element {\n51\t  return div().p(12).text_xs().text_color(color).child(text);\n52\t}\n53\t\n54\tfunction folders(v: TreeView, p: Palette, a: TreeActions): Element {\n55\t  if (v.data === null) return note(\"Reading files…\", p.dim);\n56\t  if (v.data.error !== null) return note(v.data.error, p.removed);\n57\t  const rows = treeRows(v.data.items, v.open);\n58\t  return div()\n59\t    .relative()\n60\t    .flex_1()\n61\t    .min_h_0()\n62\t    .child(\n63\t      v_virtual_list(LIST, rows.length, ROW, (i) => (rows[i] ? rowKey(rows[i]) : String(i)), (range) => rows.slice(range.start, range.end).map((r) => treeRow(r, p)))\n64\t        .on_item_click((key, cx) => (key.startsWith(\"d:\") ? a.toggleFolder(key.slice(2), cx) : a.file(Number(key.slice(2)), cx)))\n65\t        .size_full(),\n66\t    )\n67\t    .child(Scrollbar.vertical(LIST).absolute().inset_0());\n68\t}\n69\t\n70\tfunction content(v: TreeView, p: Palette): Element {\n71\t  const blob = v.blob;\n72\t  if (!blob) return note(\"Reading file…\", p.dim);\n73\t  if (blob.note) return note(blob.note, p.dim);\n74\t  const lines = blob.lines;\n75\t  return div()\n76\t    .relative()\n77\t    .flex_1()\n78\t    .min_h_0()\n79\t    .font_family(monoFont())\n80\t    .text_xs()\n81\t    .child(\n82\t      v_virtual_list(`${LIST}-file`, lines.length, LINE, (i) => String(i), (range) =>\n83\t        lines.slice(range.start, range.end).map((text, i) =>\n84\t          h_flex()\n85\t            .h(LINE)\n86\t            .px(8)\n87\t            .gap(8)\n88\t            .items_center()\n89\t            .whitespace_nowrap()\n90\t            .child(div().w(36).flex_shrink_0().text_right().text_color(p.dim).child(String(range.start + i + 1)))\n91\t            .child(div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().child(text === \"\" ? \" \" : text)),\n92\t        ),\n93\t      ).size_full(),\n94\t    )\n95\t    .child(Scrollbar.vertical(`${LIST}-file`).absolute().inset_0());\n96\t}\n97\t\n98\t/** The commit pane's File Tree tab: the tree, or one file of it. */\n99\texport function treePane(v: TreeView, p: Palette, a: TreeActions): Element {\n100\t  const file = v.file;\n101\t  const crumb = file\n102\t    ? [textButton(\"tree-back\", \"← Files\", p, (cx) => a.file(null, cx)), div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().text_xs().text_color(p.dim).child(file.path)]\n103\t    : [div().flex_1()];\n104\t  return v_flex()\n105\t    .flex_1()\n106\t    .min_h_0()\n107\t    .border_t_1()\n108\t    .border_color(p.border)\n109\t    .bg(p.surface)\n110\t    .child(\n111\t      tabBar(\n112\t        p,\n113\t        textButton(\"details-commit\", \"Commit\", p, a.commit),\n114\t        textButton(\"details-tree\", \"File Tree\", p, () => {}, true),\n115\t        ...crumb,\n116\t        textButton(\"details-close\", \"Close\", p, a.close),\n117\t      ),\n118\t    )\n119\t    .child(file ? content(v, p) : folders(v, p, a));\n120\t}\n121\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","session_id":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
{"parentUuid":"7b9d98cd-c698-4e1f-930a-38219d81e712","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/core/treeRows.ts","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/core/treeRows.ts","content":"// The files at a commit as a folder tree, the way the Changes tab draws its\n// files: folders first, each folded until opened, then the folder's own files.\n// A folder holding only one folder shares its row (\"docs/deep/\").\n\nimport { folderTree, type FolderNode } from \"./fileGroups.ts\";\nimport { nameAndFolder } from \"./paths.ts\";\nimport type { TreeFile } from \"./tree.ts\";\n\nexport type TreeRow =\n  | { kind: \"folder\"; folder: string; label: string; depth: number; open: boolean; count: number }\n  | { kind: \"file\"; file: TreeFile; name: string; index: number; depth: number };\n\n/** The rows to draw: the open folders' contents, each row with how far in it sits; `index` is the file's place in `files`. */\nexport function treeRows(files: readonly TreeFile[], open: ReadonlySet<string>): TreeRow[] {\n  const index = new Map(files.map((f, i) => [f.path, i]));\n  const walk = (node: FolderNode<TreeFile>, depth: number): TreeRow[] => [\n    ...node.folders.flatMap((g): TreeRow[] => {\n      const shown = open.has(g.folder);\n      const head: TreeRow = { kind: \"folder\", folder: g.folder, label: g.label, depth, open: shown, count: g.all.length };\n      return shown ? [head, ...walk(g, depth + 1)] : [head];\n    }),\n    ...node.files.map((file): TreeRow => ({ kind: \"file\", file, name: nameAndFolder(file.path).name, index: index.get(file.path) ?? -1, depth })),\n  ];\n  return walk(folderTree(files), 0);\n}\n\n/** The open folders with `folder` turned the other way. */\nexport function toggleFolder(open: ReadonlySet<string>, folder: string): ReadonlySet<string> {\n  return open.has(folder) ? new Set([...open].filter((f) => f !== folder)) : new Set([...open, folder]);\n}\n\n/** A file's size as a file browser writes it: bytes, then KB and MB with one decimal under 10. */\nexport function sizeText(bytes: number): string {\n  const units = [\"B\", \"KB\", \"MB\", \"GB\"];\n  let value = bytes;\n  let unit = 0;\n  while (value >= 1024 && unit < units.length - 1) {\n    value /= 1024;\n    unit += 1;\n  }\n  if (unit === 0) return `${bytes} B`;\n  const shown = value < 10 ? value.toFixed(1).replace(/\\.0$/, \"\") : String(Math.round(value));\n  return `${shown} ${units[unit]}`;\n}\n","numLines":45,"startLine":1,"totalLines":45}},"displayPath":"src/core/treeRows.ts","savedCopyFraming":{"enveloped":false}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4c8cdbc6-409c-4b2c-b97a-9e7ee9f7b4ec","timestamp":"2026-11-19T03:43:02.826Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/core/treeRows.ts\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t// The files at a commit as a folder tree, the way the Changes tab draws its\n2\t// files: folders first, each folded until opened, then the folder's own files.\n3\t// A folder holding only one folder shares its row (\"docs/deep/\").\n4\t\n5\timport { folderTree, type FolderNode } from \"./fileGroups.ts\";\n6\timport { nameAndFolder } from \"./paths.ts\";\n7\timport type { TreeFile } from \"./tree.ts\";\n8\t\n9\texport type TreeRow =\n10\t  | { kind: \"folder\"; folder: string; label: string; depth: number; open: boolean; count: number }\n11\t  | { kind: \"file\"; file: TreeFile; name: string; index: number; depth: number };\n12\t\n13\t/** The rows to draw: the open folders' contents, each row with how far in it sits; `index` is the file's place in `files`. */\n14\texport function treeRows(files: readonly TreeFile[], open: ReadonlySet<string>): TreeRow[] {\n15\t  const index = new Map(files.map((f, i) => [f.path, i]));\n16\t  const walk = (node: FolderNode<TreeFile>, depth: number): TreeRow[] => [\n17\t    ...node.folders.flatMap((g): TreeRow[] => {\n18\t      const shown = open.has(g.folder);\n19\t      const head: TreeRow = { kind: \"folder\", folder: g.folder, label: g.label, depth, open: shown, count: g.all.length };\n20\t      return shown ? [head, ...walk(g, depth + 1)] : [head];\n21\t    }),\n22\t    ...node.files.map((file): TreeRow => ({ kind: \"file\", file, name: nameAndFolder(file.path).name, index: index.get(file.path) ?? -1, depth })),\n23\t  ];\n24\t  return walk(folderTree(files), 0);\n25\t}\n26\t\n27\t/** The open folders with `folder` turned the other way. */\n28\texport function toggleFolder(open: ReadonlySet<string>, folder: string): ReadonlySet<string> {\n29\t  return open.has(folder) ? new Set([...open].filter((f) => f !== folder)) : new Set([...open, folder]);\n30\t}\n31\t\n32\t/** A file's size as a file browser writes it: bytes, then KB and MB with one decimal under 10. */\n33\texport function sizeText(bytes: number): string {\n34\t  const units = [\"B\", \"KB\", \"MB\", \"GB\"];\n35\t  let value = bytes;\n36\t  let unit = 0;\n37\t  while (value >= 1024 && unit < units.length - 1) {\n38\t    value /= 1024;\n39\t    unit += 1;\n40\t  }\n41\t  if (unit === 0) return `${bytes} B`;\n42\t  const shown = value < 10 ? value.toFixed(1).replace(/\\.0$/, \"\") : String(Math.round(value));\n43\t  return `${shown} ${units[unit]}`;\n44\t}\n45\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","session_id":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
