{"attachment":{"date":"","type":"date"},"cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","isSidechain":false,"parentUuid":"6fa0cec5-8a62-4b36-bc41-6637a387b29e","rendered":[{"content":""}],"renderedRole":"system","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","session_id":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch","timestamp":"2026-11-19T04:28:45.593Z","type":"attachment","userType":"external","uuid":"05d799df-c785-4ec5-9253-72f5e5b2e754","version":"2.1.325"}
{"parentUuid":"05d799df-c785-4ec5-9253-72f5e5b2e754","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1bb62c29-42e3-4e07-9851-bf57882be4a3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Artifact, AskUserQuestion, Bash, Edit, Glob, Grep, ListAgents, Read, Skill, TaskCreate, TaskStop, TaskUpdate, ToolSearch, Write, mcp__firecrawl__firecrawl_search</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Always reply in Korean, using MoAI-Easy's casual 해요체 (the user once corrected me: \"한글로 말하라고..\").\n   - Commit rules:\n     - Ask with AskUserQuestion before any commit or push.\n     - Stage explicit paths only.\n     - Never commit `.claudeignore` or `.worktreeinclude`.\n     - No \"🗿 MoAI\" trailer.\n   - All the work this session is uncommitted:\n     - Fork-style commit detail view.\n     - Right-click commit menu.\n     - Resizable bottom commit pane in the History tab.\n     - File Tree as a real folder tree.\n   - Earlier request: \"클릭했을때 파일은 다른것들 같이 메인창에서 열려 보이게 해주지. .\" Done: a tree file click opens the file in the main viewer tab.\n   - Latest request: \"파일열어서 보일때, 어느정도 기본 소스 색상은 넣어 주었으면 하는대 그 포맷들 많잖어.. 그리고 MD파일일경우는 변환해서 보기 좋게 보였으면 좋겠어.\"\n     - Source files should get syntax colors.\n     - Markdown files should show rendered.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - The project is a Herdr mod running on QuickJS, built with gpui-kit and gpui-base.\n   - Herdr's built-in code viewer and markdown renderer:\n     - `EditorState.new({language, value, readonly, font_family, font_size, syntax})` plus `Editor.new(state)` gives a read-only code view with highlighting, line numbers and folding.\n     - An EditorState must be created outside render (it is created in async load) and freed with `.release()`.\n     - `TextView.markdown(id, text).selectable().scrollable()` renders markdown.\n     - Language names follow Herdr's Files mod (`~/.config/herdr-app/mods/files/main.js`): `LANG[ext] ?? ext`, where ts/tsx/mjs map to \"js\", toml to \"yaml\", jsonc to \"json\", vue/svelte to \"html\". Syntax colors come from the theme's ansi colors.\n   - The viewer tab is driven by `ViewerRequest` via `openViewer(...)`. I added `view: \"file\"` with `{rev, path}`.\n   - Development rules: pure logic in `src/core`, test first, immutable state.\n   - Verification steps:\n     1. `pnpm verify`.\n     2. `pnpm -s dev`.\n     3. `herdr-app status`.\n     4. Click through with orca: commit row (1595,287); File Tree tab (1500,785); `src/` folder (1460,910); `changes.ts` (1495,982); `CHANGELOG.md` (1500,1006) when `src/` is folded.\n     5. Screenshot with `herdr-app shot`.\n   - Scratchpad: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-WorkSpace-vogle-herdr-gitdeck/c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29/scratchpad\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **src/core/treeRows.ts** (new, 100% covered):\n     - `treeRows(files, open)` builds the folder/file rows.\n     - `toggleFolder(open, folder)` returns a new set.\n     - `sizeText(bytes)` formats sizes as B/KB/MB.\n   - **tests/treeRows.test.ts** (new): 5 tests.\n   - **src/ui/treePane.ts** (new):\n     - `treePane(v, p, {commit, close, toggleFolder, file(index)})`.\n     - Rows look like the Changes tab: 24px tall, indent `10+depth*14`, folder and kind icons, size shown dim.\n     - Keys are `d:<folder>` and `f:<index>`.\n     - The tab bar is Commit, File Tree (active), a spacer, then Close.\n   - **src/core/inspect.ts**: the tree view is now `{ kind: \"tree\"; rev; data: Loaded<TreeFile>|null; open: ReadonlySet<string> }`. `file` and `blob` were removed.\n   - **src/ui/details.ts**: `bar` was renamed to the exported `tabBar(p, ...buttons)`.\n   - **src/ui/historyPane.ts**:\n     - `commitPane()` shows `treePane` when the inspect view is tree; otherwise it shows details.\n     - In the history tab, `tabBody` skips the full inspect pane for a tree.\n     - New actions: `toggleTreeFolder` and `treeFile(index, cx)`.\n   - **src/main.ts**:\n     - `treeFile(index)` calls `openViewer({ view: \"file\", repo, on, rev, path })`.\n     - `toggleTreeFolder` updates the open set.\n     - `pickCommit` reopens the tree for the new commit if the tree was open.\n     - Imports `toggleFolder`.\n   - **src/ui/inspect.ts**: the old flat tree code and `openTreeFile`/`closeTreeFile` were removed. A tree now returns `[]`.\n   - **src/core/panel.ts**:\n     - `ViewerRequest` gains `(Where & { view: \"file\"; rev: string; path: string })`.\n     - `parseViewer` accepts the new view.\n     - `viewerTitle` returns the file's base name.\n   - **src/core/tree.ts**: added `loadFileAt(git, target, rev, path)`. It runs `ls-tree -z --long rev -- path`, then `loadBlob`. A missing path gives the note \"X is not in <rev10>\"; an error gives its message as the note.\n   - **tests/panel.test.ts** and **tests/tree.test.ts**: tests added for the file request and `loadFileAt`.\n   - **src/core/codeView.ts** (new, 100% covered):\n     ```ts\n     const ALIASES = { ts:\"js\", tsx:\"js\", mts:\"js\", cts:\"js\", jsx:\"js\", mjs:\"js\", cjs:\"js\", toml:\"yaml\", jsonc:\"json\", svelte:\"html\", vue:\"html\" };\n     const MARKDOWN = new Set([\"md\",\"markdown\",\"mdx\"]);\n     export function codeLanguage(path): string  // \"txt\" when no extension\n     export function isMarkdown(path): boolean\n     ```\n   - **tests/codeView.test.ts** (new): 2 tests.\n   - **src/ui/fileBody.ts** (rewritten):\n     - `syntax()` takes colors from the theme: keyword ansi5, string ansi2, comment dim, function ansi4, type ansi3, number ansi1, constant/boolean ansi6.\n     - `codeState(path, blob)` returns an `EditorState` (readonly, `monoFont()`, size 12), or null when the blob has a note.\n     - `fileBody(blob, code, rendered, p)` shows one of three things:\n       - the note text;\n       - `TextView.markdown(\"gitdeck-markdown\", text).selectable().scrollable()` with px24/py16 when rendered;\n       - `Editor.new(code).flex_1().min_h_0()`.\n   - **src/viewer.ts**:\n     - `Shown` gains `{ kind: \"file\"; blob; code: EditorState|null; rendered: boolean }`.\n     - `read()` handles the file view with `loadFileAt`, `codeState`, and `rendered: isMarkdown(path)`.\n     - `load()` releases the old view, and also releases the new one if the request is stale. A private `release(shown)` helper does this.\n     - The bar for a file shows `markdownToggle` (Rendered/Source buttons, markdown only), then Blame and History. Those two `go()` to blame/file-log at `r.rev`/`r.path`.\n     - render: `s.kind === \"file\"` draws `fileBody(...)`.\n     - Imports `type EditorState` from gpui-base.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No new errors this stretch; typecheck passed each time.\n   - Earlier: the TS2339 error in `inspect.ts` rowsOf was fixed by adding a tree→`[]` branch, and the `viewer.ts` `openTreeFile` leftover was removed.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - `pnpm verify` exit 0: 436/436 passed, 99.65% coverage, `herdr-app status` `errors: []`.\n   - Screenshot confirmed `changes.ts` opens in the main viewer with syntax colors: keywords purple, strings green, comments dim, with line numbers.\n   - Not yet visually confirmed:\n     - Markdown rendering.\n     - The Rendered/Source toggle.\n     - The Blame/History buttons.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"파일트리는 트리로 나와야하지 않을까 그리고 여기마 파일 보여주는 디자인 포멧이 다른거 같기도 하고..\" (with a screenshot)\n   - \"클릭했을때 파일은 다른것들 같이 메인창에서 열려 보이게 해주지. .\"\n   - \"파일열어서 보일때, 어느정도 기본 소스 색상은 넣어 주었으면 하는대 그 포맷들 많잖어.. 그리고 MD파일일경우는 변환해서 보기 좋게 보였으면 좋겠어.\"\n   - Earlier standing instructions:\n     - Korean replies.\n     - Ask before commit or push.\n     - Never commit `.claudeignore` or `.worktreeinclude`.\n     - No MoAI trailer.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Verify markdown rendering in the app (`CHANGELOG.md`). Optionally check the Source toggle.\n   - Report in Korean, using the MoAI-Easy style.\n   - Nothing is committed. Ask before committing.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   - Just folded `src/` and clicked `CHANGELOG.md` at (1500,1006).\n   - Took the screenshot /private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-WorkSpace-vogle-herdr-gitdeck/c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29/scratchpad/m1s.png (resized to 1300). It has not been viewed yet.\n   - `herdr-app status` showed `errors: []`.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   1. View `m1s.png` to confirm `CHANGELOG.md` shows rendered markdown with Rendered/Source buttons. Optionally click Source to confirm the colored source view.\n   2. Report to the user in Korean. Cover:\n      - Source files get colors through Herdr's own code viewer, the same as the Files tab, plus line numbers and folding.\n      - `.md`/`.markdown`/`.mdx` files open rendered, with a Rendered/Source toggle.\n      - Test results: 436 passed.\n      - What wasn't verified.\n      - That nothing is committed.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/allan/.claude/projects/-Volumes-WorkSpace-vogle-herdr-gitdeck/c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"e63473cb-2c49-44c6-ac2b-ea6132a1e763","timestamp":"2026-11-19T04:06:47.978Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":148,"turnIndex":150},"turnOrigin":"human","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["64fec550-2b2e-4ccc-9acd-17e9fe057cdd"],"session_id":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck","sessionId":"c36cb7dc-d64c-445a-9a8d-ccb9a1219a29","version":"2.1.325","gitBranch":"feat/agent-centered-panel","slug":"nifty-leaping-sketch"}
{"parentUuid":"e63473cb-2c49-44c6-ac2b-ea6132a1e763","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/inspect.ts","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/inspect.ts","content":"// The inspect pane: a file's blame or history, or the reflog. A click on a\n// row jumps to its commit in the graph.\n\nimport { div, type Context, type Element } from \"gpui-kit\";\nimport { h_flex, v_flex, v_virtual_list, Scrollbar } from \"gpui-base\";\nimport type { ForgeChoice } from \"../core/forge/index.ts\";\nimport type { InspectView } from \"../core/inspect.ts\";\nimport { MAX_STATS, type Stats } from \"../core/stats.ts\";\nimport { ago } from \"../core/time.ts\";\nimport { monoFont, textButton, type Palette } from \"./style.ts\";\n\nconst LIST = \"gitdeck-inspect\";\nconst ROW = 18;\n\nexport interface InspectActions {\n  jump: (hash: string, cx: Context) => void;\n  close: (cx: Context) => void;\n  /** Names origin's forge, for a host gitdeck doesn't know. */\n  setForge: (kind: ForgeChoice, cx: Context) => void;\n}\n\ninterface Row {\n  /** The commit a click jumps to. */\n  hash: string;\n  /** Built when the list lays the row out: a virtual list draws only elements made inside its renderer. */\n  cells: () => Element[];\n}\n\nfunction rowsOf(v: InspectView, p: Palette, now: number): Row[] {\n  const dim = (text: string, w: number) => div().w(w).flex_shrink_0().truncate().text_color(p.dim).child(text);\n  if (v.kind === \"blame\") {\n    return (v.data?.items ?? []).map((l) => ({\n      hash: l.hash,\n      cells: () => [\n        dim(l.first ? `${l.hash.slice(0, 7)} ${l.author}` : \"\", 150),\n        dim(l.first ? ago(now, l.time) : \"\", 60),\n        div().w(36).flex_shrink_0().text_right().text_color(p.dim).child(String(l.line)),\n        div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().child(l.text === \"\" ? \" \" : l.text),\n      ],\n    }));\n  }\n  if (v.kind === \"file-log\") {\n    return (v.data?.items ?? []).map((c) => ({\n      hash: c.hash,\n      cells: () => [dim(c.hash.slice(0, 7), 60), div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().child(c.subject), dim(c.author, 120), dim(ago(now, c.time), 60)],\n    }));\n  }\n  if (v.kind === \"stats\") return statsRows(v.data, p, now);\n  if (v.kind === \"prs\") {\n    const color = (s: string) => (s === \"OPEN\" ? p.added : s === \"MERGED\" ? p.info : p.dim);\n    return (v.data?.items ?? []).map((pr) => ({\n      hash: pr.head,\n      cells: () => [\n        dim(`#${pr.number}`, 50),\n        div().w(60).flex_shrink_0().text_color(color(pr.state)).child(pr.draft ? \"DRAFT\" : pr.state),\n        div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().child(pr.title),\n        dim(pr.branch, 140),\n        dim(pr.author, 90),\n        dim(ago(now, pr.updated), 60),\n      ],\n    }));\n  }\n  // A commit's files show in the commit pane (treePane), not here.\n  if (v.kind === \"tree\") return [];\n  return (v.data?.items ?? []).map((e) => ({\n    hash: e.hash,\n    cells: () => [dim(e.name, 80), dim(e.hash.slice(0, 7), 60), div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().child(e.action), dim(ago(now, e.time), 60)],\n  }));\n}\n\nfunction bar(count: number, most: number, p: Palette): Element {\n  const width = most === 0 ? 0 : Math.max(2, Math.round((count / most) * 160));\n  return div().w(160).flex_shrink_0().child(div().h(8).w(width).rounded(2).bg(p.accent));\n}\n\n/** Totals, then authors and months, each with a bar against the largest. */\nfunction statsRows(s: Stats | null, p: Palette, now: number): Row[] {\n  if (!s) return [];\n  const text = (t: string, color = p.foreground) => ({ hash: \"\", cells: () => [div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().text_color(color).child(t)] });\n  const span = s.first !== null && s.last !== null ? `, first ${ago(now, s.first)}, last ${ago(now, s.last)}` : \"\";\n  const mostAuthor = s.authors[0]?.count ?? 0;\n  const mostMonth = Math.max(0, ...s.months.map((m) => m.count));\n  const months = s.months.slice(-24);\n  return [\n    text(`${s.commits}${s.commits >= MAX_STATS ? \"+\" : \"\"} commits (no merges) by ${s.authors.length} authors, ${s.files} files${span}`),\n    text(`Authors`, p.muted),\n    ...s.authors.slice(0, 50).map((a) => ({\n      hash: \"\",\n      cells: () => [div().w(200).flex_shrink_0().truncate().child(`${a.name} <${a.email}>`), bar(a.count, mostAuthor, p), div().text_color(p.dim).child(String(a.count))],\n    })),\n    text(months.length < s.months.length ? \"Commits per month (last 24)\" : \"Commits per month\", p.muted),\n    ...months.map((m) => ({ hash: \"\", cells: () => [div().w(200).flex_shrink_0().child(m.month), bar(m.count, mostMonth, p), div().text_color(p.dim).child(String(m.count))] })),\n  ];\n}\n\nfunction title(v: InspectView): string {\n  if (v.kind === \"blame\") return `Blame: ${v.path} at ${v.rev.slice(0, 10)}`;\n  if (v.kind === \"file-log\") return `History: ${v.path}`;\n  if (v.kind === \"stats\") return \"Repository statistics\";\n  if (v.kind === \"prs\") {\n    // Until a forge is read there's no telling which word (or CLI) it is.\n    if (v.data == null || v.data.repo === null) return \"Pull / merge requests (read-only)\";\n    const mr = v.data?.label === \"MR\";\n    return `${mr ? \"Merge requests\" : \"Pull requests\"}${v.data?.repo ? ` of ${v.data.repo}` : \"\"} (via ${mr ? \"glab\" : \"gh\"}, read-only): a click jumps to the head commit`;\n  }\n  return \"Reflog: where HEAD has been\";\n}\n\nexport function inspectPane(v: InspectView, p: Palette, a: InspectActions): Element {\n  const rows = rowsOf(v, p, Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000));\n  const error = v.data?.error ?? null;\n  const unnamed = v.kind === \"prs\" && v.data?.host != null;\n  const body =\n    v.data === null\n      ? div().p(12).text_color(p.dim).child(\"Reading…\")\n      : unnamed\n        ? h_flex()\n            .p(12)\n            .gap(8)\n            .items_center()\n            .child(div().flex_1().min_w_0().text_color(p.dim).child(error ?? \"\"))\n            .child(textButton(\"prs-forge-gitlab\", \"GitLab\", p, (cx) => a.setForge(\"gitlab\", cx)))\n            .child(textButton(\"prs-forge-github\", \"GitHub\", p, (cx) => a.setForge(\"github\", cx)))\n            .child(textButton(\"prs-forge-none\", \"Neither\", p, (cx) => a.setForge(\"none\", cx)))\n      : error !== null\n        ? div().p(12).text_color(p.removed).child(error)\n        : rows.length === 0\n          ? div().p(12).text_color(p.dim).child(\"Nothing to show\")\n          : div()\n            .relative()\n            .flex_1()\n            .min_h_0()\n            .when(v.kind === \"blame\", (el) => el.font_family(monoFont()))\n            .text_xs()\n            .child(\n              v_virtual_list(LIST, rows.length, ROW, (i) => String(i), (range) =>\n                rows.slice(range.start, range.end).map((r) =>\n                  h_flex().h(ROW).px(8).gap(8).items_center().whitespace_nowrap().cursor_pointer().hover((el) => el.bg(p.hover)).children(r.cells()),\n                ),\n              )\n                .on_item_click((key, cx) => {\n                  if (v.kind === \"stats\") return;\n                  const row = rows[Number(key)];\n                  if (row) a.jump(row.hash, cx);\n                })\n                .size_full(),\n            )\n            .child(Scrollbar.vertical(LIST).absolute().inset_0());\n  return v_flex()\n    .flex_1()\n    .min_h_0()\n    .border_t_1()\n    .border_color(p.border)\n    .bg(p.surface)\n    .child(\n      h_flex()\n        .h(28)\n        .px(8)\n        .gap(6)\n        .items_center()\n        .flex_shrink_0()\n        .border_b_1()\n        .border_color(p.border)\n        .child(div().flex_1().min_w_0().truncate().text_xs().text_color(p.muted).child(title(v)))\n        .child(textButton(\"inspect-close\", \"×\", p, a.close)),\n    )\n    .child(body);\n}\n","numLines":169,"startLine":1,"totalLines":169}},"displayPath":"src/ui/inspect.ts","savedCopyFraming":{"enveloped":false}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"291e3fff-bdab-4475-babc-982d3c262fcc","timestamp":"2026-11-19T04:28:42.251Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Volumes/WorkSpace/vogle/herdr-gitdeck/src/ui/inspect.ts\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t// The inspect pane: a file's blame or history, or the reflog. A click on a\n2\t// row jumps to its commit in the graph.\n3\t\n4\timport { div, type Context, type Element } from \"gpui-kit\";\n5\timport { h_flex, v_flex, v_virtual_list, Scrollbar } from \"gpui-base\";\n6\timport type { ForgeChoice } from \"../core/forge/index.ts\";\n7\timport type { InspectView } from \"../core/inspect.ts\";\n8\timport { MAX_STATS, type Stats } from \"../core/stats.ts\";\n9\timport { ago } from \"../core/time.ts\";\n10\timport { monoFont, textButton, type Palette } from \"./style.ts\";\n11\t\n12\tconst LIST = \"gitdeck-inspect\";\n13\tconst ROW = 18;\n14\t\n15\texport interface InspectActions {\n16\t  jump: (hash: string, cx: Context) => void;\n17\t  close: (cx: Context) => void;\n18\t  /** Names origin's forge, for a host gitdeck doesn't know. */\n19\t  setForge: (kind: ForgeChoice, cx: Context) => void;\n20\t}\n21\t\n22\tinterface Row {\n23\t  /** The commit a click jumps to. */\n24\t  hash: string;\n25\t  /** Built when the list lays the row out: a virtual list draws only elements made inside its renderer. */\n26\t  cells: () => Element[];\n27\t}\n28\t\n29\tfunction rowsOf(v: InspectView, p: Palette, now: number): Row[] {\n30\t  const dim = (text: string, w: number) => div().w(w).flex_shrink_0().truncate().text_color(p.dim).child(text);\n31\t  if (v.kind === \"blame\") {\n32\t    return (v.data?.items ?? []).map((l) => ({\n33\t      hash: l.hash,\n34\t      cells: () => [\n35\t        dim(l.first ? `${l.hash.slice(0, 7)} ${l.author}` : \"\", 150),\n36\t        dim(l.first ? ago(now, l.time) : \"\", 60),\n37\